tions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diyaavirmani/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diyaavirmani/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diyaavirmani/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diyaavirmani/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diyaavirmani/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/diyaavirmani","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/diyaavirmani/backstage/commits/5e99603b8246e8a2edf9a0a0bef55bbf9e64283a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T02:42:52Z","email":"diyavirmani41@gmail.com","name":"Diya virmani"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T02:42:52Z","email":"diyavirmani41@gmail.com","name":"Diya virmani"},"message":"feat: layout-aware capacity from SAIACS hall data and resilient KB matching\n\nAdd SAIACS''s official hall × layout table (verified against the raw page)\nand two genuine conflicts with its institute page (ground 500 vs 400;\ncluster 60 vs 30–80). Capacity now needs a named room in a layout that\nsuits the event, and each result explains which room fits or why none\ndoes, naming only relevant conflicts. The evaluation grows to 26 cases.\n\nAn additive, revision-checked sync tool appended the new claims, sources\nand spaces to the published SAIACS venue.\n\nA Knowledge Base rebuild switched to city and topic entries with\nmisattributed source lists. The app now accepts per-venue, per-city or\ntopic entries for the right city, keeps only verified paths per lead,\naccepts partial source coverage when every citation is the venue''s own,\nand matches shortened headings. All remain fail-closed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6a93c1e09fd93248e29dd1464877bbc69c85b0bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/diyaavirmani/backstage/git/trees/6a93c1e09fd93248e29dd1464877bbc69c85b0bc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/rep