https://api.github.com/users/diyaavirmani/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diyaavirmani/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/diyaavirmani","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/diyaavirmani/backstage/commits/5da5c13d1b6c2e4ea5b03ae75edc6c81230266d7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T20:34:20Z","email":"diyavirmani41@gmail.com","name":"Diya virmani"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T20:34:20Z","email":"diyavirmani41@gmail.com","name":"Diya virmani"},"message":"fix: make the suggested setup readable and require custom audience details\n\nThe proposed spaces were only visible inside a truncated single-line\ninput on phones. The suggested setup panel now lists proposed spaces,\nthe reason, equipment placement and assumptions, keeps it distinct from\ndocumented venue spaces and availability, and uses a labelled textarea\nfor adjustments that still change only the editable form.\n\nChoosing \"Other\" with only a community name no longer passes as a valid\naudience; the custom field is focused with a linked error. Leads with\nno documented fact explain that instead of rendering an empty list.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"07a294bd2225b88002233f11d039ef437d719cd3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/diyaavirmani/backstage/git/trees/07a294bd2225b88002233f11d039ef437d719cd3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/diyaavirmani/backstage/git/commits/5da5c13d1b6c2e4ea5b03ae75edc6c81230266d7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203604786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diyaavirmani/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diyaavirmani/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diyaavirmani/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diyaavirmani/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/diyaavirmani","id":203604786,"login":"diyaavirmani","node_id":"U_kgDODCLDMg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diyaavirmani/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diyaavirmani/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diyaavirmani/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diyaavirmani/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diyaavirmani/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/diyaavirmani","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/diyaavirmani/backstage/commit/5da5c13d1b6c2e4ea5b03ae75edc6c81230266d7","node_id":"C_kwDOU31JKdoAKDVkYTVjMTNkMWI2YzJlNGVhNWIwM2FlNzVlZGM2YzgxMjMwMjY2ZDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/diyaavirmani/backstage/commit/2ca6be8d29966f7bb3148aa36fce9f60803f092b","sha":"2ca6be8d29966f7bb3148aa36fce9f60803f092b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/diyaavirmani/backstage/commits/2ca6be8d29966f7bb3148aa36fce9f60803f092b"}],"sha":"5da5c13d1b6c2e4ea5b03ae75edc6c81230266d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/diyaavirmani/backstage/commits/5da5c13d1b6c2e4ea5b03ae75edc6c81230266d7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203604786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diyaavirmani/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diyaavirmani/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diyaavirmani/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diyaavirmani/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/diyaavirmani","id":203604786,"login":"diyaavirmani","node_id":"U_kgDODCLDMg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diyaavirmani/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diyaavirmani/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diyaavirmani/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diyaavirmani/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diyaavirmani/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/diyaavirmani","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/diyaavirmani/backstage/commits/2ca6be8d29966f7bb3148aa36fce9f60803f092b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T20:29:18Z","email":"diyavirmani41@gmail.com","name":"Diya virmani"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T20:29:18Z","email":"diyavirmani41@gmail.com","name":"Diya virmani"},"message":"feat: lead with sourced evidence and venue-scoped enquiry routes\n\nRecommendation and catalog cards now open with \"Why consider this\nvenue\": official hosting facts first, dated historical events labelled\nas historical, then facilities and audience terms, with qualifications\nand conflicts kept visible. Precise cited pages are linked directly on\neach card with readable role labels.\n\n\"Needs confirmation\" lists the unresolved questions and published\nenquiry routes. Routes are separate Sanity venueContact documents\n(rechecked from official pages on 2026-10-05) with purpose, venue or\norganization scope, source and check date. They are resolved\nserver-side for the exact validated venue identity, never by the\nmodel, and are stored with private research drafts. An editable\nenquiry built from the discovery snapshot can be copied; nothing is\nsent.\n\nDiscovery orders leads by brief-relevant evidence, using a published\ncontact only as a tie-breaker. Additive, idempotent enrichment tooling\ncreated 5 sources and 10 contacts after a dry run; the Knowledge Base\nquery and venue claims are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4291517fdc04c59842ee58c8a3fedf5636c8b988","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/diyaavirmani/backstage/git/trees/4291517fdc04c59842ee58c8a3fedf5636c8b988"},"url":"ht