ttps://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/b49ec1ee8b84093f7b639c3519e18083cf0ad374","node_id":"C_kwDOU4p2ytoAKGI0OWVjMWVlOGI4NDA5M2Y3YjYzOWMzNTE5ZTE4MDgzY2YwYWQzNzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/7fb42194c77e6b00d1a2f5ce91aeb4f1b5b64957","sha":"7fb42194c77e6b00d1a2f5ce91aeb4f1b5b64957","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/7fb42194c77e6b00d1a2f5ce91aeb4f1b5b64957"}],"sha":"b49ec1ee8b84093f7b639c3519e18083cf0ad374","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/b49ec1ee8b84093f7b639c3519e18083cf0ad374"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/7fb42194c77e6b00d1a2f5ce91aeb4f1b5b64957/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T04:46:25Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T04:46:25Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"message":"filters: nowtv.com.tr, field-confirmed with one line and no exceptions\n\nwww.nowtv.com.tr##+js(set-local-storage-item, cookieChoiceMade, true)\n\nThat plus the two redirect rules is the whole of it: the video plays with no\nexception on gtm.js and none on gpt.js. The line was a comment in these notes\npending confirmation; it is confirmed, so it is a filter.\n\nThe gpt.js whitelist that looked necessary for a while is worth recording,\nbecause the explanation was not where either of us was looking. Their player\nis first-party /js/app.js and touches googletag 47 times, and uBO GPT\nresource throws on 65 of the real file 141 callable names. Allowing the real\ngpt.js made those calls land - and so does replacing that resource with the\none here, which answers all 141. The whitelist was never about the container.\n\nAlso recorded, because both errors were mine: counting video elements and\ndata-player-inited measures a player being constructed rather than playing,\nand the control run is what mattered - that page never reaches playback in a\nheadless browser even with everything allowed, so every conclusion drawn from\nit was noise. The report was right twice while my measurements said otherwise.","tree":{"sha":"10444ac4b81d928d1d531c56618843c8ad36f57f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/trees/10444ac4b81d928d1d531c56618843c8ad36f57f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/commits/7fb42194c77e6b00d1a2f5ce91aeb4f1b5b64957","verification":{"payload":"tree 10444ac4b81d928d1d531c56618843c8ad36f57f\nparent ce775a17d90558e99131b0de1fc35f663d25b2fe\nauthor Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791089185 +1300\ncommitter Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791089185 +1300\n\nfilters: nowtv.com.tr, field-confirmed with one line and no exceptions\n\nwww.nowtv.com.tr##+js(set-local-storage-item, cookieChoiceMade, true)\n\nThat plus the two redirect rules is the whole of it: the video plays with no\nexception on gtm.js and none on gpt.js. The line was a comment in these notes\npending confirmation; it is confirmed, so it is a filter.\n\nThe gpt.js whitelist that looked necessary for a while is worth recording,\nbecause the explanation was not where either of us was looking. Their player\nis first-party /js/app.js and touches googletag 47 times, and uBO GPT\nresource throws on 65 of the real file 141 callable names. Allowing the real\ngpt.js made those calls land - and so does replacing that resource with the\none here, which answers all 141. The whitelist was never about the container.\n\nAlso recorded, because both errors were mine: counting video elements and\ndata-player-inited measures a player being constructed rather than playing,\nand the control run is what mattered - that page never reaches playback in a\nheadless browser even with everything allowed, so every conclusion drawn from\nit was noise. The report was right twice while my measurements said otherwise.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPCSVWMUDHjp4kSP8mCo6DMbbZd\nwVKwk1D89AEPXKgVYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQLQFhwaHA9VkQi78oeBSqHJ8tG074px82nz79dC7OM9Yvlfa6KHlAxiqrXiWp+d6jV\noXBKzbZzpQx29U9C30owM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T04:46:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/7fb42194c77e6b00d1a2f5ce91aeb4f1b5b64957","node_id":"C_kwDOU4p2ytoAKDdmYjQyMTk0Yzc3ZTZiMDBkMWEyZjVjZTkxYWViNGYxYjViNjQ5NTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/ce775a17d90558e99131b0de1fc35f663d25b2fe","sha":"ce775a17d90558e99131b0de1fc35f663d25b2fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/ce775a17d90558e99131b0de1fc35f663d25b2fe"}],"sha":"7fb42194c77e6b00d1a2f5ce91aeb4f1b5b64957","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/7fb42194c77e6b00d1a2f5ce91aeb4f1b5b64957"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/ce775a17d90558e99131b0de1fc35f663d25b2fe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T04:37:45Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T04:37:45Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"message":"docs: AGENTS.md, the stale token and two rules that cost something\n\nThree things.\n\nThe scriptlet-token line still named gtm-neutered, which has not been a\nresource here for a long time - a reader following it would have written a\nfilter that injects nothing and says nothing, which is the exact failure the\nline exists to warn about.\n\nReleasing knew that a pinned tag has to exist and not that it has to be\ncurrent. v1.10.0 resolved perfectly while serving gtm-tag 1.3.0 against a\nmain at 1.4.0, so the documented install handed out a resource three commits\nold and a correct filter did nothing. The second CI check is now written down,\nand with it the rule it implies: a resource bump comes with its release. Most\npushes are still not releases - just not anything under src/.\n\nAnd a new section for the GPT resource, because taking over a resource that\nalready works needs its reason recorded. Two rules generalise past it: answer\ninput you do not implement rather than throwing at the caller, since allowing\nand blocking both leave a page coherent and throwing is the only outcome that\ndoes neither; and measure against the real file rather than another\nstand-in, which is how 24 became 65. It also says which part of AdGuard was\nworth taking (the slot events, because a page branching on isEmpty is a wait)\nand which was not (an iframe is a prop for a detector).","tree":{"sha":"acf6094899504eb89e5843d51ac01ebe5e25bb7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/trees/acf6094899504eb89e5843d51ac01ebe5e25bb7c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/commits/ce775a17d90558e99131b0de1fc35f663d25b2fe","verification":{"payload":"tree acf6094899504eb89e5843d51ac01ebe5e25bb7c\nparent c0edbb6659cc9660a9d52409179427b06d46193c\nauthor Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791088665 +1300\ncommitter Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791088665 +1300\n\ndocs: AGENTS.md, the stale token and two rules that cost something\n\nThree things.\n\nThe scriptlet-token line still named gtm-neutered, which has not been a\nresource here for a long time - a reader following it would have written a\nfilter that injects nothing and says nothing, which is the exact failure the\nline exists to warn about.\n\nReleasing knew that a pinned tag has to exist and not that it has to be\ncurrent. v1.10.0 resolved perfectly while serving gtm-tag 1.3.0 against a\nmain at 1.4.0, so the documented install handed out a resource three commits\nold and a correct filter did nothing. The second CI check is now written down,\nand with it the rule it implies: a resource bump comes with its release. Most\npushes are still not releases - just not anything under src/.\n\nAnd a new section for the GPT resource, because taking over a resource that\nalready works needs its reason recorded. Two rules generalise past it: answer\ninput you do not implement rather than throwing at the caller, since allowing\nand blocking both leave a page coherent and throwing is the only outcome that\ndoes neither; and measure against the real file rather than another\nstand-in, which is how 24 became 65. It also says which part of AdGuard was\nworth taking (the slot events, because a page branching on isEmpty is a wait)\nand which was not (an iframe is a prop for a detector).\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPCSVWMUDHjp4kSP8mCo6DMbbZd\nwVKwk1D89AEPXKgVYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQJVWAYK3xBohtCCB/KqgFtyVvL3LVNWk03rNwgW2A+WZQoYKhwUuNKtiUagiRxsnF8\nZIc6kN9S3b0Lm2BWJ1+wk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T04:37:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/ce775a17d90558e99131b0de1fc35f663d25b2fe","node_id":"C_kwDOU4p2ytoAKGNlNzc1YTE3ZDkwNTU4ZTk5MTMxYjBkZTFmYzM1ZjY2M2QyNWIyZmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/c0edbb6659cc9660a9d52409179427b06d46193c","sha":"c0edbb6659cc9660a9d52409179427b06d46193c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/c0edbb6659cc9660a9d52409179427b06d46193c"}],"sha":"ce775a17d90558e99131b0de1fc35f663d25b2fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/ce775a17d90558e99131b0de1fc35f663d25b2fe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/c0edbb6659cc9660a9d52409179427b06d46193c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T02:18:45Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T02:18:45Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"message":"docs: CLAUDE.md, with the names that exist and the lessons that landed\n\ngtm-neutered has not been a resource name in this repo for a long time; the\nline about it named a token that does not exist. Replaced with the real ones.\n\nA page wait had two spellings when that list was written and has four now -\nhide.end() and ga hitCallback joined eventCallback and gtag event_callback.\n\nFour added, each of which cost something to learn today: a resource bump has\nto come with its release, because a pinned URL that serves old code turns a\ncorrect filter into a silent no-op; never mint an id; answer input you do not\nimplement rather than throwing at the caller; and measure against the real\nfile rather than another stand-in, which is how 24 became 65.\n\nAnd on the mutation habit: read the baseline first. A failing suite makes\nevery mutation report \"caught\", which happened here.","tree":{"sha":"40261e99d2688616fde31a211e8d73c45f88efee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/trees/40261e99d2688616fde31a211e8d73c45f88efee"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/commits/c0edbb6659cc9660a9d52409179427b06d46193c","verification":{"payload":"tree 40261e99d2688616fde31a211e8d73c45f88efee\nparent b81a92a8f7f3ac259bc0c29587b992eac2d95e0f\nauthor Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791080325 +1300\ncommitter Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791080325 +1300\n\ndocs: CLAUDE.md, with the names that exist and the lessons that landed\n\ngtm-neutered has not been a resource name in this repo for a long time; the\nline about it named a token that does not exist. Replaced with the real ones.\n\nA page wait had two spellings when that list was written and has four now -\nhide.end() and ga hitCallback joined eventCallback and gtag event_callback.\n\nFour added, each of which cost something to learn today: a resource bump has\nto come with its release, because a pinned URL that serves old code turns a\ncorrect filter into a silent no-op; never mint an id; answer input you do not\nimplement rather than throwing at the caller; and measure against the real\nfile rather than another stand-in, which is how 24 became 65.\n\nAnd on the mutation habit: read the baseline first. A failing suite makes\nevery mutation report \"caught\", which happened here.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPCSVWMUDHjp4kSP8mCo6DMbbZd\nwVKwk1D89AEPXKgVYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQJmLR0Lezo40OcRLwA3G/DUpU+hIpournnqP/j9tcwYHI4Mn83hPOrA90nLs1P1B7C\njjMprEhKr8M6t7JqW/Ogg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T02:18:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/c0edbb6659cc9660a9d52409179427b06d46193c","node_id":"C_kwDOU4p2ytoAKGMwZWRiYjY2NTljYzk2NjBhOWQ1MjQwOTE3OTQyN2IwNmQ0NjE5M2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/b81a92a8f7f3ac259bc0c29587b992eac2d95e0f","sha":"b81a92a8f7f3ac259bc0c29587b992eac2d95e0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/b81a92a8f7f3ac259bc0c29587b992eac2d95e0f"}],"sha":"c0edbb6659cc9660a9d52409179427b06d46193c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/c0edbb6659cc9660a9d52409179427b06d46193c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/b81a92a8f7f3ac259bc0c29587b992eac2d95e0f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T01:34:56Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T01:34:56Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"message":"v1.16.0: gpt 1.0.0, a Publisher Tag stand-in that answers\n\nReplaces uBO''s resource of the same name, and needs no filter to do it: their\nown lists already redirect gpt.js to googletagservices_gpt.js, and a user\nresource of a built-in''s name replaces the built-in. Installing this repo is\nthe whole of it, which also means this has to be at least as safe as what it\ndisplaces.\n\nIt exists because theirs throws. 28 documented, publisher-facing GPT calls\nraise a TypeError on it rather than answering, which takes out the rest of\nwhatever function the page was in - slot.getResponseInformation() returning\nnull so the universal .lineItemId read throws, googletag.enums absent so the\nproperty access throws before any call, setConfig and getConfig absent,\nsecureSignalProviders absent, defineUnit absent, pubads()\n.setTagForUnderAgeOfConsent and .isInitialLoadDisabled absent, slot\n.setForceSafeFrame absent, and twenty more across the slot, companionAds() and\ncontent().\n\nAllowing the real file and blocking it both leave a page coherent. A stub that\nthrows is the only outcome that does neither, and that is the whole argument\nfor replacing a resource that otherwise works.\n\nThe surface was enumerated from the real gpt.js in a browser rather than\ncopied from another resource, which matters because the first attempt at this\nused AdGuard''s as the reference and was wrong twice over: it counted\nslot.getId and slot.setTagForChildDirectedTreatment as defects, and both are\nabsent from the real file too, so throwing on them is faithful. A superset of\nanother stand-in measures nothing. The real file carries googletag 29 names,\npubads() 51, defineSlot(...) 37, sizeMapping() 2, companionAds() 14,\ncontent() 6, and secureSignalProviders 4 - which is NOT an array, whatever the\nname suggests. This answers all of them, with three extras kept because uBO''s\nhas carried them for years: pubadsReady, slot.getDomId,\ncompanionAds().enableSyncLoading.\n\nTwo rules kept from the rest of this repo. No invented ids: getCorrelator()\nanswers '''' and getTagSessionCorrelator() answers 0, because the real ones join\na page''s requests together and minting one here would be this resource\ncreating the thing the blocking exists to prevent. No signal collection:\nsecureSignalProviders.push does nothing, so a third party''s collectorFunction\nis never invoked and no encrypted signal is generated, let alone sent -\nincluding whatever the page queued before this arrived, since draining it\nwould run those collectors.\n\nWhat it does answer is the slot events a page branches on. All five fire,\ndeferred, with isEmpty true: a page that waits to find out whether its slot\nfilled should be told, and a resource that registers the listener and never\ncalls it leaves the page mid-decision, so a slot meant to collapse when empty\nstays open for ever. It builds no google_ads_iframe_*: an event is a page''s\nown question answered, an iframe carrying data-load-complete is a prop for\nsomething checking whether an ad rendered.\n\n15 tests, 12 mutations, 242 and 184 overall. One bug the tests found rather\nthan review: evaluated twice on a page - as a redirect and as a scriptlet -\nthe second copy put an empty listeners Map in front of the first''s, so every\nlistener a page had already registered went deaf. A marker leaves the first\ncopy in charge.","tree":{"sha":"8f8f93adc2198b3a3c3845aaf3ecbb4e4ab359e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/trees/8f8f93adc2198b3a3c3845aaf3ecbb4e4ab359e8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/commits/b81a92a8f7f3ac259bc0c29587b992eac2d95e0f","verification":{"payload":"tree 8f8f93adc2198b3a3c3845aaf3ecbb4e4ab359e8\nparent b2203f80f041f1c2e575dd8dae5cce9ea25e2a9e\nauthor Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791077696 +1300\ncommitter Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791077696 +1300\n\nv1.16.0: gpt 1.0.0, a Publisher Tag stand-in that answers\n\nReplaces uBO''s resource of the same name, and needs no filter to do it: their\nown lists already redirect gpt.js to googletagservices_gpt.js, and a user\nresource of a built-in''s name replaces the built-in. Installing this repo is\nthe whole of it, which also means this has to be at least as safe as what it\ndisplaces.\n\nIt exists because theirs throws. 28 documented, publisher-facing GPT calls\nraise a TypeError on it rather than answering, which takes out the rest of\nwhatever function the page was in - slot.getResponseInformation() returning\nnull so the universal .lineItemId read throws, googletag.enums absent so the\nproperty access throws before any call, setConfig and getConfig absent,\nsecureSignalProviders absent, defineUnit absent, pubads()\n.setTagForUnderAgeOfConsent and .isInitialLoadDisabled absent, slot\n.setForceSafeFrame absent, and twenty more across the slot, companionAds() and\ncontent().\n\nAllowing the real file and blocking it both leave a page coherent. A stub that\nthrows is the only outcome that does neither, and that is the whole argument\nfor replacing a resource that otherwise works.\n\nThe surface was enumerated from the real gpt.js in a browser rather than\ncopied from another resource, which matters because the first attempt at this\nused AdGuard''s as the reference and was wrong twice over: it counted\nslot.getId and slot.setTagForChildDirectedTreatment as defects, and both are\nabsent from the real file too, so throwing on them is faithful. A superset of\nanother stand-in measures nothing. The real file carries googletag 29 names,\npubads() 51, defineSlot(...) 37, sizeMapping() 2, companionAds() 14,\ncontent() 6, and secureSignalProviders 4 - which is NOT an array, whatever the\nname suggests. This answers all of them, with three extras kept because uBO''s\nhas carried them for years: pubadsReady, slot.getDomId,\ncompanionAds().enableSyncLoading.\n\nTwo rules kept from the rest of this repo. No invented ids: getCorrelator()\nanswers '''' and getTagSessionCorrelator() answers 0, because the real ones join\na page''s requests together and minting one here would be this resource\ncreating the thing the blocking exists to prevent. No signal collection:\nsecureSignalProviders.push does nothing, so a third party''s collectorFunction\nis never invoked and no encrypted signal is generated, let alone sent -\nincluding whatever the page queued before this arrived, since draining it\nwould run those collectors.\n\nWhat it does answer is the slot events a page branches on. All five fire,\ndeferred, with isEmpty true: a page that waits to find out whether its slot\nfilled should be told, and a resource that registers the listener and never\ncalls it leaves the page mid-decision, so a slot meant to collapse when empty\nstays open for ever. It builds no google_ads_iframe_*: an event is a page''s\nown question answered, an iframe carrying data-load-complete is a prop for\nsomething checking whether an ad rendered.\n\n15 tests, 12 mutations, 242 and 184 overall. One bug the tests found rather\nthan review: evaluated twice on a page - as a redirect and as a scriptlet -\nthe second copy put an empty listeners Map in front of the first''s, so every\nlistener a page had already registered went deaf. A marker leaves the first\ncopy in charge.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPCSVWMUDHjp4kSP8mCo6DMbbZd\nwVKwk1D89AEPXKgVYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQIwmK3nvAPxE3CI0MKcQ6GQYk+oK0auwZf0B1DkIqU3PYQgKqZTGPfytHx6P3EHEpn\nNqFexoQ13V7In4+QKtQAU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T01:34:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/b81a92a8f7f3ac259bc0c29587b992eac2d95e0f","node_id":"C_kwDOU4p2ytoAKGI4MWE5MmE4ZjdmM2FjMjU5YmMwYzI5NTg3Yjk5MmVhYzJkOTVlMGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/b2203f80f041f1c2e575dd8dae5cce9ea25e2a9e","sha":"b2203f80f041f1c2e575dd8dae5cce9ea25e2a9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/b2203f80f041f1c2e575dd8dae5cce9ea25e2a9e"}],"sha":"b81a92a8f7f3ac259bc0c29587b992eac2d95e0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/b81a92a8f7f3ac259bc0c29587b992eac2d95e0f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/b2203f80f041f1c2e575dd8dae5cce9ea25e2a9e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T00:53:41Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T00:53:41Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"message":"v1.15.0: gtm 1.8.0, answer hitCallback on the ga this file puts up\n\nFrom comparing this resource against uBO''s and AdGuard''s rather than reading\nit: AdGuard answers three callback spellings that neither uBO''s gtm stub nor\nthis one did. One of them is this file''s own business.\n\n  ga(''send'', ''pageview'', { hitCallback: () => location.href = url })\n\nThis resource puts up window.ga itself, so where analytics.js was blocked with\nno surrogate of its own that stub is the only ga on the page - and a page\nnavigating from the callback had a dead link, caused by the stub rather than\nby the blocking. uBO''s analytics surrogate answers it where it applies and\nstill wins there; this answers their three shapes for the case where it does\nnot: a trailing options object, a trailing function, and ''hitCallback'' given\npositionally with a function after it.\n\nDeferred by a tick, because theirs answers after the hit rather than inside\nthe call, and a page that navigates from it should not do so before its own\nline has finished.\n\nOne divergence from uBO inside what was taken. Their surrogate hands the\ntrailing-function shape a tracker built with ga.create(). This hands over one\nwhose get() answers undefined: a get(''clientId'') returning something\nplausible would be this resource minting a tracking id, which is the line\ngtag(''get'', ...) already refuses to cross.\n\nThe other two spellings are deliberately not taken, and the document says so.\ndataLayer.push([ { callback } ]) is the _gaq shape, and AdGuard answers it\nbecause one resource of theirs serves analytics.js and gtm.js both; this one\ndoes not. A nested event_callback could not be tied to anything a real page\ndoes, and copying surface because another project has it is how a stand-in\ngrows ways to be wrong.\n\nAlso in the comparison document, as a negative result: there is nothing to\nlearn from either project on privacy. Searched across five of their Google\nresources for gaOptout, ga-disable, doNotTrack, google_tag_data, _gl, gclid,\ndocument.cookie and removeItem - the only hits are hitCallback and AdGuard''s\ngoogle_optimize noop. Neither sets an opt-out, clears a cookie or strips link\ndecoration; the privacy comes from the request not being made. Where this repo\ngoes further is tabulated rather than claimed.\n\n6 tests, 5 mutations, 227 and 172 overall. Two harness findings, both mine:\nthe positional-hitCallback test passed the function last, so the branch above\ncaught it and the test passed against the branch being deleted; and rewriting\nthe ga block stranded an older mutation''s anchor, which npm run anchors caught\nbefore this commit. A duplicate mutation of the same guard was dropped.","tree":{"sha":"6380115889da41af10d9c1cab61ecf7579354e74","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/trees/6380115889da41af10d9c1cab61ecf7579354e74"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/commits/b2203f80f041f1c2e575dd8dae5cce9ea25e2a9e","verification":{"payload":"tree 6380115889da41af10d9c1cab61ecf7579354e74\nparent 1f81fad43e33722ebc219509d935076a988a8cac\nauthor Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791075221 +1300\ncommitter Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791075221 +1300\n\nv1.15.0: gtm 1.8.0, answer hitCallback on the ga this file puts up\n\nFrom comparing this resource against uBO''s and AdGuard''s rather than reading\nit: AdGuard answers three callback spellings that neither uBO''s gtm stub nor\nthis one did. One of them is this file''s own business.\n\n  ga(''send'', ''pageview'', { hitCallback: () => location.href = url })\n\nThis resource puts up window.ga itself, so where analytics.js was blocked with\nno surrogate of its own that stub is the only ga on the page - and a page\nnavigating from the callback had a dead link, caused by the stub rather than\nby the blocking. uBO''s analytics surrogate answers it where it applies and\nstill wins there; this answers their three shapes for the case where it does\nnot: a trailing options object, a trailing function, and ''hitCallback'' given\npositionally with a function after it.\n\nDeferred by a tick, because theirs answers after the hit rather than inside\nthe call, and a page that navigates from it should not do so before its own\nline has finished.\n\nOne divergence from uBO inside what was taken. Their surrogate hands the\ntrailing-function shape a tracker built with ga.create(). This hands over one\nwhose get() answers undefined: a get(''clientId'') returning something\nplausible would be this resource minting a tracking id, which is the line\ngtag(''get'', ...) already refuses to cross.\n\nThe other two spellings are deliberately not taken, and the document says so.\ndataLayer.push([ { callback } ]) is the _gaq shape, and AdGuard answers it\nbecause one resource of theirs serves analytics.js and gtm.js both; this one\ndoes not. A nested event_callback could not be tied to anything a real page\ndoes, and copying surface because another project has it is how a stand-in\ngrows ways to be wrong.\n\nAlso in the comparison document, as a negative result: there is nothing to\nlearn from either project on privacy. Searched across five of their Google\nresources for gaOptout, ga-disable, doNotTrack, google_tag_data, _gl, gclid,\ndocument.cookie and removeItem - the only hits are hitCallback and AdGuard''s\ngoogle_optimize noop. Neither sets an opt-out, clears a cookie or strips link\ndecoration; the privacy comes from the request not being made. Where this repo\ngoes further is tabulated rather than claimed.\n\n6 tests, 5 mutations, 227 and 172 overall. Two harness findings, both mine:\nthe positional-hitCallback test passed the function last, so the branch above\ncaught it and the test passed against the branch being deleted; and rewriting\nthe ga block stranded an older mutation''s anchor, which npm run anchors caught\nbefore this commit. A duplicate mutation of the same guard was dropped.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPCSVWMUDHjp4kSP8mCo6DMbbZd\nwVKwk1D89AEPXKgVYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQIxcCWHxXmDO/I4d18YpUVc0s8wFHO9o1akzZ1vXzWATc3y3ErIKPmEjbYWC062SIo\nHaNdXClzLO1Sutef0T6Qs=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T00:53:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/b2203f80f041f1c2e575dd8dae5cce9ea25e2a9e","node_id":"C_kwDOU4p2ytoAKGIyMjAzZjgwZjA0MWYxYzJlNTc1ZGQ4ZGFlNWNjZTllYTI1ZTJhOWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/1f81fad43e33722ebc219509d935076a988a8cac","sha":"1f81fad43e33722ebc219509d935076a988a8cac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/1f81fad43e33722ebc219509d935076a988a8cac"}],"sha":"b2203f80f041f1c2e575dd8dae5cce9ea25e2a9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/b2203f80f041f1c2e575dd8dae5cce9ea25e2a9e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/1f81fad43e33722ebc219509d935076a988a8cac/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T00:32:00Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T00:32:00Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"message":"docs: put this repo in the comparison, on the file where it belongs\n\nThe GPT tables had no column for us because we ship no GPT resource, which\nleft the obvious question unanswered. All three projects do ship a gtm.js\nstand-in, so that is the table where this repo is comparable, and it is now\nthe first one - measured the same way, each resource served as the gtm.js a\npage actually requests, behind Google''s own snippet.\n\nAdGuard turns out to have no gtm.js resource of its own any more: their\ngoogletagmanager-gtm redirect is obsolete and the name aliases to\ngoogle-analytics, so a redirected container is answered by their Analytics\nmock. That is a position rather than an oversight - it treats gtm.js as an\nanalytics script - and uBO''s 43-line stub takes the same view.\n\nFour rows carry more than a tick, and two of them are ours to own:\n\n- dataLayer.push''s return. The real one answers with the new length. uBO''s\n  returns undefined, AdGuard''s returns noopFunc deliberately, ours returns a\n  number because it keeps the page''s own array.\n- the anti-flicker with a second container still expected. Google''s snippet\n  lists every container it waits for and only the last one in should call\n  end(). uBO''s and AdGuard''s call it unconditionally, un-hiding a page another\n  container is still loading for; ours defers, as their own code does.\n- gtag''s event_callback, which uBO misses - so a page whose links open from a\n  gtag event has no working links.\n- an unknown registry method throws here. Stated as deliberate rather than\n  buried: it throws against the real gtm.js too, and answering every unknown\n  read with a function would make typeof checks lie. That is a different thing\n  from the gpt.js rows, where what throws is documented and publisher-facing.\n\nThe globals table is the clearest statement of the trade: uBO and AdGuard add\none name, this repo adds eight. Written as a cost, because it is one - every\none is a surface a site could detect, accepted in exchange for the breakages\nthey fix, and consent=off gives back the consent ones.\n\nTwo measurement errors on the way, both mine, both caught by the harness\nrather than by reading: the first fixture''s anti-flicker block omitted the\ncontainer id, so it read as if this repo failed to end the hiding when it was\ncorrectly declining to; and a probe key with a stray escape broke the script\nbefore it ran.","tree":{"sha":"32d95ae53ffa6ddad14a3fb6cd6d4d44ddbb1232","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/trees/32d95ae53ffa6ddad14a3fb6cd6d4d44ddbb1232"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/commits/1f81fad43e33722ebc219509d935076a988a8cac","verification":{"payload":"tree 32d95ae53ffa6ddad14a3fb6cd6d4d44ddbb1232\nparent 9ceed1300943146ec3b943f96c53e29ba3d6d977\nauthor Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791073920 +1300\ncommitter Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791073920 +1300\n\ndocs: put this repo in the comparison, on the file where it belongs\n\nThe GPT tables had no column for us because we ship no GPT resource, which\nleft the obvious question unanswered. All three projects do ship a gtm.js\nstand-in, so that is the table where this repo is comparable, and it is now\nthe first one - measured the same way, each resource served as the gtm.js a\npage actually requests, behind Google''s own snippet.\n\nAdGuard turns out to have no gtm.js resource of its own any more: their\ngoogletagmanager-gtm redirect is obsolete and the name aliases to\ngoogle-analytics, so a redirected container is answered by their Analytics\nmock. That is a position rather than an oversight - it treats gtm.js as an\nanalytics script - and uBO''s 43-line stub takes the same view.\n\nFour rows carry more than a tick, and two of them are ours to own:\n\n- dataLayer.push''s return. The real one answers with the new length. uBO''s\n  returns undefined, AdGuard''s returns noopFunc deliberately, ours returns a\n  number because it keeps the page''s own array.\n- the anti-flicker with a second container still expected. Google''s snippet\n  lists every container it waits for and only the last one in should call\n  end(). uBO''s and AdGuard''s call it unconditionally, un-hiding a page another\n  container is still loading for; ours defers, as their own code does.\n- gtag''s event_callback, which uBO misses - so a page whose links open from a\n  gtag event has no working links.\n- an unknown registry method throws here. Stated as deliberate rather than\n  buried: it throws against the real gtm.js too, and answering every unknown\n  read with a function would make typeof checks lie. That is a different thing\n  from the gpt.js rows, where what throws is documented and publisher-facing.\n\nThe globals table is the clearest statement of the trade: uBO and AdGuard add\none name, this repo adds eight. Written as a cost, because it is one - every\none is a surface a site could detect, accepted in exchange for the breakages\nthey fix, and consent=off gives back the consent ones.\n\nTwo measurement errors on the way, both mine, both caught by the harness\nrather than by reading: the first fixture''s anti-flicker block omitted the\ncontainer id, so it read as if this repo failed to end the hiding when it was\ncorrectly declining to; and a probe key with a stray escape broke the script\nbefore it ran.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPCSVWMUDHjp4kSP8mCo6DMbbZd\nwVKwk1D89AEPXKgVYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQCUXsImRc9jTE8VAovmRgBmfITEoW9O+tWUJe0uRMJXlxvKIVSw7feJgpL542bTstE\nXb0z+KfcQrnwL1JksZMgw=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T00:32:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/1f81fad43e33722ebc219509d935076a988a8cac","node_id":"C_kwDOU4p2ytoAKDFmODFmYWQ0M2UzMzcyMmViYzIxOTUwOWQ5MzUwNzZhOTg4YThjYWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/9ceed1300943146ec3b943f96c53e29ba3d6d977","sha":"9ceed1300943146ec3b943f96c53e29ba3d6d977","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/9ceed1300943146ec3b943f96c53e29ba3d6d977"}],"sha":"1f81fad43e33722ebc219509d935076a988a8cac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/1f81fad43e33722ebc219509d935076a988a8cac"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/9ceed1300943146ec3b943f96c53e29ba3d6d977/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T23:48:44Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T23:48:44Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"message":"docs: uBO''s GPT resource against AdGuard''s, measured\n\nCame out of chasing nowtv.com.tr, where a video wants gpt.js allowed and the\nplayer touches googletag 47 times. The surrogate was the obvious suspect and\nis not the answer - AdGuard''s resource behind that page leaves the player in\nthe same state as uBO''s - but the comparison is worth keeping, so here it is\nwith the measurements rather than an impression.\n\nBoth resources evaluated into the same blank page in headless Chrome and\nprobed with what publisher code actually does. AdGuard''s surface is a strict\nsuperset: uBO has no method AdGuard lacks, anywhere. The slot is where the gap\nis, 20 methods against 38, which is also where page code spends its time.\n\nThe finding worth acting on is not the size. Three of uBO''s throw rather than\nanswer - slot.getResponseInformation() returns null so the universal\n.lineItemId read throws, and googletag.setConfig and\npubads().isInitialLoadDisabled do not exist at all. A noop stub degrades a\npage; a throwing stub breaks it, and allowing or blocking the real file both\nleave the page coherent, so throwing is the one option that does neither.\nsetConfig is the one that widens with time, since GPT has moved publisher\nconfiguration there.\n\nSecond is the events. uBO''s addEventListener registers a listener and never\ncalls it, so the common empty-slot collapse runs neither branch and the page\nsits mid-decision instead of being told \"empty\".\n\nBoth define exactly one global and set both readiness flags, so a page cannot\ntell them apart by looking - which is the part people assume differs.\n\nBenefits are given for both rather than a verdict: 154 lines against 455 is\nless to audit, holds no state and creates no iframe on a page''s behalf, and\nfor a page that defines slots and does not look back it is enough. The split\nis whether a page is better under-served or over-served, and that differs per\npage. The throwing is not a trade-off.\n\nWhat transfers to this repo is one rule, now explicit in AGENTS.md: answer\ninput you do not implement rather than throwing at the caller. The TCF\nstand-in added in gtm 1.7.0 answers an unrecognised command with\ncallback(null, false) for exactly that reason.\n\nThis repo ships no GPT resource and should not: it is not a tag manager\nloader, and uBO already carries one of that name.","tree":{"sha":"75a1731f7115e3b5c1c27a3f3626b53684f2101c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/trees/75a1731f7115e3b5c1c27a3f3626b53684f2101c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/commits/9ceed1300943146ec3b943f96c53e29ba3d6d977","verification":{"payload":"tree 75a1731f7115e3b5c1c27a3f3626b53684f2101c\nparent c20014b2b57b6428df69e8a12c4006e685fac55a\nauthor Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791071324 +1300\ncommitter Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791071324 +1300\n\ndocs: uBO''s GPT resource against AdGuard''s, measured\n\nCame out of chasing nowtv.com.tr, where a video wants gpt.js allowed and the\nplayer touches googletag 47 times. The surrogate was the obvious suspect and\nis not the answer - AdGuard''s resource behind that page leaves the player in\nthe same state as uBO''s - but the comparison is worth keeping, so here it is\nwith the measurements rather than an impression.\n\nBoth resources evaluated into the same blank page in headless Chrome and\nprobed with what publisher code actually does. AdGuard''s surface is a strict\nsuperset: uBO has no method AdGuard lacks, anywhere. The slot is where the gap\nis, 20 methods against 38, which is also where page code spends its time.\n\nThe finding worth acting on is not the size. Three of uBO''s throw rather than\nanswer - slot.getResponseInformation() returns null so the universal\n.lineItemId read throws, and googletag.setConfig and\npubads().isInitialLoadDisabled do not exist at all. A noop stub degrades a\npage; a throwing stub breaks it, and allowing or blocking the real file both\nleave the page coherent, so throwing is the one option that does neither.\nsetConfig is the one that widens with time, since GPT has moved publisher\nconfiguration there.\n\nSecond is the events. uBO''s addEventListener registers a listener and never\ncalls it, so the common empty-slot collapse runs neither branch and the page\nsits mid-decision instead of being told \"empty\".\n\nBoth define exactly one global and set both readiness flags, so a page cannot\ntell them apart by looking - which is the part people assume differs.\n\nBenefits are given for both rather than a verdict: 154 lines against 455 is\nless to audit, holds no state and creates no iframe on a page''s behalf, and\nfor a page that defines slots and does not look back it is enough. The split\nis whether a page is better under-served or over-served, and that differs per\npage. The throwing is not a trade-off.\n\nWhat transfers to this repo is one rule, now explicit in AGENTS.md: answer\ninput you do not implement rather than throwing at the caller. The TCF\nstand-in added in gtm 1.7.0 answers an unrecognised command with\ncallback(null, false) for exactly that reason.\n\nThis repo ships no GPT resource and should not: it is not a tag manager\nloader, and uBO already carries one of that name.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPCSVWMUDHjp4kSP8mCo6DMbbZd\nwVKwk1D89AEPXKgVYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQMjzeN+rKPfaVkKqk6qrOwnMI5Ie49uLGS48E2B2xhnGj34hmyYR6U3UtJXwjdOChp\nDaDxXBat7uutn+X5bRzwQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T23:48:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/9ceed1300943146ec3b943f96c53e29ba3d6d977","node_id":"C_kwDOU4p2ytoAKDljZWVkMTMwMDk0MzE0NmVjM2I5NDNmOTZjNTNlMjliYTNkNmQ5Nzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/c20014b2b57b6428df69e8a12c4006e685fac55a","sha":"c20014b2b57b6428df69e8a12c4006e685fac55a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/c20014b2b57b6428df69e8a12c4006e685fac55a"}],"sha":"9ceed1300943146ec3b943f96c53e29ba3d6d977","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/9ceed1300943146ec3b943f96c53e29ba3d6d977"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/c20014b2b57b6428df69e8a12c4006e685fac55a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T11:55:50Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T11:55:50Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"message":"v1.14.0: gtm 1.7.0, answer the TCF question a container took with it\n\nnowtv.com.tr''s video needs an exception on gtm.js. Its container holds\nexactly one script - OneTrust''s otSDKStub.js - and the player''s init loop is\n\n  var userMadeChoiceBefore =\n      localStorage.getItem(\"cookieChoiceMade\") === \"true\";\n  setInterval(function() {\n    if (el != null && typeof ADMPlayer != ''undefined''\n        && userMadeChoiceBefore && oneTrustInitited && ...) { ... }\n\nwhere oneTrustInitited has exactly one source:\n\n  window.__tcfapi(''addEventListener'', 2, function(tcData, success) {\n    if (success && (tcData.eventStatus === ''tcloaded''\n        || tcData.eventStatus === ''useractioncomplete'')) {\n      initGoogleAds(tcData); } });\n\nSo with the container replaced __tcfapi never arrives and the loop spins for\never. Their GPT path gives up after two seconds; the player never does.\n\nThis answers it from the redirect alone, with a refusal: gdprApplies true and\nnot one purpose, vendor, special feature or publisher consent - the strictest\nthing that API can say. Measured against the live page, that is enough to turn\noneTrustInitited true and get the player constructed, where before both were\nfalse.\n\nconsent=all does NOT reach it. The group variables are a judgement about a\nsite showing its own content; a TCF purpose consent tells every ad vendor on\nthe page they may proceed, which is the one thing this must never say for\nsomeone. consent=off removes it. No __tcfapiLocator frame either - that is\nthere so third party frames can ask the CMP for a consent string, and there is\nnothing here for them to have.\n\nWhat this does not settle, said plainly because it was reported twice and I\ngot it wrong twice: that page also needs its own localStorage flag\n(set-local-storage-item, cookieChoiceMade, true), and its player is\nfirst-party /js/app.js which touches googletag 47 times. If gpt.js has to be\nallowed for playback, that is a question about uBO''s GPT surrogate, not about\nthis resource. My first measurements counted <video> elements and\ndata-player-inited and called that working; playback never starts in a\nheadless browser here even with everything allowed, so the gpt.js claim is\nrecorded rather than measured.\n\n14 tests, 10 mutations. One of those mutations survived and one test had to be\nrepinned: adding tcf= to the summary line broke the test that pins it exactly,\nand until that was fixed every mutation reported \"caught\" off a red baseline -\nwhich is worth remembering, because a red baseline makes a mutation run say\nnothing at all.","tree":{"sha":"a7f0543b0509991140134669a94e43450fe018a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/trees/a7f0543b0509991140134669a94e43450fe018a3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/commits/c20014b2b57b6428df69e8a12c4006e685fac55a","verification":{"payload":"tree a7f0543b0509991140134669a94e43450fe018a3\nparent 75b316f708c6a1a939e87f56a31dd6cc4ef629d5\nauthor Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791028550 +1300\ncommitter Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791028550 +1300\n\nv1.14.0: gtm 1.7.0, answer the TCF question a container took with it\n\nnowtv.com.tr''s video needs an exception on gtm.js. Its container holds\nexactly one script - OneTrust''s otSDKStub.js - and the player''s init loop is\n\n  var userMadeChoiceBefore =\n      localStorage.getItem(\"cookieChoiceMade\") === \"true\";\n  setInterval(function() {\n    if (el != null && typeof ADMPlayer != ''undefined''\n        && userMadeChoiceBefore && oneTrustInitited && ...) { ... }\n\nwhere oneTrustInitited has exactly one source:\n\n  window.__tcfapi(''addEventListener'', 2, function(tcData, success) {\n    if (success && (tcData.eventStatus === ''tcloaded''\n        || tcData.eventStatus === ''useractioncomplete'')) {\n      initGoogleAds(tcData); } });\n\nSo with the container replaced __tcfapi never arrives and the loop spins for\never. Their GPT path gives up after two seconds; the player never does.\n\nThis answers it from the redirect alone, with a refusal: gdprApplies true and\nnot one purpose, vendor, special feature or publisher consent - the strictest\nthing that API can say. Measured against the live page, that is enough to turn\noneTrustInitited true and get the player constructed, where before both were\nfalse.\n\nconsent=all does NOT reach it. The group variables are a judgement about a\nsite showing its own content; a TCF purpose consent tells every ad vendor on\nthe page they may proceed, which is the one thing this must never say for\nsomeone. consent=off removes it. No __tcfapiLocator frame either - that is\nthere so third party frames can ask the CMP for a consent string, and there is\nnothing here for them to have.\n\nWhat this does not settle, said plainly because it was reported twice and I\ngot it wrong twice: that page also needs its own localStorage flag\n(set-local-storage-item, cookieChoiceMade, true), and its player is\nfirst-party /js/app.js which touches googletag 47 times. If gpt.js has to be\nallowed for playback, that is a question about uBO''s GPT surrogate, not about\nthis resource. My first measurements counted <video> elements and\ndata-player-inited and called that working; playback never starts in a\nheadless browser here even with everything allowed, so the gpt.js claim is\nrecorded rather than measured.\n\n14 tests, 10 mutations. One of those mutations survived and one test had to be\nrepinned: adding tcf= to the summary line broke the test that pins it exactly,\nand until that was fixed every mutation reported \"caught\" off a red baseline -\nwhich is worth remembering, because a red baseline makes a mutation run say\nnothing at all.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPCSVWMUDHjp4kSP8mCo6DMbbZd\nwVKwk1D89AEPXKgVYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQAkCRSfWiuaARe4h2OxCnkKoA/ugAP5M/tM7QENT+JpZnBk3F9Uo3kn/wQdHLHddFU\nRvZJbGmYQyW4DFDX64OA8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T11:55:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/c20014b2b57b6428df69e8a12c4006e685fac55a","node_id":"C_kwDOU4p2ytoAKGMyMDAxNGIyYjU3YjY0MjhkZjY5ZThhMTJjNDAwNmU2ODVmYWM1NWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/75b316f708c6a1a939e87f56a31dd6cc4ef629d5","sha":"75b316f708c6a1a939e87f56a31dd6cc4ef629d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/75b316f708c6a1a939e87f56a31dd6cc4ef629d5"}],"sha":"c20014b2b57b6428df69e8a12c4006e685fac55a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/c20014b2b57b6428df69e8a12c4006e685fac55a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/75b316f708c6a1a939e87f56a31dd6cc4ef629d5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T11:10:56Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T11:10:56Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"message":"v1.13.0: tag 1.6.0, a trigger on the path\n\nshop.moen.com/pages/faucet-finder-quiz shows nothing where the container is\nreplaced. The quiz is Zoovu, the page already carries the mount -\n<div id=\"zoovu-assistant\"> - and GTM-5M3PDQZ8 carries the only thing that\nfills it. Nothing in that chain is on any list: zoovu.com appears in no\nfilter list at all, so the launcher was simply never injected.\n\nMeasured against the live page: with gtm.js replaced the mount is empty, and\nwith the line below it holds the same zv-advisor the container produces, down\nto the data-zoovu-assistant-claimed attribute.\n\n  shop.moen.com##+js(gtm-tag, https://api-barracuda.zoovu.com/api/v1/launchers/mznpQl/moen-faucet-discovery, path=/pages/faucet-finder-quiz)\n\npath= is why that is not just a url. The container holds the tag behind\n\n  _eq macro 56 /pages/faucet-finder-quiz\n  macro 56: {\"function\":\"__u\",\"vtp_component\":\"PATH\"}\n\nand when= cannot say it - when= reads the data layer, and a path is not in\nit. Without a path form the line loads a vendor meant for one page on every\npage of a shop, which is the objection this file already makes about\nscriptlet filters not being scopable to a path. Their four shapes of the test\nare one argument: path=/x (_eq), path=/x* (_sw), path=*x (_ew), path=*x*\n(_cn). Only the ends are wildcards, so a path with a * in the middle is text.\nOff the page it was for, the line stands down and names it:\nskipped=path want=/pages/faucet-finder-quiz\n\nnpm run tags reads these out of a container and prints the whole filter now,\nso a path-triggered tag needs no hand-assembly - which is most of them.\n\n207 tests, 157 mutations. Two of my own slips on the way, both caught by the\nharness rather than by reading: a mutation anchor left stale by editing the\nline it pointed at, and a test that asserted the opposite of its own comment\nabout a mid-string star.","tree":{"sha":"8c75997b2c13c37b6840b86a0192a2d35062d220","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/trees/8c75997b2c13c37b6840b86a0192a2d35062d220"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/commits/75b316f708c6a1a939e87f56a31dd6cc4ef629d5","verification":{"payload":"tree 8c75997b2c13c37b6840b86a0192a2d35062d220\nparent 2ea7ae1eaa0325c9a4a6a7b69d60d6c938a79150\nauthor Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791025856 +1300\ncommitter Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791025856 +1300\n\nv1.13.0: tag 1.6.0, a trigger on the path\n\nshop.moen.com/pages/faucet-finder-quiz shows nothing where the container is\nreplaced. The quiz is Zoovu, the page already carries the mount -\n<div id=\"zoovu-assistant\"> - and GTM-5M3PDQZ8 carries the only thing that\nfills it. Nothing in that chain is on any list: zoovu.com appears in no\nfilter list at all, so the launcher was simply never injected.\n\nMeasured against the live page: with gtm.js replaced the mount is empty, and\nwith the line below it holds the same zv-advisor the container produces, down\nto the data-zoovu-assistant-claimed attribute.\n\n  shop.moen.com##+js(gtm-tag, https://api-barracuda.zoovu.com/api/v1/launchers/mznpQl/moen-faucet-discovery, path=/pages/faucet-finder-quiz)\n\npath= is why that is not just a url. The container holds the tag behind\n\n  _eq macro 56 /pages/faucet-finder-quiz\n  macro 56: {\"function\":\"__u\",\"vtp_component\":\"PATH\"}\n\nand when= cannot say it - when= reads the data layer, and a path is not in\nit. Without a path form the line loads a vendor meant for one page on every\npage of a shop, which is the objection this file already makes about\nscriptlet filters not being scopable to a path. Their four shapes of the test\nare one argument: path=/x (_eq), path=/x* (_sw), path=*x (_ew), path=*x*\n(_cn). Only the ends are wildcards, so a path with a * in the middle is text.\nOff the page it was for, the line stands down and names it:\nskipped=path want=/pages/faucet-finder-quiz\n\nnpm run tags reads these out of a container and prints the whole filter now,\nso a path-triggered tag needs no hand-assembly - which is most of them.\n\n207 tests, 157 mutations. Two of my own slips on the way, both caught by the\nharness rather than by reading: a mutation anchor left stale by editing the\nline it pointed at, and a test that asserted the opposite of its own comment\nabout a mid-string star.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPCSVWMUDHjp4kSP8mCo6DMbbZd\nwVKwk1D89AEPXKgVYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQHyZ6rsELUZp/WEqchQiRljGCkIiT+MqzQqVkMalfneZvj7wCXsHNm7Ph6fwiFKKEE\nIUClNVu590VUIq8WDsbQo=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T11:10:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/75b316f708c6a1a939e87f56a31dd6cc4ef629d5","node_id":"C_kwDOU4p2ytoAKDc1YjMxNmY3MDhjNmExYTkzOWU4N2Y1NmEzMWRkNmNjNGVmNjI5ZDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/2ea7ae1eaa0325c9a4a6a7b69d60d6c938a79150","sha":"2ea7ae1eaa0325c9a4a6a7b69d60d6c938a79150","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/2ea7ae1eaa0325c9a4a6a7b69d60d6c938a79150"}],"sha":"75b316f708c6a1a939e87f56a31dd6cc4ef629d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/75b316f708c6a1a939e87f56a31dd6cc4ef629d5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/2ea7ae1eaa0325c9a4a6a7b69d60d6c938a79150/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T10:48:55Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T10:48:55Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"message":"v1.12.0: tag 1.5.0, the SDE their account picks a campaign by\n\nReported twice as \"still not working\", with a console showing\nbuilt=lpTag site=3178090, their tag running, all 36 taglets loaded and the\nvisitor API called. Everything healthy and nothing rendered, which is the\nhardest shape there is to read from a log - and the log was right both times.\n\nThat container has FIVE tags touching lpTag, not one. The bootstrap is the\nfirst; the fifth is\n\n  var isSupported = CheckAbcSupport(), targetChannel = \"chat\";\n  isSupported && (targetChannel = \"abc\");\n  lpTag.sdes.push({ type: \"mrktInfo\", info: { campaignId: targetChannel } });\n\nand that is how their account selects a campaign. Reproducing the bootstrap\nalone gets a page where nothing is wrong and no engagement is served.\n\nMeasured against the live page, each pair run back to back, which is what\nsettled it after a wrong guess that this was LivePerson''s own targeting:\n\n  container allowed    section [\"service\",\"contact-us\"]   2 elements\n  bootstrap alone      section []                         0\n  bootstrap + the SDE  section []                         2\n\nSo campaign= pushes it, and it has to be in the filter: campaignId=zzzqqq\nrenders nothing, so the value is targeted on exactly, it is a literal in\ntheir container tag, and it is nowhere in the page. Not defaultable.\n\nA third tag sets lpTag.section from the path. Seeded to match the control\nexactly it changed nothing, and with the SDE the button renders with section\nempty - which is the lucky answer, because section is per-path and a cosmetic\nfilter cannot be scoped to a path.\n\nmrktInfo is the only SDE accepted, deliberately: the others that container\npushes are a visitor''s income band, basket and order, and a filter argument\nis no place to invent those.\n\nAlso fixed while comparing the two objects field by field: a seeded\nlpTag.section was being flattened by String(), which would hand their\nframework \"service,contact-us\" where their container assigns an array.\n\n22 tests, 21 mutations, all caught.","tree":{"sha":"195e86dc793f867f1bdf840fab37eabed4f876f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/trees/195e86dc793f867f1bdf840fab37eabed4f876f0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/commits/2ea7ae1eaa0325c9a4a6a7b69d60d6c938a79150","verification":{"payload":"tree 195e86dc793f867f1bdf840fab37eabed4f876f0\nparent 29f6ad9af4083becdae9551274699c0db9e20f1f\nauthor Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791024535 +1300\ncommitter Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791024535 +1300\n\nv1.12.0: tag 1.5.0, the SDE their account picks a campaign by\n\nReported twice as \"still not working\", with a console showing\nbuilt=lpTag site=3178090, their tag running, all 36 taglets loaded and the\nvisitor API called. Everything healthy and nothing rendered, which is the\nhardest shape there is to read from a log - and the log was right both times.\n\nThat container has FIVE tags touching lpTag, not one. The bootstrap is the\nfirst; the fifth is\n\n  var isSupported = CheckAbcSupport(), targetChannel = \"chat\";\n  isSupported && (targetChannel = \"abc\");\n  lpTag.sdes.push({ type: \"mrktInfo\", info: { campaignId: targetChannel } });\n\nand that is how their account selects a campaign. Reproducing the bootstrap\nalone gets a page where nothing is wrong and no engagement is served.\n\nMeasured against the live page, each pair run back to back, which is what\nsettled it after a wrong guess that this was LivePerson''s own targeting:\n\n  container allowed    section [\"service\",\"contact-us\"]   2 elements\n  bootstrap alone      section []                         0\n  bootstrap + the SDE  section []                         2\n\nSo campaign= pushes it, and it has to be in the filter: campaignId=zzzqqq\nrenders nothing, so the value is targeted on exactly, it is a literal in\ntheir container tag, and it is nowhere in the page. Not defaultable.\n\nA third tag sets lpTag.section from the path. Seeded to match the control\nexactly it changed nothing, and with the SDE the button renders with section\nempty - which is the lucky answer, because section is per-path and a cosmetic\nfilter cannot be scoped to a path.\n\nmrktInfo is the only SDE accepted, deliberately: the others that container\npushes are a visitor''s income band, basket and order, and a filter argument\nis no place to invent those.\n\nAlso fixed while comparing the two objects field by field: a seeded\nlpTag.section was being flattened by String(), which would hand their\nframework \"service,contact-us\" where their container assigns an array.\n\n22 tests, 21 mutations, all caught.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPCSVWMUDHjp4kSP8mCo6DMbbZd\nwVKwk1D89AEPXKgVYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQM3EoOi7rW2IxILvw0wP0dJADiReEC4hJGk7WUvI1+nGYgk/345RuHmT2QVluGokIQ\nzmiYLzhaDZeO0NmNOABgk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T10:48:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/2ea7ae1eaa0325c9a4a6a7b69d60d6c938a79150","node_id":"C_kwDOU4p2ytoAKDJlYTdhZTFlYWEwMzI1YzlhNGE2YTdiNjlkNjBkNmM5MzhhNzkxNTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/29f6ad9af4083becdae9551274699c0db9e20f1f","sha":"29f6ad9af4083becdae9551274699c0db9e20f1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/29f6ad9af4083becdae9551274699c0db9e20f1f"}],"sha":"2ea7ae1eaa0325c9a4a6a7b69d60d6c938a79150","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/2ea7ae1eaa0325c9a4a6a7b69d60d6c938a79150"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/29f6ad9af4083becdae9551274699c0db9e20f1f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T10:29:09Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T10:29:09Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"message":"v1.11.1: tag 1.4.1, so the version in the console means one thing\n\nThe previous commit changed what gtm-tag does and left it reporting 1.4.0.\nThat breaks the thing the console line is for: two builds answering to the\nsame number, on a report being diagnosed from exactly that line. The check\nadded in v1.11.0 does not catch it either - it compares the version in dist\nagainst the version the pinned tag serves, and both said 1.4.0.\n\nSo: tag 1.4.1, release v1.11.1, and the rule it implies - a change to what a\nresource does is a change to its version, whether or not anything else makes\nyou bump it.","tree":{"sha":"67fc242f26672089b12749e6185cd8db5ab6f2f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/trees/67fc242f26672089b12749e6185cd8db5ab6f2f7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/commits/29f6ad9af4083becdae9551274699c0db9e20f1f","verification":{"payload":"tree 67fc242f26672089b12749e6185cd8db5ab6f2f7\nparent 503362cce40bb61caa625841c71e9c66e626eef7\nauthor Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791023349 +1300\ncommitter Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791023349 +1300\n\nv1.11.1: tag 1.4.1, so the version in the console means one thing\n\nThe previous commit changed what gtm-tag does and left it reporting 1.4.0.\nThat breaks the thing the console line is for: two builds answering to the\nsame number, on a report being diagnosed from exactly that line. The check\nadded in v1.11.0 does not catch it either - it compares the version in dist\nagainst the version the pinned tag serves, and both said 1.4.0.\n\nSo: tag 1.4.1, release v1.11.1, and the rule it implies - a change to what a\nresource does is a change to its version, whether or not anything else makes\nyou bump it.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPCSVWMUDHjp4kSP8mCo6DMbbZd\nwVKwk1D89AEPXKgVYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQEH+u4Ba25zhXpSjnAar6F7lXScKDjQe9cIsIZ1mBNJ0ab0cwSHXgabsL9RD1g+1U9\n8eb3wLBerIij0H1/5dmwQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T10:29:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/29f6ad9af4083becdae9551274699c0db9e20f1f","node_id":"C_kwDOU4p2ytoAKDI5ZjZhZDlhZjQwODNiZWNkYWU5NTUxMjc0Njk5YzBkYjllMjBmMWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/503362cce40bb61caa625841c71e9c66e626eef7","sha":"503362cce40bb61caa625841c71e9c66e626eef7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/503362cce40bb61caa625841c71e9c66e626eef7"}],"sha":"29f6ad9af4083becdae9551274699c0db9e20f1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/29f6ad9af4083becdae9551274699c0db9e20f1f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/503362cce40bb61caa625841c71e9c66e626eef7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T10:28:36Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T10:28:36Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"message":"tag: record both of their milestones, not only the one still to come\n\nChasing a report that the medibank button still does not show with\ngtm-tag 1.4.0 reporting built=lpTag site=3178090 and their taglet framework\nvisibly running. Not confirmed as the cause, but it is a real divergence from\nthe snippet this stands in for, found by comparing the two:\n\nTheirs is called from a container tag and registers both listeners, so it\nrecords _timing.contReady and _timing.domReady on every page. This runs one\ntask after the document parsed, and on a slow page that can be after load as\nwell - and a load listener registered then never fires, leaving\n_timing.domReady unset where theirs would have had it. Their framework reads\nthat object.\n\nSo the milestone is taken from readyState where the event has already gone,\nrather than waited for. contReady was already handled that way; domReady was\nnot, which is the asymmetry that made it easy to miss.\n\nThe DOM_READY trigger itself was never at risk - _domReady guards on isDom\nand fires it once - so this is about the timing object their taglets read.\n\n17 tests, 16 mutations.","tree":{"sha":"c7ce7e153871b6ee66096e80ad35229546e738fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/trees/c7ce7e153871b6ee66096e80ad35229546e738fa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/commits/503362cce40bb61caa625841c71e9c66e626eef7","verification":{"payload":"tree c7ce7e153871b6ee66096e80ad35229546e738fa\nparent 89b65102c0643dc48e760788f14a85e3e8a96dc8\nauthor Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791023316 +1300\ncommitter Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791023316 +1300\n\ntag: record both of their milestones, not only the one still to come\n\nChasing a report that the medibank button still does not show with\ngtm-tag 1.4.0 reporting built=lpTag site=3178090 and their taglet framework\nvisibly running. Not confirmed as the cause, but it is a real divergence from\nthe snippet this stands in for, found by comparing the two:\n\nTheirs is called from a container tag and registers both listeners, so it\nrecords _timing.contReady and _timing.domReady on every page. This runs one\ntask after the document parsed, and on a slow page that can be after load as\nwell - and a load listener registered then never fires, leaving\n_timing.domReady unset where theirs would have had it. Their framework reads\nthat object.\n\nSo the milestone is taken from readyState where the event has already gone,\nrather than waited for. contReady was already handled that way; domReady was\nnot, which is the asymmetry that made it easy to miss.\n\nThe DOM_READY trigger itself was never at risk - _domReady guards on isDom\nand fires it once - so this is about the timing object their taglets read.\n\n17 tests, 16 mutations.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPCSVWMUDHjp4kSP8mCo6DMbbZd\nwVKwk1D89AEPXKgVYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQEUKI7V8/wKc1FAXtK4iiuCrSYPsiihEXeg1QLg7S9pJUHPPhgFlhOmrQ70R0OySGZ\n9i3Y3l1ouoBz9kF0LezQM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T10:28:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/503362cce40bb61caa625841c71e9c66e626eef7","node_id":"C_kwDOU4p2ytoAKDUwMzM2MmNjZTQwYmI2MWNhYTYyNTg0MWM3MWU5YzY2ZTYyNmVlZjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/89b65102c0643dc48e760788f14a85e3e8a96dc8","sha":"89b65102c0643dc48e760788f14a85e3e8a96dc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/89b65102c0643dc48e760788f14a85e3e8a96dc8"}],"sha":"503362cce40bb61caa625841c71e9c66e626eef7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/503362cce40bb61caa625841c71e9c66e626eef7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/89b65102c0643dc48e760788f14a85e3e8a96dc8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T10:21:43Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T10:21:43Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"message":"v1.11.0: cut the release the install URL points at\n\nReported as \"the medibank filter isn''t working\", and the filter was right.\nThe documented install is pinned - v1.10.0 - and that tag serves gtm-tag\n1.3.0, which has no LivePerson support in it at all, so the line appended\nnothing and said nothing. Three resource bumps went to main today with no\nrelease behind them: gtm 1.5.0 -> 1.6.0 (stub=) and tag 1.3.0 -> 1.4.0\n(the lpTag builder, then the refusal).\n\nSo: v1.11.0, carrying googletagmanager_gtm 1.6.0 and gtm-tag 1.4.0.\n\nAnd a check so it cannot happen again. There was already one that the pinned\nURL resolves, added after v1.1.2 and v1.1.4 were pinned and never tagged -\nbut a tag that exists is not a tag that is current, and v1.10.0 resolved\nperfectly while serving code three commits old. The new one compares the\nresource VERSION in each dist file against what the pinned ref actually\nserves, and fails when they differ:\n\n  STALE gtm-tag.js: v1.10.0 serves 1.3.0, this commit builds 1.4.0\n\nWhich means a resource bump now has to come with its release. That is the\nright amount of friction: a bump nobody can fetch is a bump that did not\nhappen, and the only sign of it was someone else''s filter not working.","tree":{"sha":"a6ab28f4a54981fb0545abbbf3f90e3358364e04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/trees/a6ab28f4a54981fb0545abbbf3f90e3358364e04"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/commits/89b65102c0643dc48e760788f14a85e3e8a96dc8","verification":{"payload":"tree a6ab28f4a54981fb0545abbbf3f90e3358364e04\nparent a654374fc7db5539974b6de8cdb2e23e35d73e05\nauthor Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791022903 +1300\ncommitter Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791022903 +1300\n\nv1.11.0: cut the release the install URL points at\n\nReported as \"the medibank filter isn''t working\", and the filter was right.\nThe documented install is pinned - v1.10.0 - and that tag serves gtm-tag\n1.3.0, which has no LivePerson support in it at all, so the line appended\nnothing and said nothing. Three resource bumps went to main today with no\nrelease behind them: gtm 1.5.0 -> 1.6.0 (stub=) and tag 1.3.0 -> 1.4.0\n(the lpTag builder, then the refusal).\n\nSo: v1.11.0, carrying googletagmanager_gtm 1.6.0 and gtm-tag 1.4.0.\n\nAnd a check so it cannot happen again. There was already one that the pinned\nURL resolves, added after v1.1.2 and v1.1.4 were pinned and never tagged -\nbut a tag that exists is not a tag that is current, and v1.10.0 resolved\nperfectly while serving code three commits old. The new one compares the\nresource VERSION in each dist file against what the pinned ref actually\nserves, and fails when they differ:\n\n  STALE gtm-tag.js: v1.10.0 serves 1.3.0, this commit builds 1.4.0\n\nWhich means a resource bump now has to come with its release. That is the\nright amount of friction: a bump nobody can fetch is a bump that did not\nhappen, and the only sign of it was someone else''s filter not working.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPCSVWMUDHjp4kSP8mCo6DMbbZd\nwVKwk1D89AEPXKgVYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQGT49GRFHMG+l6Q36tj8yJ3e59oGHklAjHvhW2aMIgHe3nXmxPyt5JsMOJesRuaUWB\nMs4dTZaVyUu0IOaFBtLwc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T10:21:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/89b65102c0643dc48e760788f14a85e3e8a96dc8","node_id":"C_kwDOU4p2ytoAKDg5YjY1MTAyYzA2NDNkYzQ4ZTc2MDc4OGYxNGE4NWUzZThhOTZkYzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/a654374fc7db5539974b6de8cdb2e23e35d73e05","sha":"a654374fc7db5539974b6de8cdb2e23e35d73e05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/a654374fc7db5539974b6de8cdb2e23e35d73e05"}],"sha":"89b65102c0643dc48e760788f14a85e3e8a96dc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/89b65102c0643dc48e760788f14a85e3e8a96dc8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/a654374fc7db5539974b6de8cdb2e23e35d73e05/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T10:16:16Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T10:16:16Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"message":"docs: when the redirect can do it alone, and when it cannot\n\nThe question asked on every site in here: can the two redirect rules carry\nthis with nothing site-specific added? It has one test, and the table says\nwhat it is - where the missing piece can be read from.\n\nA consent category set is a constant, a wait''s name is in the page''s own\naddEventListener, and a container''s template code is still in the page, so\nthose three need no filter and should not have one. A tag''s url, a tenant id,\nthe name of a global an app polls and a vendor account id were only ever in\nthe container or the app''s own bundle, so those need a +js() line - and\nredirect= has no syntax for carrying a value, whichever resource hosts the\nfix.\n\nAlso says the part that is easy to miss: the per-site cases need the resource\ninstalled, so they do not reach uBO Lite, where an exception on the container\nis still the answer.","tree":{"sha":"178568fa224126b522da438a2c49bb585c804046","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/trees/178568fa224126b522da438a2c49bb585c804046"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/commits/a654374fc7db5539974b6de8cdb2e23e35d73e05","verification":{"payload":"tree 178568fa224126b522da438a2c49bb585c804046\nparent b048dcc4be7841c46a17619193b0acd1f6dd03ac\nauthor Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791022576 +1300\ncommitter Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791022576 +1300\n\ndocs: when the redirect can do it alone, and when it cannot\n\nThe question asked on every site in here: can the two redirect rules carry\nthis with nothing site-specific added? It has one test, and the table says\nwhat it is - where the missing piece can be read from.\n\nA consent category set is a constant, a wait''s name is in the page''s own\naddEventListener, and a container''s template code is still in the page, so\nthose three need no filter and should not have one. A tag''s url, a tenant id,\nthe name of a global an app polls and a vendor account id were only ever in\nthe container or the app''s own bundle, so those need a +js() line - and\nredirect= has no syntax for carrying a value, whichever resource hosts the\nfix.\n\nAlso says the part that is easy to miss: the per-site cases need the resource\ninstalled, so they do not reach uBO Lite, where an exception on the container\nis still the answer.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPCSVWMUDHjp4kSP8mCo6DMbbZd\nwVKwk1D89AEPXKgVYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQI2VHtOpXsTPkhdN7bXpsQ41cl1c5ZiPH0plGdKfus5VKzH9Lm/BlWxIrgoWlUc9bJ\n7joX+fn7DJuZAnkFm+Gw0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T10:16:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/a654374fc7db5539974b6de8cdb2e23e35d73e05","node_id":"C_kwDOU4p2ytoAKGE2NTQzNzRmYzdkYjU1Mzk5NzRiNmRlOGNkYjJlMjNlMzVkNzNlMDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/b048dcc4be7841c46a17619193b0acd1f6dd03ac","sha":"b048dcc4be7841c46a17619193b0acd1f6dd03ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/b048dcc4be7841c46a17619193b0acd1f6dd03ac"}],"sha":"a654374fc7db5539974b6de8cdb2e23e35d73e05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/a654374fc7db5539974b6de8cdb2e23e35d73e05"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/b048dcc4be7841c46a17619193b0acd1f6dd03ac/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T10:15:06Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T10:15:06Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"message":"tag: refuse their tag url with no account rather than append it bare\n\nThe shorter line a filter author reaches for first,\n\n  www.medibank.com.au##+js(gtm-tag, https://lptag.liveperson.net/tag/tag.js)\n\ndoes not work, and measured on their page it fails in the worst way it could:\n\n  LivePerson elements: 0    \"Message us\": false\n  window.lpTag: object      site: null    tag version: 4.1.18\n\nwindow.lpTag is an object because tag.js opens with\nwindow.lpTag = window.lpTag || {} before it throws on the rest, so \"is lpTag\nthere?\" answers yes, the tag reports a version, a request goes out, and the\nbutton is still gone. On top of that this printed injected=<url>, a success\nline for a line that cannot work.\n\nSo a url on their host and path with no account anywhere is refused, with the\nmissing thing named, and nothing is appended - no half-built lpTag left behind\nto mislead whoever looks next:\n\n  [gtm-rr] gtm-tag 1.4.0 refused=site url=https://lptag.liveperson.net/tag/tag.js\n\nAnd the one case where that shorter line is right is now read: a page that\nsets lpTag.site itself, which is the other documented way for the account to\narrive. That value is checked like any other, because it ends up in a script\nsrc - a mutation caught that, since every test until then seeded a valid id.\n\n16 tests, 15 mutations, all caught.","tree":{"sha":"ca7e179239e0d13d1beb47f64d15111e65e6b6ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/trees/ca7e179239e0d13d1beb47f64d15111e65e6b6ef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/commits/b048dcc4be7841c46a17619193b0acd1f6dd03ac","verification":{"payload":"tree ca7e179239e0d13d1beb47f64d15111e65e6b6ef\nparent 741e3ded4a2626fd37f6e04ce2ec74264a052301\nauthor Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791022506 +1300\ncommitter Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791022506 +1300\n\ntag: refuse their tag url with no account rather than append it bare\n\nThe shorter line a filter author reaches for first,\n\n  www.medibank.com.au##+js(gtm-tag, https://lptag.liveperson.net/tag/tag.js)\n\ndoes not work, and measured on their page it fails in the worst way it could:\n\n  LivePerson elements: 0    \"Message us\": false\n  window.lpTag: object      site: null    tag version: 4.1.18\n\nwindow.lpTag is an object because tag.js opens with\nwindow.lpTag = window.lpTag || {} before it throws on the rest, so \"is lpTag\nthere?\" answers yes, the tag reports a version, a request goes out, and the\nbutton is still gone. On top of that this printed injected=<url>, a success\nline for a line that cannot work.\n\nSo a url on their host and path with no account anywhere is refused, with the\nmissing thing named, and nothing is appended - no half-built lpTag left behind\nto mislead whoever looks next:\n\n  [gtm-rr] gtm-tag 1.4.0 refused=site url=https://lptag.liveperson.net/tag/tag.js\n\nAnd the one case where that shorter line is right is now read: a page that\nsets lpTag.site itself, which is the other documented way for the account to\narrive. That value is checked like any other, because it ends up in a script\nsrc - a mutation caught that, since every test until then seeded a valid id.\n\n16 tests, 15 mutations, all caught.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPCSVWMUDHjp4kSP8mCo6DMbbZd\nwVKwk1D89AEPXKgVYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQA/AtK8CCPGPiSzwfIcpOKoxmw635+faxK0Vm9RvUDks+nCDeYs554lPMgvQwDMYAt\nVtNbB72Mli9SBC+YcXKww=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T10:15:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/b048dcc4be7841c46a17619193b0acd1f6dd03ac","node_id":"C_kwDOU4p2ytoAKGIwNDhkY2M0YmU3ODQxYzQ2YTE3NjE5MTkzYjBhY2QxZjZkZDAzYWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/741e3ded4a2626fd37f6e04ce2ec74264a052301","sha":"741e3ded4a2626fd37f6e04ce2ec74264a052301","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/741e3ded4a2626fd37f6e04ce2ec74264a052301"}],"sha":"b048dcc4be7841c46a17619193b0acd1f6dd03ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/b048dcc4be7841c46a17619193b0acd1f6dd03ac"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/741e3ded4a2626fd37f6e04ce2ec74264a052301/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T10:02:23Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T10:02:23Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"message":"tag 1.4.0: build the object a loader reads its account off\n\nuAssets #33693. medibank.com.au''s \"Message us\" button is gone, and it is a\nLivePerson engagement - an LPMcontainer holding their own\nmessage-us-button.svg. The only copy of the snippet that starts it is a\nCustom HTML tag in GTM-TS6X5PB, with the account behind a container macro.\nWhere that snippet used to sit inline the page has a bare\n\"<!--Live person and standard tag -->\", and not one of their twenty\nclientlibs mentions lpTag, so nothing is left in the page to wait for.\n\nNaming the script is not enough, which is the part worth writing down\nbecause it looks like it should be. Their tag.js opens with\n\n  window.lpTag = window.lpTag || {}\n\nand that reads as self-starting. It is not: the account comes from\n\"site = a.site || b.site\" off objects the snippet was expected to have built,\nand b.defer(...) is the next thing it touches. Appended alone it throws\n\"TypeError: b.defer is not a function\" with lpTag.site null. What is missing\nis not a url, it is the object - an account id, three queueing functions, a\nloader for their taglets, and seven arrays those push into.\n\nSo gtm-tag builds it, keyed on that host and path, with the account read out\nof the url''s own site= parameter:\n\n  www.medibank.com.au##+js(gtm-tag, https://lptag.liveperson.net/tag/tag.js?site=3178090)\n  www.medibankoshc.com.au##+js(gtm-tag, https://lptag.liveperson.net/tag/tag.js?site=3178090)\n\nNo extra argument, and an ordinary gtm-tag line. The first draft of this was\na fifth resource; folding it in cost nothing and removed a name from the\ninstall.\n\nThat object is published boilerplate, the same on every LivePerson site but\nfor the id, and it is rebuilt here rather than copied. It unblocks nothing:\nlptag.liveperson.net is on no default list, the rule that would is in\nFanboy''s Social/Chat addon, and where that is on the append does not load.\nwindow._lptStop is honoured, and a page where the real snippet already ran is\nleft alone with kept=theirs, as their own snippet leaves a second copy.\n\nMeasured in Chrome against the live page with gtm.js still replaced: the\nbutton is back, lpTag.site is 3178090, their tag 4.1.18 runs, and the request\nset matches what allowing the container produces. The exceptions this\nreplaces let that whole container back in, a Facebook pixel among the rest.\n\n14 tests, 12 mutations. Two bugs came out of those tests rather than review:\nit waited for DOMContentLoaded where it needed a head, and appended to\nnothing while printing its success line; and it dropped lpTag.sdes and vars\nwhere a page had seeded them, which their snippet preserves.","tree":{"sha":"0d332532100b0ea5234cbf86ac681552021753b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/trees/0d332532100b0ea5234cbf86ac681552021753b4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/commits/741e3ded4a2626fd37f6e04ce2ec74264a052301","verification":{"payload":"tree 0d332532100b0ea5234cbf86ac681552021753b4\nparent 879003679072934203e4e7b35b94442b2856731e\nauthor Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791021743 +1300\ncommitter Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791021743 +1300\n\ntag 1.4.0: build the object a loader reads its account off\n\nuAssets #33693. medibank.com.au''s \"Message us\" button is gone, and it is a\nLivePerson engagement - an LPMcontainer holding their own\nmessage-us-button.svg. The only copy of the snippet that starts it is a\nCustom HTML tag in GTM-TS6X5PB, with the account behind a container macro.\nWhere that snippet used to sit inline the page has a bare\n\"<!--Live person and standard tag -->\", and not one of their twenty\nclientlibs mentions lpTag, so nothing is left in the page to wait for.\n\nNaming the script is not enough, which is the part worth writing down\nbecause it looks like it should be. Their tag.js opens with\n\n  window.lpTag = window.lpTag || {}\n\nand that reads as self-starting. It is not: the account comes from\n\"site = a.site || b.site\" off objects the snippet was expected to have built,\nand b.defer(...) is the next thing it touches. Appended alone it throws\n\"TypeError: b.defer is not a function\" with lpTag.site null. What is missing\nis not a url, it is the object - an account id, three queueing functions, a\nloader for their taglets, and seven arrays those push into.\n\nSo gtm-tag builds it, keyed on that host and path, with the account read out\nof the url''s own site= parameter:\n\n  www.medibank.com.au##+js(gtm-tag, https://lptag.liveperson.net/tag/tag.js?site=3178090)\n  www.medibankoshc.com.au##+js(gtm-tag, https://lptag.liveperson.net/tag/tag.js?site=3178090)\n\nNo extra argument, and an ordinary gtm-tag line. The first draft of this was\na fifth resource; folding it in cost nothing and removed a name from the\ninstall.\n\nThat object is published boilerplate, the same on every LivePerson site but\nfor the id, and it is rebuilt here rather than copied. It unblocks nothing:\nlptag.liveperson.net is on no default list, the rule that would is in\nFanboy''s Social/Chat addon, and where that is on the append does not load.\nwindow._lptStop is honoured, and a page where the real snippet already ran is\nleft alone with kept=theirs, as their own snippet leaves a second copy.\n\nMeasured in Chrome against the live page with gtm.js still replaced: the\nbutton is back, lpTag.site is 3178090, their tag 4.1.18 runs, and the request\nset matches what allowing the container produces. The exceptions this\nreplaces let that whole container back in, a Facebook pixel among the rest.\n\n14 tests, 12 mutations. Two bugs came out of those tests rather than review:\nit waited for DOMContentLoaded where it needed a head, and appended to\nnothing while printing its success line; and it dropped lpTag.sdes and vars\nwhere a page had seeded them, which their snippet preserves.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPCSVWMUDHjp4kSP8mCo6DMbbZd\nwVKwk1D89AEPXKgVYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQKnOwdu/RbyyeF3FPKkV0YSchQ0gQ6W+mbwS+y4EhxhlAiTQArVbuSExBHfL/reiPv\nFu9C8vVngpZEd4OSPn6wk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T10:02:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/741e3ded4a2626fd37f6e04ce2ec74264a052301","node_id":"C_kwDOU4p2ytoAKDc0MWUzZGVkNGEyNjI2ZmQzN2Y2ZTA0Y2UyZWM3NDI2NGEwNTIzMDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/879003679072934203e4e7b35b94442b2856731e","sha":"879003679072934203e4e7b35b94442b2856731e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/879003679072934203e4e7b35b94442b2856731e"}],"sha":"741e3ded4a2626fd37f6e04ce2ec74264a052301","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/741e3ded4a2626fd37f6e04ce2ec74264a052301"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/879003679072934203e4e7b35b94442b2856731e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T09:11:58Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T09:11:58Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"message":"docs: fill hokkaido-np.co.jp''s slider instead of hiding it\n\nThe note here said the spinner goes and the slider stays empty, and offered a\ncosmetic rule for the gap. There is a better answer: the vendor chain is\nstartable, and one gtm-tag line starts all of it.\n\n  www.hokkaido-np.co.jp##+js(gtm-tag, https://cdn.activity.smart-bdash.com/tag-manager/bd-7verxz/btm.js)\n\nbtm.js is the single script GTM-MZB2Z66 injects. It loads ai_recommend.js,\nwhich waits for window.edirium_rec from *.rec.edirium.co.jp, asks b-dash for\nits campaigns, and evals the render callback those carry - and that callback\nis what builds the slides and dispatches aiRecommendGenerated. It is not in\nany script, so nothing here could have stood in for it; naming the head of\nthe chain is what reaches it.\n\nMeasured in Chrome against the live page, gtm.js replaced by this resource\nand EasyPrivacy left on: without the line #ai_recommend_section has no\nchildren and the spinner is display:flex; with it, three article slides and\nthe spinner removed by their own callback, with btm.js and each step\nrequested exactly once. ||smart-bdash.com/tracking-script/ keeps bdash_log.js\nout throughout, so the recommendations come back without b-dash''s logging -\nthe rest of that chain is on no list.\n\nOne measurement artefact worth not repeating: injecting the scriptlet into\nevery frame made btm.js look like it was being requested 165 times. That was\nthe page''s ad iframes each running it, not a loop.","tree":{"sha":"76db7006590ed3331a3084055a18f2ea14a809b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/trees/76db7006590ed3331a3084055a18f2ea14a809b4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/commits/879003679072934203e4e7b35b94442b2856731e","verification":{"payload":"tree 76db7006590ed3331a3084055a18f2ea14a809b4\nparent 898b63bda70af935c767d4cb4ab2cc67971937db\nauthor Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791018718 +1300\ncommitter Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791018718 +1300\n\ndocs: fill hokkaido-np.co.jp''s slider instead of hiding it\n\nThe note here said the spinner goes and the slider stays empty, and offered a\ncosmetic rule for the gap. There is a better answer: the vendor chain is\nstartable, and one gtm-tag line starts all of it.\n\n  www.hokkaido-np.co.jp##+js(gtm-tag, https://cdn.activity.smart-bdash.com/tag-manager/bd-7verxz/btm.js)\n\nbtm.js is the single script GTM-MZB2Z66 injects. It loads ai_recommend.js,\nwhich waits for window.edirium_rec from *.rec.edirium.co.jp, asks b-dash for\nits campaigns, and evals the render callback those carry - and that callback\nis what builds the slides and dispatches aiRecommendGenerated. It is not in\nany script, so nothing here could have stood in for it; naming the head of\nthe chain is what reaches it.\n\nMeasured in Chrome against the live page, gtm.js replaced by this resource\nand EasyPrivacy left on: without the line #ai_recommend_section has no\nchildren and the spinner is display:flex; with it, three article slides and\nthe spinner removed by their own callback, with btm.js and each step\nrequested exactly once. ||smart-bdash.com/tracking-script/ keeps bdash_log.js\nout throughout, so the recommendations come back without b-dash''s logging -\nthe rest of that chain is on no list.\n\nOne measurement artefact worth not repeating: injecting the scriptlet into\nevery frame made btm.js look like it was being requested 165 times. That was\nthe page''s ad iframes each running it, not a loop.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPCSVWMUDHjp4kSP8mCo6DMbbZd\nwVKwk1D89AEPXKgVYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQNy4bInfkg2a5w4+9GHhabFBfKrXsVbp5Blr5hFQWF3dHfNJh5Jo3Uuwn7ph078gmK\nx+0F372bwzJB4q2QvUTAk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T09:12:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/879003679072934203e4e7b35b94442b2856731e","node_id":"C_kwDOU4p2ytoAKDg3OTAwMzY3OTA3MjkzNDIwM2U0ZTdiMzViOTQ0NDJiMjg1NjczMWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/898b63bda70af935c767d4cb4ab2cc67971937db","sha":"898b63bda70af935c767d4cb4ab2cc67971937db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/898b63bda70af935c767d4cb4ab2cc67971937db"}],"sha":"879003679072934203e4e7b35b94442b2856731e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/879003679072934203e4e7b35b94442b2856731e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/898b63bda70af935c767d4cb4ab2cc67971937db/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T08:08:47Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T08:08:47Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"message":"gtm 1.6.0: answer the global a page polls for with no timeout\n\nuAssets #32369. b2c.voegol.com.br''s sign-in screen never redirects to its\nidentity provider with the container replaced, and says nothing about why:\n\n    ngAfterViewInit() {\n        this.waitForWindowProp(''amplitude'').subscribe(a => {\n            this.goToLoginSmiles(this.culture, {\n                deviceId: a.getDeviceId(), sessionId: a.getSessionId() }); }); }\n    waitForWindowProp(name, every = 1200) {\n        return timer(0, every).pipe(\n            map(() => window[name]), filter(v => !!v), take(1)); }\n\nwindow.amplitude is what their Amplitude tag''s injected wrapper creates, so\nthe poll runs every 1.2 seconds for ever. It also explains why an exception\nfor cdn.amplitude.com did nothing on its own: the container is what requests\nthat script.\n\nstub= puts up the shape rather than a vendor - a function that answers to any\nproperty with itself and returns undefined however it is called:\n\n    b2c.voegol.com.br##+js(googletagmanager_gtm, stub=amplitude)\n\nundefined and not a plausible id, because the page sends what it reads\nstraight on into a URL bound for someone else, and minting a tracking id\nthere is the line gtag(''get'', ...) already refuses to cross. Falsy leaves the\nparameter out and the sign-in carries on without it. A global already there is\nleft alone, and a real SDK arriving later replaces the stub.\n\nThe name has to come from the filter: a container is JSON this resource never\nfetches - it is served instead of it - so there is nothing at runtime to read\na vendor''s global off, and a read of an absent property is not observable.\n\nAGENTS.md said an exception was the honest answer here. It was wrong, and the\ncorrection is in it: two failed shortcuts were evidence the gate had not been\nfound, not evidence there was none. The gate was in the third bundle the route\nloads, a module-federation remote that had not been read.\n\n13 tests, 7 mutations. Two of the tests found real bugs before they shipped: a\ncall returning the stub put a function where a device id goes, and a stub\nanswering for ''then'' made itself a thenable - a second wait with no end.","tree":{"sha":"37fdd997a3a2c0cbb2c29e5af79c74fff17eb988","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/trees/37fdd997a3a2c0cbb2c29e5af79c74fff17eb988"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/commits/898b63bda70af935c767d4cb4ab2cc67971937db","verification":{"payload":"tree 37fdd997a3a2c0cbb2c29e5af79c74fff17eb988\nparent 43e4c85a56e8a0d982643bd82defd3b9dbc76175\nauthor Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791014927 +1300\ncommitter Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791014927 +1300\n\ngtm 1.6.0: answer the global a page polls for with no timeout\n\nuAssets #32369. b2c.voegol.com.br''s sign-in screen never redirects to its\nidentity provider with the container replaced, and says nothing about why:\n\n    ngAfterViewInit() {\n        this.waitForWindowProp(''amplitude'').subscribe(a => {\n            this.goToLoginSmiles(this.culture, {\n                deviceId: a.getDeviceId(), sessionId: a.getSessionId() }); }); }\n    waitForWindowProp(name, every = 1200) {\n        return timer(0, every).pipe(\n            map(() => window[name]), filter(v => !!v), take(1)); }\n\nwindow.amplitude is what their Amplitude tag''s injected wrapper creates, so\nthe poll runs every 1.2 seconds for ever. It also explains why an exception\nfor cdn.amplitude.com did nothing on its own: the container is what requests\nthat script.\n\nstub= puts up the shape rather than a vendor - a function that answers to any\nproperty with itself and returns undefined however it is called:\n\n    b2c.voegol.com.br##+js(googletagmanager_gtm, stub=amplitude)\n\nundefined and not a plausible id, because the page sends what it reads\nstraight on into a URL bound for someone else, and minting a tracking id\nthere is the line gtag(''get'', ...) already refuses to cross. Falsy leaves the\nparameter out and the sign-in carries on without it. A global already there is\nleft alone, and a real SDK arriving later replaces the stub.\n\nThe name has to come from the filter: a container is JSON this resource never\nfetches - it is served instead of it - so there is nothing at runtime to read\na vendor''s global off, and a read of an absent property is not observable.\n\nAGENTS.md said an exception was the honest answer here. It was wrong, and the\ncorrection is in it: two failed shortcuts were evidence the gate had not been\nfound, not evidence there was none. The gate was in the third bundle the route\nloads, a module-federation remote that had not been read.\n\n13 tests, 7 mutations. Two of the tests found real bugs before they shipped: a\ncall returning the stub put a function where a device id goes, and a stub\nanswering for ''then'' made itself a thenable - a second wait with no end.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPCSVWMUDHjp4kSP8mCo6DMbbZd\nwVKwk1D89AEPXKgVYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQJk2SH/F1n9QUTM+7n51EE2p9vBpU7xhD/dmQ6QnNqYjoCSnZ4ktIZyS7zfVX3Y98L\nuDVJjSDXQoqIQkCewpdgw=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T08:08:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/898b63bda70af935c767d4cb4ab2cc67971937db","node_id":"C_kwDOU4p2ytoAKDg5OGI2M2JkYTcwYWY5MzVjNzY3ZDRjYjRhYjJjYzY3OTcxOTM3ZGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/43e4c85a56e8a0d982643bd82defd3b9dbc76175","sha":"43e4c85a56e8a0d982643bd82defd3b9dbc76175","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/43e4c85a56e8a0d982643bd82defd3b9dbc76175"}],"sha":"898b63bda70af935c767d4cb4ab2cc67971937db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/898b63bda70af935c767d4cb4ab2cc67971937db"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/43e4c85a56e8a0d982643bd82defd3b9dbc76175/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T07:43:04Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T07:43:04Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"message":"docs: the third shape, where an exception is the honest answer\n\nTwo shapes this resource answers, and one it does not.\n\n  loader        petzl.com: the container injects Maps and OneTrust\n                -> gtm-tag with the url\n  writer        shonenjumpplus.com: the container writes carousel HTML\n                -> answerable where the page kept the same code in a\n                   template, which it had\n  orchestrator  b2c.voegol.com.br: the container takes a device id from\n                one injected script, feature flags from another through\n                container code holding the vendor''s deployment key in a\n                container variable, caches them to\n                localStorage.mapStorageExp and pushes an event the app\n                waits on before it will navigate\n                -> no\n\nTwo shortcuts were tried on the third and both failed, which is the part\nworth writing down: stubbing the client''s global, where theirs is named\nfeatureExperiment rather than the vendor''s experiment; and seeding the\ncache by hand so the wait completes - the readiness gate was satisfied,\nno timeout warning, and the page still did not navigate, because\nsomething downstream reads the flag VALUES. A resource can answer a\ncontract. It cannot produce a vendor''s data, and inventing a variant\npicks a side of someone''s A/B test for them.\n\nuAssets #32369 is that case, and its two exceptions are right. The second\nof them cannot work alone by construction: nothing requests\ncdn.amplitude.com/libs/ unless the container runs.\n\nAlso checked, and not the cause: the only location.href assignment in\nall 1032KB of that container is GTM''s own link-click tracking, and the\nsite''s Adobe Launch stays blocked while the redirect works.","tree":{"sha":"21f643dd937b4318e4524c397a23be9855217657","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/trees/21f643dd937b4318e4524c397a23be9855217657"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/commits/43e4c85a56e8a0d982643bd82defd3b9dbc76175","verification":{"payload":"tree 21f643dd937b4318e4524c397a23be9855217657\nparent a4291c85782939492df0fa4e12bbdbbf305aeebb\nauthor Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791013384 +1300\ncommitter Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791013384 +1300\n\ndocs: the third shape, where an exception is the honest answer\n\nTwo shapes this resource answers, and one it does not.\n\n  loader        petzl.com: the container injects Maps and OneTrust\n                -> gtm-tag with the url\n  writer        shonenjumpplus.com: the container writes carousel HTML\n                -> answerable where the page kept the same code in a\n                   template, which it had\n  orchestrator  b2c.voegol.com.br: the container takes a device id from\n                one injected script, feature flags from another through\n                container code holding the vendor''s deployment key in a\n                container variable, caches them to\n                localStorage.mapStorageExp and pushes an event the app\n                waits on before it will navigate\n                -> no\n\nTwo shortcuts were tried on the third and both failed, which is the part\nworth writing down: stubbing the client''s global, where theirs is named\nfeatureExperiment rather than the vendor''s experiment; and seeding the\ncache by hand so the wait completes - the readiness gate was satisfied,\nno timeout warning, and the page still did not navigate, because\nsomething downstream reads the flag VALUES. A resource can answer a\ncontract. It cannot produce a vendor''s data, and inventing a variant\npicks a side of someone''s A/B test for them.\n\nuAssets #32369 is that case, and its two exceptions are right. The second\nof them cannot work alone by construction: nothing requests\ncdn.amplitude.com/libs/ unless the container runs.\n\nAlso checked, and not the cause: the only location.href assignment in\nall 1032KB of that container is GTM''s own link-click tracking, and the\nsite''s Adobe Launch stays blocked while the redirect works.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPCSVWMUDHjp4kSP8mCo6DMbbZd\nwVKwk1D89AEPXKgVYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQF1YDkcOOM3AruHV/+DppLuKbMYT+JR6zSZFQYUMWPEbgxzHWkYZgFc+A8h1N03rV1\ncdH7kWEAusSemH2kot6wQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T07:43:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/43e4c85a56e8a0d982643bd82defd3b9dbc76175","node_id":"C_kwDOU4p2ytoAKDQzZTRjODVhNTZlOGEwZDk4MjY0M2JkODJkZWZkM2I5ZGJjNzYxNzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/a4291c85782939492df0fa4e12bbdbbf305aeebb","sha":"a4291c85782939492df0fa4e12bbdbbf305aeebb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/a4291c85782939492df0fa4e12bbdbbf305aeebb"}],"sha":"43e4c85a56e8a0d982643bd82defd3b9dbc76175","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/43e4c85a56e8a0d982643bd82defd3b9dbc76175"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/a4291c85782939492df0fa4e12bbdbbf305aeebb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T06:42:54Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T06:42:54Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"message":"gtm 1.5.0: give back the consent state the container took with it\n\nA container loads the site''s consent manager, and a page reads that\nmanager''s state to decide whether to show its own content.\nglobalblue.com/es/refund-points-map:\n\n  checkOptanonActiveGroups() {\n      const i = window.OptanonActiveGroups ?? '''';\n      return i.includes(''C0001'') && i.includes(''C0002'') && i.includes(''C0003'') }\n  openOTYTNotification() { window.OneTrust?.ToggleInfoDisplay() }\n\nReplacing the loader takes the manager with it, so that variable is never\nset, the map never renders, and the reopen button optional-chains into\nnothing. Blocking gtm.js did that, which makes it this resource''s to\nanswer: a visitor who installed only this one has nothing else to reach\nfor, and telling them to install another repo is not an answer.\n\nWhere this stood in for the container and nothing else has spoken, it\npublishes the categories a page needs to show its own content -\nC0001,C0002,C0003, necessary, performance and functional - and NOT C0004\nor C0005, targeting and social, which is what an ad is gated on. With it:\na minimal OneTrust whose UI methods are no-ops so a reopen button is not\ndead, the page''s own OptanonWrapper() if it defined one, and\nOneTrustGroupsUpdated, which is how a page re-checks - globalblue does\nfromEvent(window, ''OneTrustGroupsUpdated'') and runs change detection off\nit.\n\nNothing is transmitted. This is a variable a page reads; the requests\nthat follow are still the filter lists'' business. consent=all asks for\ntargeting too, consent=off asks for none - which is the right answer for\nanyone running consent-rr, where a stored and transmitted refusal sits\nbehind the page-side state.\n\nA filter''s argument arrives after this file''s own call, so off and all\nadjust what was put up rather than deciding it; the branches that tried\nto decide it were dead code, and the harness said so. It also found that\na state anything else had set was being half-overwritten, and that\nnothing proved the not-installed case - a page with no loader proves\nnothing, since nothing runs there. A container=kept page does.\n\nAnd the write-shim test from v1.8.0 was vacuous: it replaced\ndocument.write after the shim was in place, bypassing it, so the\npass-through check it existed for was removable. CI caught that; the stub\nnow stands in before the resource runs.","tree":{"sha":"c5209cf1c50dcab1f956376e2b40983db95bf2ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/trees/c5209cf1c50dcab1f956376e2b40983db95bf2ad"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/commits/a4291c85782939492df0fa4e12bbdbbf305aeebb","verification":{"payload":"tree c5209cf1c50dcab1f956376e2b40983db95bf2ad\nparent d20c1672afe8d7f3f963b5e5848a1a08f70ca437\nauthor Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791009774 +1300\ncommitter Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791009774 +1300\n\ngtm 1.5.0: give back the consent state the container took with it\n\nA container loads the site''s consent manager, and a page reads that\nmanager''s state to decide whether to show its own content.\nglobalblue.com/es/refund-points-map:\n\n  checkOptanonActiveGroups() {\n      const i = window.OptanonActiveGroups ?? '''';\n      return i.includes(''C0001'') && i.includes(''C0002'') && i.includes(''C0003'') }\n  openOTYTNotification() { window.OneTrust?.ToggleInfoDisplay() }\n\nReplacing the loader takes the manager with it, so that variable is never\nset, the map never renders, and the reopen button optional-chains into\nnothing. Blocking gtm.js did that, which makes it this resource''s to\nanswer: a visitor who installed only this one has nothing else to reach\nfor, and telling them to install another repo is not an answer.\n\nWhere this stood in for the container and nothing else has spoken, it\npublishes the categories a page needs to show its own content -\nC0001,C0002,C0003, necessary, performance and functional - and NOT C0004\nor C0005, targeting and social, which is what an ad is gated on. With it:\na minimal OneTrust whose UI methods are no-ops so a reopen button is not\ndead, the page''s own OptanonWrapper() if it defined one, and\nOneTrustGroupsUpdated, which is how a page re-checks - globalblue does\nfromEvent(window, ''OneTrustGroupsUpdated'') and runs change detection off\nit.\n\nNothing is transmitted. This is a variable a page reads; the requests\nthat follow are still the filter lists'' business. consent=all asks for\ntargeting too, consent=off asks for none - which is the right answer for\nanyone running consent-rr, where a stored and transmitted refusal sits\nbehind the page-side state.\n\nA filter''s argument arrives after this file''s own call, so off and all\nadjust what was put up rather than deciding it; the branches that tried\nto decide it were dead code, and the harness said so. It also found that\na state anything else had set was being half-overwritten, and that\nnothing proved the not-installed case - a page with no loader proves\nnothing, since nothing runs there. A container=kept page does.\n\nAnd the write-shim test from v1.8.0 was vacuous: it replaced\ndocument.write after the shim was in place, bypassing it, so the\npass-through check it existed for was removable. CI caught that; the stub\nnow stands in before the resource runs.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPCSVWMUDHjp4kSP8mCo6DMbbZd\nwVKwk1D89AEPXKgVYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQAItn4sBBiO8RkWtmBo6CfnUH3yqSTAcQORV+3LrGaVV5TC5PQt3D37Koa2eqZNo+k\nwAeRE8zOsCcyC1tu3d5AM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T06:42:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/a4291c85782939492df0fa4e12bbdbbf305aeebb","node_id":"C_kwDOU4p2ytoAKGE0MjkxYzg1NzgyOTM5NDkyZGYwZmE0ZTEyYmJkYmJmMzA1YWVlYmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/d20c1672afe8d7f3f963b5e5848a1a08f70ca437","sha":"d20c1672afe8d7f3f963b5e5848a1a08f70ca437","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/d20c1672afe8d7f3f963b5e5848a1a08f70ca437"}],"sha":"a4291c85782939492df0fa4e12bbdbbf305aeebb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/a4291c85782939492df0fa4e12bbdbbf305aeebb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/d20c1672afe8d7f3f963b5e5848a1a08f70ca437/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T06:31:54Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T06:31:54Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"message":"tag 1.3.0: carry the attributes a tag needs, named in any order\n\nA src alone does not reproduce every tag a container holds. OneTrust''s\nloader carries its tenant on the element -\n\n  <script src=\"https://cdn.cookielaw.org/scripttemplates/otSDKStub.js\"\n          data-domain-script=\"bb3af1ef-...\">\n\n- and that is the tag a site''s content is most often gated on: petzl.com\nand globalblue.com both keep their consent manager there, and\nglobalblue''s map is gated on OptanonActiveGroups holding C0001, C0002 and\nC0003, which only a consent manager sets. Without a way to set an\nattribute this could not stand in for either, so a gtm-rr user with no\nconsent-rr had nothing to reach for - which is a gtm-rr gap, not someone\nelse''s.\n\nattr:name=value, as many as wanted, set on the element and never on the\nurl, where a tenant id would land in a query string their loader does not\nread. Nothing vendor-specific ships: dist/ has no mention of cookielaw,\nonetrust or otSDKStub, only the comments in src/ that the build strips.\nThe arguments can be named too - url=, needs=, when= - because position\nis a poor way to ask for the fourth thing, and an empty position stays\nwhere it is.\n\nA mutation found its own redundancy here: the empty-argument guard\nsurvived, because these are assigned by index and an empty one moves\nnothing along. It is gone. The resource that collapsed positions instead\nis the one that put ''self'' where a selector goes.","tree":{"sha":"94858d4285f286a2096f98e04ccaf1c3a3291c5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/trees/94858d4285f286a2096f98e04ccaf1c3a3291c5c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/commits/d20c1672afe8d7f3f963b5e5848a1a08f70ca437","verification":{"payload":"tree 94858d4285f286a2096f98e04ccaf1c3a3291c5c\nparent 5f9c55cbdbd5a9302d7e09e2650df5f1dc574c40\nauthor Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791009114 +1300\ncommitter Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791009114 +1300\n\ntag 1.3.0: carry the attributes a tag needs, named in any order\n\nA src alone does not reproduce every tag a container holds. OneTrust''s\nloader carries its tenant on the element -\n\n  <script src=\"https://cdn.cookielaw.org/scripttemplates/otSDKStub.js\"\n          data-domain-script=\"bb3af1ef-...\">\n\n- and that is the tag a site''s content is most often gated on: petzl.com\nand globalblue.com both keep their consent manager there, and\nglobalblue''s map is gated on OptanonActiveGroups holding C0001, C0002 and\nC0003, which only a consent manager sets. Without a way to set an\nattribute this could not stand in for either, so a gtm-rr user with no\nconsent-rr had nothing to reach for - which is a gtm-rr gap, not someone\nelse''s.\n\nattr:name=value, as many as wanted, set on the element and never on the\nurl, where a tenant id would land in a query string their loader does not\nread. Nothing vendor-specific ships: dist/ has no mention of cookielaw,\nonetrust or otSDKStub, only the comments in src/ that the build strips.\nThe arguments can be named too - url=, needs=, when= - because position\nis a poor way to ask for the fourth thing, and an empty position stays\nwhere it is.\n\nA mutation found its own redundancy here: the empty-argument guard\nsurvived, because these are assigned by index and an empty one moves\nnothing along. It is gone. The resource that collapsed positions instead\nis the one that put ''self'' where a selector goes.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPCSVWMUDHjp4kSP8mCo6DMbbZd\nwVKwk1D89AEPXKgVYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQP4FusOpaT6BxyZC6R1W7akTrKiPdwGMmgiJdUmwMciedeGne47m01dbXIVZU0QTtf\nr/WzeqNt6sGbUykjyw5gs=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T06:31:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/d20c1672afe8d7f3f963b5e5848a1a08f70ca437","node_id":"C_kwDOU4p2ytoAKGQyMGMxNjcyYWZlOGQ3ZjNmOTYzYjVlNTg0OGExYTA4ZjcwY2E0Mzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/5f9c55cbdbd5a9302d7e09e2650df5f1dc574c40","sha":"5f9c55cbdbd5a9302d7e09e2650df5f1dc574c40","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/5f9c55cbdbd5a9302d7e09e2650df5f1dc574c40"}],"sha":"d20c1672afe8d7f3f963b5e5848a1a08f70ca437","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/d20c1672afe8d7f3f963b5e5848a1a08f70ca437"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/5f9c55cbdbd5a9302d7e09e2650df5f1dc574c40/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T06:08:16Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T06:08:16Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"message":"tag 1.2.0: catch what an injected script writes, as their postscribe does\n\nA tag whose script calls document.write. GTM has a path for it -\ninternal.injectHtml takes supportDocumentWrite, and tag 148 of\nhokkaido-np.co.jp''s container switches it on because b-dash''s btm.js\nwrites - and without it the write is simply lost: a script appended async\nruns after parsing, when document.write would replace the whole document,\nso browsers ignore it and the tag quietly does nothing.\n\nSo document.write and writeln are caught while that script runs, and what\nit wrote is put where the script sits. Only while it runs:\ndocument.currentScript says which script is executing, and a write by\nanything else goes to the real one untouched. The originals are given\nback on load or error.\n\nEach written script element is rebuilt rather than inserted, because one\nthat came out of innerHTML is marked already-started and never runs -\nthe same rebuild their own executor does for a text/gtmscript node - and\nwith async false, so they keep the order they were written in. One line\nwhen it happens: wrote=<n> from=<url>.\n\nFour tests play the browser''s half, since jsdom will not fetch and run an\nexternal script: currentScript while it runs, load when it is done. One\nof them needed its own document: the rest of that file uses\nrunScripts outside-only, where an inserted script never executes and the\nassertion would have passed for the wrong reason.","tree":{"sha":"e83ab6be5c267071c36ca284ba82c3824b18280e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/trees/e83ab6be5c267071c36ca284ba82c3824b18280e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/commits/5f9c55cbdbd5a9302d7e09e2650df5f1dc574c40","verification":{"payload":"tree e83ab6be5c267071c36ca284ba82c3824b18280e\nparent 73db4d113c504c867f089803408e6bb3a9d4bf41\nauthor Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791007696 +1300\ncommitter Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791007696 +1300\n\ntag 1.2.0: catch what an injected script writes, as their postscribe does\n\nA tag whose script calls document.write. GTM has a path for it -\ninternal.injectHtml takes supportDocumentWrite, and tag 148 of\nhokkaido-np.co.jp''s container switches it on because b-dash''s btm.js\nwrites - and without it the write is simply lost: a script appended async\nruns after parsing, when document.write would replace the whole document,\nso browsers ignore it and the tag quietly does nothing.\n\nSo document.write and writeln are caught while that script runs, and what\nit wrote is put where the script sits. Only while it runs:\ndocument.currentScript says which script is executing, and a write by\nanything else goes to the real one untouched. The originals are given\nback on load or error.\n\nEach written script element is rebuilt rather than inserted, because one\nthat came out of innerHTML is marked already-started and never runs -\nthe same rebuild their own executor does for a text/gtmscript node - and\nwith async false, so they keep the order they were written in. One line\nwhen it happens: wrote=<n> from=<url>.\n\nFour tests play the browser''s half, since jsdom will not fetch and run an\nexternal script: currentScript while it runs, load when it is done. One\nof them needed its own document: the rest of that file uses\nrunScripts outside-only, where an inserted script never executes and the\nassertion would have passed for the wrong reason.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPCSVWMUDHjp4kSP8mCo6DMbbZd\nwVKwk1D89AEPXKgVYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQIfAi47ztnV1LZoO2qQd9CJijzf0x1V078AqWoyxDVftMbpm9nxAltV4qIwBDxQtfb\n5Ex8XtLz6tHOzKhDmw0wQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T06:08:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/5f9c55cbdbd5a9302d7e09e2650df5f1dc574c40","node_id":"C_kwDOU4p2ytoAKDVmOWM1NWNiZGJkNWE5MzAyZDdlMDllMjY1MGRmNWYxZGM1NzRjNDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/73db4d113c504c867f089803408e6bb3a9d4bf41","sha":"73db4d113c504c867f089803408e6bb3a9d4bf41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/73db4d113c504c867f089803408e6bb3a9d4bf41"}],"sha":"5f9c55cbdbd5a9302d7e09e2650df5f1dc574c40","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/5f9c55cbdbd5a9302d7e09e2650df5f1dc574c40"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/73db4d113c504c867f089803408e6bb3a9d4bf41/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T05:49:19Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T05:49:19Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"message":"test: uBO''s no-argument call must do nothing at all\n\nCI caught this on v1.7.0 and it is a missing test, not a broken\nresource: with the selector guard removed, the call uBO appends for the\nglobal filter - no arguments, on every page it covers - goes looking\nwith an empty selector, and querySelectorAll('''') throws once every 50ms\nfor ten seconds into the console. Nothing asserted the quiet.\n\nThe local full run that should have found it first was the one racing my\nown edits, so its verdict was void. The harness reports that now.","tree":{"sha":"07630f32aa17cc146fc404f171d78edcbba15aed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/trees/07630f32aa17cc146fc404f171d78edcbba15aed"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/commits/73db4d113c504c867f089803408e6bb3a9d4bf41","verification":{"payload":"tree 07630f32aa17cc146fc404f171d78edcbba15aed\nparent 9e4c9e0e2834d3a0d0a8697eac7b330de3ccf47d\nauthor Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791006559 +1300\ncommitter Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791006559 +1300\n\ntest: uBO''s no-argument call must do nothing at all\n\nCI caught this on v1.7.0 and it is a missing test, not a broken\nresource: with the selector guard removed, the call uBO appends for the\nglobal filter - no arguments, on every page it covers - goes looking\nwith an empty selector, and querySelectorAll('''') throws once every 50ms\nfor ten seconds into the console. Nothing asserted the quiet.\n\nThe local full run that should have found it first was the one racing my\nown edits, so its verdict was void. The harness reports that now.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPCSVWMUDHjp4kSP8mCo6DMbbZd\nwVKwk1D89AEPXKgVYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQLMeBxDlbMJlp0tqfI9QQSFOEXfPTgle/GXJ2dj4DtLak/V64f9LhJDsCix47lVA5M\nCbBXq+PuT9Sd8YjbjwZQQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T05:49:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/73db4d113c504c867f089803408e6bb3a9d4bf41","node_id":"C_kwDOU4p2ytoAKDczZGI0ZDExM2M1MDRjODY3ZjA4OTgwMzQwOGU2YmIzYTlkNGJmNDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/9e4c9e0e2834d3a0d0a8697eac7b330de3ccf47d","sha":"9e4c9e0e2834d3a0d0a8697eac7b330de3ccf47d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/9e4c9e0e2834d3a0d0a8697eac7b330de3ccf47d"}],"sha":"73db4d113c504c867f089803408e6bb3a9d4bf41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/73db4d113c504c867f089803408e6bb3a9d4bf41"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/9e4c9e0e2834d3a0d0a8697eac7b330de3ccf47d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T05:47:52Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T05:47:52Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"message":"gtm 1.4.1: leave a page''s wait to a container that answered\n\nField-seen on hokkaido-np.co.jp with gtm.js allowlisted: one copy of this\nreported yielded=live-container while another told the page its wait was\nover. Theirs answers its own page - that is what the yield means - and\ntheir bind is what triggers it, which comes after the install. So the\ncheck belongs at the moment of telling rather than before it: the core\nhands out live(), read when it is asked, and both the telling and the\ntemplate scan stand down once it answers true.\n\nAlso in the harness, after a second afternoon lost to the same thing: a\nrun now compares every file against the snapshot it took, and says the\nresults are suspect if something else wrote one while it ran. Editing\nduring a run means the restore overwrites the edit and the suite in\nbetween tests a file nobody meant to test - which this time looked\nexactly like four tests turning flaky, and was not.","tree":{"sha":"c2771b6400c53626684e460e6aa88f36a7d8a7a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/trees/c2771b6400c53626684e460e6aa88f36a7d8a7a3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/commits/9e4c9e0e2834d3a0d0a8697eac7b330de3ccf47d","verification":{"payload":"tree c2771b6400c53626684e460e6aa88f36a7d8a7a3\nparent 9fafe590cc9ceb9f26a04a7c2e5048e2107d4eb0\nauthor Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791006472 +1300\ncommitter Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791006472 +1300\n\ngtm 1.4.1: leave a page''s wait to a container that answered\n\nField-seen on hokkaido-np.co.jp with gtm.js allowlisted: one copy of this\nreported yielded=live-container while another told the page its wait was\nover. Theirs answers its own page - that is what the yield means - and\ntheir bind is what triggers it, which comes after the install. So the\ncheck belongs at the moment of telling rather than before it: the core\nhands out live(), read when it is asked, and both the telling and the\ntemplate scan stand down once it answers true.\n\nAlso in the harness, after a second afternoon lost to the same thing: a\nrun now compares every file against the snapshot it took, and says the\nresults are suspect if something else wrote one while it ran. Editing\nduring a run means the restore overwrites the edit and the suite in\nbetween tests a file nobody meant to test - which this time looked\nexactly like four tests turning flaky, and was not.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPCSVWMUDHjp4kSP8mCo6DMbbZd\nwVKwk1D89AEPXKgVYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQFXrqis6EzhNzoDmqrbRYN9xRY0gB3T3YthNpDD7JIWiMsZpBRhhdyI1EW2fHdtwC9\nclvCg3WsCcZlJP5NtpUgc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T05:47:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/9e4c9e0e2834d3a0d0a8697eac7b330de3ccf47d","node_id":"C_kwDOU4p2ytoAKDllNGM5ZTBlMjgzNGQzYTBkMGE4Njk3ZWFjN2IzMzBkZTNjY2Y0N2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/9fafe590cc9ceb9f26a04a7c2e5048e2107d4eb0","sha":"9fafe590cc9ceb9f26a04a7c2e5048e2107d4eb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/9fafe590cc9ceb9f26a04a7c2e5048e2107d4eb0"}],"sha":"9e4c9e0e2834d3a0d0a8697eac7b330de3ccf47d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/9e4c9e0e2834d3a0d0a8697eac7b330de3ccf47d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/9fafe590cc9ceb9f26a04a7c2e5048e2107d4eb0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T05:21:04Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T05:21:04Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"message":"gtm 1.4.0: end a wait whose name only the page knows\n\nGTM gives a page three ways to be told the work is done and this answers\nall three - eventCallback, gtag''s event_callback, the anti-flicker\nhide.end(). A site can hand-roll a fourth, and then the name is the\npage''s own.\n\nhokkaido-np.co.jp spins a 読み込み中... overlay over its recommendation\nslider, and the only thing that takes it away is\n\n  window.addEventListener(''aiRecommendGenerated'', () => {\n      spinnerOverlay.style.display = ''none'';\n      aiRecommendArea.style.height = ''100%''; });\n\nWhat fires it is three vendors deep inside their container: a Custom HTML\ntag document.writes b-dash''s btm.js, which creates bdash4_ai_rec and\nloads ai_recommend.js and Edirium''s recommender.js. With the container\nreplaced the overlay spins for ever, and the exception being used for it\nlets the whole container back in - Facebook, TikTok, Twitter, Yahoo,\nmicroad, SmartNews, Clarity.\n\nThe redirect alone is enough now. A page registers what it waits for, so\nthis wraps addEventListener on the window and the document, keeps the\nnames nothing standard fires, and reads the handlers. Then it fires only\nwhat looks like a page revealing its own content:\n\n  not a standard DOM event\n  nothing consent-, login- or payment-shaped in the name, because optin\n    and consent are events too - b-dash''s own script dispatches both\n  every handler mentions display, visibility, hidden, opacity, classList\n    or .remove()\n  and no handler fetches, builds an element, pushes to a data layer,\n    touches cookies or navigates\n  and this stood in for the container\n\nEach gate has a mutation. The event is dispatched at the document and\nbubbling, because a window listener hears that and a document listener\ndoes not hear a dispatch at window; once per page, recorded on the window\nso two deliveries do not fire it twice. event=name in a filter overrides\nthe lot, and the arguments are named now - template=, needs=, event= -\nbecause position is a poor way to ask for the third.\n\nIt ends the wait; it cannot produce what the page waited FOR, so that\nslider is empty.\n\nThe tests for this passed for the wrong reason first: the fixtures\nregistered the page''s listener during jsdom''s parse, which is before the\nwrapper rather than after it as on a real page, and four negative cases\nwere passing vacuously. The positive case failing is what showed it.","tree":{"sha":"b02aabe52776d3131d9dfe1c719a58bb500e9d7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/trees/b02aabe52776d3131d9dfe1c719a58bb500e9d7d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/commits/9fafe590cc9ceb9f26a04a7c2e5048e2107d4eb0","verification":{"payload":"tree b02aabe52776d3131d9dfe1c719a58bb500e9d7d\nparent 763a669c80b9985242b0a23ddbdb04f7ebee3c30\nauthor Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791004864 +1300\ncommitter Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791004864 +1300\n\ngtm 1.4.0: end a wait whose name only the page knows\n\nGTM gives a page three ways to be told the work is done and this answers\nall three - eventCallback, gtag''s event_callback, the anti-flicker\nhide.end(). A site can hand-roll a fourth, and then the name is the\npage''s own.\n\nhokkaido-np.co.jp spins a 読み込み中... overlay over its recommendation\nslider, and the only thing that takes it away is\n\n  window.addEventListener(''aiRecommendGenerated'', () => {\n      spinnerOverlay.style.display = ''none'';\n      aiRecommendArea.style.height = ''100%''; });\n\nWhat fires it is three vendors deep inside their container: a Custom HTML\ntag document.writes b-dash''s btm.js, which creates bdash4_ai_rec and\nloads ai_recommend.js and Edirium''s recommender.js. With the container\nreplaced the overlay spins for ever, and the exception being used for it\nlets the whole container back in - Facebook, TikTok, Twitter, Yahoo,\nmicroad, SmartNews, Clarity.\n\nThe redirect alone is enough now. A page registers what it waits for, so\nthis wraps addEventListener on the window and the document, keeps the\nnames nothing standard fires, and reads the handlers. Then it fires only\nwhat looks like a page revealing its own content:\n\n  not a standard DOM event\n  nothing consent-, login- or payment-shaped in the name, because optin\n    and consent are events too - b-dash''s own script dispatches both\n  every handler mentions display, visibility, hidden, opacity, classList\n    or .remove()\n  and no handler fetches, builds an element, pushes to a data layer,\n    touches cookies or navigates\n  and this stood in for the container\n\nEach gate has a mutation. The event is dispatched at the document and\nbubbling, because a window listener hears that and a document listener\ndoes not hear a dispatch at window; once per page, recorded on the window\nso two deliveries do not fire it twice. event=name in a filter overrides\nthe lot, and the arguments are named now - template=, needs=, event= -\nbecause position is a poor way to ask for the third.\n\nIt ends the wait; it cannot produce what the page waited FOR, so that\nslider is empty.\n\nThe tests for this passed for the wrong reason first: the fixtures\nregistered the page''s listener during jsdom''s parse, which is before the\nwrapper rather than after it as on a real page, and four negative cases\nwere passing vacuously. The positive case failing is what showed it.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPCSVWMUDHjp4kSP8mCo6DMbbZd\nwVKwk1D89AEPXKgVYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQD/+jGmLdk5KzG+iU+5lTP+l42mGyaCg7TY1LFps66irtst42KcZj3/C017U3JaX5x\nEQj9eiCEsRCTLLSZevLwU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T05:21:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/9fafe590cc9ceb9f26a04a7c2e5048e2107d4eb0","node_id":"C_kwDOU4p2ytoAKDlmYWZlNTkwY2M5Y2ViOWYyNmEwNGE3YzJlNTA0OGUyMTA3ZDRlYjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/763a669c80b9985242b0a23ddbdb04f7ebee3c30","sha":"763a669c80b9985242b0a23ddbdb04f7ebee3c30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/763a669c80b9985242b0a23ddbdb04f7ebee3c30"}],"sha":"9fafe590cc9ceb9f26a04a7c2e5048e2107d4eb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/9fafe590cc9ceb9f26a04a7c2e5048e2107d4eb0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/763a669c80b9985242b0a23ddbdb04f7ebee3c30/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T05:08:14Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T05:08:14Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"message":"tools: an anchors check, and read a protocol-relative script src\n\nnpm run anchors checks that every mutation''s `from` still matches its file\nexactly once, in about a second and with no builds. That is the one\nfailure a shorter mutation run cannot see: a rename in the code a\nmutation watches leaves it matching nothing, so it tests nothing and says\nnothing - which is how CI went red on v1.6.0 while a targeted run of the\nsame area passed. CI runs it before the mutations now.\n\nIt reports an anchor as unanswerable rather than stale when the file has\nuncommitted changes. A mutation run in progress keeps one line broken at\na time, so the check lied twice while being written - once pointing at\ngtm-core.js, once at gtm-tag.js, each time the line the runner happened\nto have removed at that moment.\n\nAnd tools/tags.mjs was dropping a protocol-relative script src as a\npartial url. hokkaido-np.co.jp''s container injects\n\n  //cdn.activity.smart-bdash.com/tag-manager/bd-7verxz/btm.js\n\nwith document.write, and that is what loads their recommendation widget:\nbtm.js creates bdash4_ai_rec, loads ai_recommend.js and Edirium''s\nrecommender.js, and the page hides its spinner on an event from that\nchain. The tool reported the container as injecting one ad pixel. It now\nreads five scripts there, protocol-relative ones normalised to https.","tree":{"sha":"46e5eb67880f83698b1add442991c7739368f082","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/trees/46e5eb67880f83698b1add442991c7739368f082"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/commits/763a669c80b9985242b0a23ddbdb04f7ebee3c30","verification":{"payload":"tree 46e5eb67880f83698b1add442991c7739368f082\nparent 98fc5b0b9a514b06b349fec09204425249e55f84\nauthor Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791004094 +1300\ncommitter Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791004094 +1300\n\ntools: an anchors check, and read a protocol-relative script src\n\nnpm run anchors checks that every mutation''s `from` still matches its file\nexactly once, in about a second and with no builds. That is the one\nfailure a shorter mutation run cannot see: a rename in the code a\nmutation watches leaves it matching nothing, so it tests nothing and says\nnothing - which is how CI went red on v1.6.0 while a targeted run of the\nsame area passed. CI runs it before the mutations now.\n\nIt reports an anchor as unanswerable rather than stale when the file has\nuncommitted changes. A mutation run in progress keeps one line broken at\na time, so the check lied twice while being written - once pointing at\ngtm-core.js, once at gtm-tag.js, each time the line the runner happened\nto have removed at that moment.\n\nAnd tools/tags.mjs was dropping a protocol-relative script src as a\npartial url. hokkaido-np.co.jp''s container injects\n\n  //cdn.activity.smart-bdash.com/tag-manager/bd-7verxz/btm.js\n\nwith document.write, and that is what loads their recommendation widget:\nbtm.js creates bdash4_ai_rec, loads ai_recommend.js and Edirium''s\nrecommender.js, and the page hides its spinner on an event from that\nchain. The tool reported the container as injecting one ad pixel. It now\nreads five scripts there, protocol-relative ones normalised to https.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPCSVWMUDHjp4kSP8mCo6DMbbZd\nwVKwk1D89AEPXKgVYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQBByjJnTkGiMWc7+7jl8+K+lYvWxDRSS3MBTUQzrZlokrv6YCff+19Nl7bh0tWCUiA\nrcClPFjEXEclDsINMnrQ0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T05:08:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/763a669c80b9985242b0a23ddbdb04f7ebee3c30","node_id":"C_kwDOU4p2ytoAKDc2M2E2NjljODBiOTk4NTI0MmIwYTIzZGRiZGIwNGY3ZWJlZTNjMzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/98fc5b0b9a514b06b349fec09204425249e55f84","sha":"98fc5b0b9a514b06b349fec09204425249e55f84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/98fc5b0b9a514b06b349fec09204425249e55f84"}],"sha":"763a669c80b9985242b0a23ddbdb04f7ebee3c30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/763a669c80b9985242b0a23ddbdb04f7ebee3c30"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/98fc5b0b9a514b06b349fec09204425249e55f84/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T04:55:03Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T04:55:03Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"message":"tools: read a tag''s html in both forms, and re-anchor the guard mutation\n\nTwo things, both about something going unread in silence.\n\ntools/tags.mjs read only the string form of a Custom HTML tag:\n\n  \"vtp_html\":\"<script>...\"\n\nwhile GTM stores a tag with a container variable interpolated into it as\nan array instead:\n\n  \"vtp_html\":[\"template\",\"<script>...\",[\"macro\",7],\"...\"]\n\n24 of the 203 __html tags in hokkaido-np.co.jp''s container are in that\nsecond form, so the tool skipped 12% of it without a word - exactly where\na tag that mattered could have been hiding. It reads both now, joins the\nstring pieces and leaves a macro marked as {{macro 7}}, since only the\ncontainer can resolve one. Checked against four real containers: petzl\nstill yields its two, shonenjumpplus its six writers, and the 24 turn out\nto be user-id and TikTok identify tags.\n\nAnd the mutation CI failed on: ''no once-guard on the page callback'' was\nanchored to item.eventCallback = guard, which gtm 1.3.0 renamed to\nholder[field] = guard when the answer learned to find a callback in\neither place. Re-anchored to that line, where it covers both spellings,\nand the duplicate added alongside it is gone: 104 mutations.\n\nThat anchor was checked the fast way this time - every mutation''s from\nstring resolved against the committed sources, exactly one match each -\nwhich is the check that would have caught it before the push.","tree":{"sha":"66310382fd2257317c0e9ecbc2d85fac0873c42b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/trees/66310382fd2257317c0e9ecbc2d85fac0873c42b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/commits/98fc5b0b9a514b06b349fec09204425249e55f84","verification":{"payload":"tree 66310382fd2257317c0e9ecbc2d85fac0873c42b\nparent b5517eef136055567b9504aeba0f9d028968580a\nauthor Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791003303 +1300\ncommitter Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791003303 +1300\n\ntools: read a tag''s html in both forms, and re-anchor the guard mutation\n\nTwo things, both about something going unread in silence.\n\ntools/tags.mjs read only the string form of a Custom HTML tag:\n\n  \"vtp_html\":\"<script>...\"\n\nwhile GTM stores a tag with a container variable interpolated into it as\nan array instead:\n\n  \"vtp_html\":[\"template\",\"<script>...\",[\"macro\",7],\"...\"]\n\n24 of the 203 __html tags in hokkaido-np.co.jp''s container are in that\nsecond form, so the tool skipped 12% of it without a word - exactly where\na tag that mattered could have been hiding. It reads both now, joins the\nstring pieces and leaves a macro marked as {{macro 7}}, since only the\ncontainer can resolve one. Checked against four real containers: petzl\nstill yields its two, shonenjumpplus its six writers, and the 24 turn out\nto be user-id and TikTok identify tags.\n\nAnd the mutation CI failed on: ''no once-guard on the page callback'' was\nanchored to item.eventCallback = guard, which gtm 1.3.0 renamed to\nholder[field] = guard when the answer learned to find a callback in\neither place. Re-anchored to that line, where it covers both spellings,\nand the duplicate added alongside it is gone: 104 mutations.\n\nThat anchor was checked the fast way this time - every mutation''s from\nstring resolved against the committed sources, exactly one match each -\nwhich is the check that would have caught it before the push.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPCSVWMUDHjp4kSP8mCo6DMbbZd\nwVKwk1D89AEPXKgVYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQAusBl93dXAuwiNHu2QM0Qegq+Gy6XXkTfhYAdXtCuijcN7MbYnEYAT/W10vFK+vcO\n9oy6LHhifxcKtBuKaHkww=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T04:55:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/98fc5b0b9a514b06b349fec09204425249e55f84","node_id":"C_kwDOU4p2ytoAKDk4ZmM1YjBiOWE1MTRiMDZiMzQ5ZmVjMDkyMDQ0MjUyNDllNTVmODQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/b5517eef136055567b9504aeba0f9d028968580a","sha":"b5517eef136055567b9504aeba0f9d028968580a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/b5517eef136055567b9504aeba0f9d028968580a"}],"sha":"98fc5b0b9a514b06b349fec09204425249e55f84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/98fc5b0b9a514b06b349fec09204425249e55f84"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/b5517eef136055567b9504aeba0f9d028968580a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T04:18:11Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T04:18:11Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"message":"gtm 1.3.0: answer the callback a gtag event is waiting on\n\nA page''s wait has two spellings and this answered one of them. GTM''s is a\nfield on the pushed object; gtag''s is inside the params of a command:\n\n  gtag(''event'', ''article_click'', {\n      destination_url: url,\n      event_callback: ( ) => { window.open(url, ''_blank'') },\n      event_timeout: 1000\n  })\n\nwhich reaches the layer as an arguments object, so it is not a field on\nwhat was pushed at all and the existing answer never saw it.\n\nField-found on gamelog.apexlegends-leaksnews.com, where every article\nopens from one of these and nothing else: their handler is\n\n  typeof window < ''u'' && window.gtag\n    ? window.gtag(''event'', ''article_click'', { ..., event_callback: () =>\n        window.open(r.link, ''_blank'', ''noopener,noreferrer''),\n        event_timeout: 1e3 })\n    : window.open(r.link, ''_blank'', ''noopener,noreferrer'')\n\nand their own snippet defines gtag, so the page takes that branch whether\na loader arrived or not. With nobody to answer, no link on the page\nworks - which is what the exception for gtag/js was covering.\n\nSame answer as before, now found in either place: deferred to the next\ntick, and the field replaced with the once-guard so a real gtag working\nthrough the same queued arguments object later cannot open a second tab.\nNarrow on purpose - gtag(''event'', name, params) and nothing else, which\nis also the shape of their conversion-with-redirect - and event_timeout\nis read only to keep it out of the model.\n\nSix tests built from their own handler, three mutations.","tree":{"sha":"99a8048896fb38c9a6fdc6a93f14c0205d516769","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/trees/99a8048896fb38c9a6fdc6a93f14c0205d516769"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/commits/b5517eef136055567b9504aeba0f9d028968580a","verification":{"payload":"tree 99a8048896fb38c9a6fdc6a93f14c0205d516769\nparent cb1ab79fd77ef01e858ce781c54bddec09b5fb57\nauthor Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791001091 +1300\ncommitter Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1791001091 +1300\n\ngtm 1.3.0: answer the callback a gtag event is waiting on\n\nA page''s wait has two spellings and this answered one of them. GTM''s is a\nfield on the pushed object; gtag''s is inside the params of a command:\n\n  gtag(''event'', ''article_click'', {\n      destination_url: url,\n      event_callback: ( ) => { window.open(url, ''_blank'') },\n      event_timeout: 1000\n  })\n\nwhich reaches the layer as an arguments object, so it is not a field on\nwhat was pushed at all and the existing answer never saw it.\n\nField-found on gamelog.apexlegends-leaksnews.com, where every article\nopens from one of these and nothing else: their handler is\n\n  typeof window < ''u'' && window.gtag\n    ? window.gtag(''event'', ''article_click'', { ..., event_callback: () =>\n        window.open(r.link, ''_blank'', ''noopener,noreferrer''),\n        event_timeout: 1e3 })\n    : window.open(r.link, ''_blank'', ''noopener,noreferrer'')\n\nand their own snippet defines gtag, so the page takes that branch whether\na loader arrived or not. With nobody to answer, no link on the page\nworks - which is what the exception for gtag/js was covering.\n\nSame answer as before, now found in either place: deferred to the next\ntick, and the field replaced with the once-guard so a real gtag working\nthrough the same queued arguments object later cannot open a second tab.\nNarrow on purpose - gtag(''event'', name, params) and nothing else, which\nis also the shape of their conversion-with-redirect - and event_timeout\nis read only to keep it out of the model.\n\nSix tests built from their own handler, three mutations.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPCSVWMUDHjp4kSP8mCo6DMbbZd\nwVKwk1D89AEPXKgVYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQDeePzPsR7DDTTNhCVXDXYe4VO49FDdpl89oLi8KON1rl0cQ33Xi0Ykznd9JBkE91Y\nUKmVRkpM7LYNe4/x047gQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T04:18:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/b5517eef136055567b9504aeba0f9d028968580a","node_id":"C_kwDOU4p2ytoAKGI1NTE3ZWVmMTM2MDU1NTY3Yjk1MDRhZWJhMGY5ZDAyODk2ODU4MGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/cb1ab79fd77ef01e858ce781c54bddec09b5fb57","sha":"cb1ab79fd77ef01e858ce781c54bddec09b5fb57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/cb1ab79fd77ef01e858ce781c54bddec09b5fb57"}],"sha":"b5517eef136055567b9504aeba0f9d028968580a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/b5517eef136055567b9504aeba0f9d028968580a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/cb1ab79fd77ef01e858ce781c54bddec09b5fb57/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T03:11:38Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T03:11:38Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"message":"gtm 1.2.0: run the deferred code a page kept for itself\n\nA container''s other job is writing into the page, and no resource can\nstand in for that - the content is the container. But a site that has\nmoved that work browser-side often leaves the same code in the page,\ninside an inert <template>, waiting for something to insert it.\nshonenjumpplus.com carries four, one per banner area, each filling its\nown container from 27KB of its own banner HTML and ending with the event\nthe carousel waits for. Nothing inserted them, and their container''s own\ntags target .gtm-* classes the page no longer has - so the carousel was\nten empty slides, which is the breakage reported upstream and answered\nthere with an exception for gtm.js.\n\nA template''s content is inert, but a script taken out of one runs as soon\nas it lands in the document: it was never parser-inserted, so nothing\nmarks it as already started. Only the scripts are taken, so none of the\ntemplate''s other markup is duplicated into the page, and each template is\nrun once.\n\nThis happens with no filter at all - the redirect on its own is enough -\nand it is deliberately narrow, because running whatever a page holds back\nin a template is a way to un-gate a consent-gated embed. It runs one only\nwhere all of this holds:\n\n  this stood in for the container     a page whose own container answered\n                                      is not missing anything\n  the template holds code and no\n  other markup                        markup is a payload someone clones\n                                      when they are ready\n  every script is inline              a third-party script is the page''s\n                                      own to load, and a gated embed looks\n                                      exactly like one\n  no script, iframe, object, embed\n  or document.write in the code       code can load a third party itself,\n                                      which is the same objection\n\nshonenjumpplus''s four pass all four. A filter may still name a selector -\ngoogletagmanager_gtm, template.js-x[, aGlobal] - which is a person\ndeciding, and that path keeps the waiting for a global or a late template.\n\nTwo structural changes made the arguments possible at all, both\nmutation-tested: consentRRGtm is declared before the @include of the\nshared core, because uBO names a resource after its first function and\nthat is the only one a filter''s arguments reach; and the call the file\nmakes itself passes ''self'', so that one call stands in for the container\nwhile uBO''s per-filter calls only carry out what their arguments ask.","tree":{"sha":"91151074d707e18d7f1f28aa1cb9f3c630a20098","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/trees/91151074d707e18d7f1f28aa1cb9f3c630a20098"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/commits/cb1ab79fd77ef01e858ce781c54bddec09b5fb57","verification":{"payload":"tree 91151074d707e18d7f1f28aa1cb9f3c630a20098\nparent 3aa00e35d1a41a9680dc906154b7df55b6579c22\nauthor Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1790997098 +1300\ncommitter Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1790997098 +1300\n\ngtm 1.2.0: run the deferred code a page kept for itself\n\nA container''s other job is writing into the page, and no resource can\nstand in for that - the content is the container. But a site that has\nmoved that work browser-side often leaves the same code in the page,\ninside an inert <template>, waiting for something to insert it.\nshonenjumpplus.com carries four, one per banner area, each filling its\nown container from 27KB of its own banner HTML and ending with the event\nthe carousel waits for. Nothing inserted them, and their container''s own\ntags target .gtm-* classes the page no longer has - so the carousel was\nten empty slides, which is the breakage reported upstream and answered\nthere with an exception for gtm.js.\n\nA template''s content is inert, but a script taken out of one runs as soon\nas it lands in the document: it was never parser-inserted, so nothing\nmarks it as already started. Only the scripts are taken, so none of the\ntemplate''s other markup is duplicated into the page, and each template is\nrun once.\n\nThis happens with no filter at all - the redirect on its own is enough -\nand it is deliberately narrow, because running whatever a page holds back\nin a template is a way to un-gate a consent-gated embed. It runs one only\nwhere all of this holds:\n\n  this stood in for the container     a page whose own container answered\n                                      is not missing anything\n  the template holds code and no\n  other markup                        markup is a payload someone clones\n                                      when they are ready\n  every script is inline              a third-party script is the page''s\n                                      own to load, and a gated embed looks\n                                      exactly like one\n  no script, iframe, object, embed\n  or document.write in the code       code can load a third party itself,\n                                      which is the same objection\n\nshonenjumpplus''s four pass all four. A filter may still name a selector -\ngoogletagmanager_gtm, template.js-x[, aGlobal] - which is a person\ndeciding, and that path keeps the waiting for a global or a late template.\n\nTwo structural changes made the arguments possible at all, both\nmutation-tested: consentRRGtm is declared before the @include of the\nshared core, because uBO names a resource after its first function and\nthat is the only one a filter''s arguments reach; and the call the file\nmakes itself passes ''self'', so that one call stands in for the container\nwhile uBO''s per-filter calls only carry out what their arguments ask.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPCSVWMUDHjp4kSP8mCo6DMbbZd\nwVKwk1D89AEPXKgVYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQEspkXNO4YDee/wB17s4U8kT8KceIq5HptqqxDFW+U0mD2DwpTCp/5e9bYOvIwlNgM\nq/+XH1y34S+eGh7qHs3gY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T03:11:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/cb1ab79fd77ef01e858ce781c54bddec09b5fb57","node_id":"C_kwDOU4p2ytoAKGNiMWFiNzlmZDc3ZWYwMWU4NThjZTc4MWM1NGJkZGVjMDliNWZiNTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/3aa00e35d1a41a9680dc906154b7df55b6579c22","sha":"3aa00e35d1a41a9680dc906154b7df55b6579c22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/3aa00e35d1a41a9680dc906154b7df55b6579c22"}],"sha":"cb1ab79fd77ef01e858ce781c54bddec09b5fb57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/cb1ab79fd77ef01e858ce781c54bddec09b5fb57"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/3aa00e35d1a41a9680dc906154b7df55b6579c22/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T02:13:48Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T02:13:48Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"message":"tag 1.1.2: back the wait off once the callback is no longer a race\n\nThe poll ran every 50ms for ten seconds, which is 200 timer wakeups on\nevery page a filter covers but the trigger excludes - rude on a phone for\nno gain, because the thing it is waiting for either turns up in the first\ntick or two, when a page assigns it from a ready handler, or it is a page\nthat may do something much later.\n\n50ms for the first second, 500ms after that: 37 wakeups for the same ten\nseconds, and the CPU of the whole wait against a 2000-entry data layer\ngoes from 41.7ms to 11.4ms. Measured, both numbers.\n\nBoth ends are mutation-tested, because a backoff that starts slow loses\nthe race it exists for. Three tests that sped the clock by matching the\n50ms step exactly had to learn about the second step, or they would have\nrun the 500ms ones at full speed and timed the suite out.","tree":{"sha":"8cd86bd0742d8683b648dd32e5b61b43ee154ca9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/trees/8cd86bd0742d8683b648dd32e5b61b43ee154ca9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/commits/3aa00e35d1a41a9680dc906154b7df55b6579c22","verification":{"payload":"tree 8cd86bd0742d8683b648dd32e5b61b43ee154ca9\nparent d4be93e7d91d2a1f436454becbb22122fdfe67f5\nauthor Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1790993628 +1300\ncommitter Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1790993628 +1300\n\ntag 1.1.2: back the wait off once the callback is no longer a race\n\nThe poll ran every 50ms for ten seconds, which is 200 timer wakeups on\nevery page a filter covers but the trigger excludes - rude on a phone for\nno gain, because the thing it is waiting for either turns up in the first\ntick or two, when a page assigns it from a ready handler, or it is a page\nthat may do something much later.\n\n50ms for the first second, 500ms after that: 37 wakeups for the same ten\nseconds, and the CPU of the whole wait against a 2000-entry data layer\ngoes from 41.7ms to 11.4ms. Measured, both numbers.\n\nBoth ends are mutation-tested, because a backoff that starts slow loses\nthe race it exists for. Three tests that sped the clock by matching the\n50ms step exactly had to learn about the second step, or they would have\nrun the 500ms ones at full speed and timed the suite out.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPCSVWMUDHjp4kSP8mCo6DMbbZd\nwVKwk1D89AEPXKgVYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQLNm8cu4Kl9+Qa1Rt9oD7QwCCNqTYhNpFZdFwsKx15DZx2K0Xd7iefrXEU2RHjjTuB\nB+6gWl2WsXQa9jK8qrKAA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T02:13:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/3aa00e35d1a41a9680dc906154b7df55b6579c22","node_id":"C_kwDOU4p2ytoAKDNhYTAwZTM1ZDFhNDFhOTY4MGRjOTA2MTU0YjdkZjU1YjY1NzljMjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/d4be93e7d91d2a1f436454becbb22122fdfe67f5","sha":"d4be93e7d91d2a1f436454becbb22122fdfe67f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/d4be93e7d91d2a1f436454becbb22122fdfe67f5"}],"sha":"3aa00e35d1a41a9680dc906154b7df55b6579c22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/3aa00e35d1a41a9680dc906154b7df55b6579c22"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/d4be93e7d91d2a1f436454becbb22122fdfe67f5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T01:40:19Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T01:40:19Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"message":"1.4.0: dist/gtm-rr-all.js, every resource in one file\n\nOne userResourcesLocation URL instead of three. A resources file holds as\nmany resources as it likes, each starting at its own /// name.js and\nending at a blank line - the same shape uBO builds anyway when it joins\nthe contents of several URLs with ''\\n\\n''. Nothing is merged: the\nresources keep their own names and versions, and a filter asks for one by\nname exactly as before. Checked through uBO''s own parser: the one file\nyields all three, each byte-identical to its standalone build.\n\nMerging the code instead - folding gtm-tag into googletagmanager_gtm - is\na trap worth writing down. uBO names a resource after its FIRST function,\nso +js(googletagmanager_gtm, <url>, ...) would call\nconsentRRGtmCore(options) with a string where it wants its options\nobject, and the two entry points would have to tell themselves apart at\nruntime. That is the same silent shape as the {{1}} bug, and it would tie\na per-site tool to a global stub.\n\ntools/build.mjs is mutation-tested for the first time here: what it emits\nis what ships. Dropping a resource from the bundle and joining without\nthe blank line between them are both caught.","tree":{"sha":"24ac86697795607f966b33d6e61bb54f787ec085","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/trees/24ac86697795607f966b33d6e61bb54f787ec085"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/commits/d4be93e7d91d2a1f436454becbb22122fdfe67f5","verification":{"payload":"tree 24ac86697795607f966b33d6e61bb54f787ec085\nparent 8ca2e65e1ca9e27fac1a5b2b65396d109f480de7\nauthor Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1790991619 +1300\ncommitter Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1790991619 +1300\n\n1.4.0: dist/gtm-rr-all.js, every resource in one file\n\nOne userResourcesLocation URL instead of three. A resources file holds as\nmany resources as it likes, each starting at its own /// name.js and\nending at a blank line - the same shape uBO builds anyway when it joins\nthe contents of several URLs with ''\\n\\n''. Nothing is merged: the\nresources keep their own names and versions, and a filter asks for one by\nname exactly as before. Checked through uBO''s own parser: the one file\nyields all three, each byte-identical to its standalone build.\n\nMerging the code instead - folding gtm-tag into googletagmanager_gtm - is\na trap worth writing down. uBO names a resource after its FIRST function,\nso +js(googletagmanager_gtm, <url>, ...) would call\nconsentRRGtmCore(options) with a string where it wants its options\nobject, and the two entry points would have to tell themselves apart at\nruntime. That is the same silent shape as the {{1}} bug, and it would tie\na per-site tool to a global stub.\n\ntools/build.mjs is mutation-tested for the first time here: what it emits\nis what ships. Dropping a resource from the bundle and joining without\nthe blank line between them are both caught.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPCSVWMUDHjp4kSP8mCo6DMbbZd\nwVKwk1D89AEPXKgVYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQIfeep6iWw78vc3kxLxY1sz75CmprxIeQC7+jxuIJjmcyjQpyYLUb3aifFhRqAz8gQ\nYLPo+zNma6aMpNknTl6wA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T01:40:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/d4be93e7d91d2a1f436454becbb22122fdfe67f5","node_id":"C_kwDOU4p2ytoAKGQ0YmU5M2U3ZDkxZDJhMWY0MzY0NTRiZWNiYjIyMTIyZmRmZTY3ZjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/8ca2e65e1ca9e27fac1a5b2b65396d109f480de7","sha":"8ca2e65e1ca9e27fac1a5b2b65396d109f480de7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/8ca2e65e1ca9e27fac1a5b2b65396d109f480de7"}],"sha":"d4be93e7d91d2a1f436454becbb22122fdfe67f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/d4be93e7d91d2a1f436454becbb22122fdfe67f5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/8ca2e65e1ca9e27fac1a5b2b65396d109f480de7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T01:22:43Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T01:22:43Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"message":"tag 1.1.1: take the filter''s arguments as parameters, as uBO passes them\n\nuBO reads a function name off the front of a resource and, where there is\none, the code it injects for the filter is a call:\n\n  const match = /^function\\s+([^(\\s]+)\\s*\\(/.exec(details.js);\n  const fname = match && match[1];\n  if ( fname ) { content = fname + ''({{args}});'' }\n  else { ...content.replace(''{{''+(i+1)+''}}'', arglist[i])... }\n\nThis resource opens with function consentRRGtmTag(), so uBO called it with\nthe url and the callback name while the resource read them from ''{{1}}''\nand ''{{2}}'' - literal text in a browser. It saw no url and returned, and\nthat path says nothing, so there was no console line and no tag. Field:\nthe page had PageType=DealerLocator in the data layer and the real\ninitGmaps in place, and still no Maps script.\n\nAlso in the core: uBO calls the resource with no arguments as well, since\nthe whole file is injected and its own trailing call is what passes the\noptions. consentRRGtmCore(options) threw on options.paths into uBO''s\ncatch - a swallowed exception in the way of the next person debugging.\n\nThe reason 21 tests passed over this: the test helper substituted the\nplaceholders itself, which is a contract uBO does not use for a resource\nshaped like this one. It now runs uBO''s regex and takes the same branch,\nand a test pins the contract - a named function at the front, and no {{n}}\nleft anywhere in the resource.","tree":{"sha":"4b1980686437664515d158de69d4fb63f7d249e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/trees/4b1980686437664515d158de69d4fb63f7d249e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/commits/8ca2e65e1ca9e27fac1a5b2b65396d109f480de7","verification":{"payload":"tree 4b1980686437664515d158de69d4fb63f7d249e1\nparent 0a63fcd0f0fd08997bec657f706c0d5ca7efe61a\nauthor Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1790990563 +1300\ncommitter Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1790990563 +1300\n\ntag 1.1.1: take the filter''s arguments as parameters, as uBO passes them\n\nuBO reads a function name off the front of a resource and, where there is\none, the code it injects for the filter is a call:\n\n  const match = /^function\\s+([^(\\s]+)\\s*\\(/.exec(details.js);\n  const fname = match && match[1];\n  if ( fname ) { content = fname + ''({{args}});'' }\n  else { ...content.replace(''{{''+(i+1)+''}}'', arglist[i])... }\n\nThis resource opens with function consentRRGtmTag(), so uBO called it with\nthe url and the callback name while the resource read them from ''{{1}}''\nand ''{{2}}'' - literal text in a browser. It saw no url and returned, and\nthat path says nothing, so there was no console line and no tag. Field:\nthe page had PageType=DealerLocator in the data layer and the real\ninitGmaps in place, and still no Maps script.\n\nAlso in the core: uBO calls the resource with no arguments as well, since\nthe whole file is injected and its own trailing call is what passes the\noptions. consentRRGtmCore(options) threw on options.paths into uBO''s\ncatch - a swallowed exception in the way of the next person debugging.\n\nThe reason 21 tests passed over this: the test helper substituted the\nplaceholders itself, which is a contract uBO does not use for a resource\nshaped like this one. It now runs uBO''s regex and takes the same branch,\nand a test pins the contract - a named function at the front, and no {{n}}\nleft anywhere in the resource.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPCSVWMUDHjp4kSP8mCo6DMbbZd\nwVKwk1D89AEPXKgVYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQGl2Rq8IG/7l6QLX0f4H3tibszWWUSoJetWEaCz1kRqo5OmCbMIuuXG73K2jQySZk7\nbisR+P/klQ9Z+ExoXXUQA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T01:22:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/8ca2e65e1ca9e27fac1a5b2b65396d109f480de7","node_id":"C_kwDOU4p2ytoAKDhjYTJlNjVlMWNhOWUyN2ZhYzFhNWIyYjY1Mzk2ZDEwOWY0ODBkZTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/0a63fcd0f0fd08997bec657f706c0d5ca7efe61a","sha":"0a63fcd0f0fd08997bec657f706c0d5ca7efe61a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/0a63fcd0f0fd08997bec657f706c0d5ca7efe61a"}],"sha":"8ca2e65e1ca9e27fac1a5b2b65396d109f480de7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/8ca2e65e1ca9e27fac1a5b2b65396d109f480de7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/0a63fcd0f0fd08997bec657f706c0d5ca7efe61a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T01:01:36Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T01:01:36Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"message":"tag 1.1.0: take the container''s own trigger as a condition\n\nWhat a container checks before firing a tag is a condition on the data\nlayer, and the page writes that itself, so it can be tested without the\ncontainer. petzl.com pushes\n\n  {''PageName'':''Web_DealerLocator'',''PageType'':''DealerLocator'', ...}\n\nand their Maps tag is held behind a _cn on PageType. gtm-tag now takes\nthat as a third argument, Key=substring, read the way their model reads\nit: last write of the key wins, and a dotted key walks in.\n\nThis is not a nicety. A scriptlet filter can be scoped to a domain and\nnever to a path, so the petzl line ran on every page of the site - and\nsince 1.0.1, where a page has only the empty initGmaps placeholder the\ntag is loaded anyway after ten seconds, which meant 320KB of Maps on\nevery page. A page the trigger does not match now gets nothing: a\ntrigger is not a thing to give the benefit of the doubt to, unlike a\ncallback that may simply be late.\n\ntools/tags.mjs resolves each tag''s trigger through the container''s\nrules, predicates and macros and writes the whole line. Two things it\nhad to get right: rules reference tags by index into tags, not by\ntag_id; and the same script can be in a container twice behind different\ntriggers - petzl''s Maps tag is there for their sandbox hosts as well as\nlive, so deduplicating by url kept the first and reported the sandbox\none. They are merged now.\n\nA mutation found a weak test while this was written: the data layer\nfixtures had the matching push last, which no real page does, because a\ncontainer pushes gtm.dom and gtm.load after it.","tree":{"sha":"96ed6190085890098d1aab21c2c2aebdcc87ede4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/trees/96ed6190085890098d1aab21c2c2aebdcc87ede4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/commits/0a63fcd0f0fd08997bec657f706c0d5ca7efe61a","verification":{"payload":"tree 96ed6190085890098d1aab21c2c2aebdcc87ede4\nparent 17a57816c86ebc148dd158966e9af57758766277\nauthor Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1790989296 +1300\ncommitter Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1790989296 +1300\n\ntag 1.1.0: take the container''s own trigger as a condition\n\nWhat a container checks before firing a tag is a condition on the data\nlayer, and the page writes that itself, so it can be tested without the\ncontainer. petzl.com pushes\n\n  {''PageName'':''Web_DealerLocator'',''PageType'':''DealerLocator'', ...}\n\nand their Maps tag is held behind a _cn on PageType. gtm-tag now takes\nthat as a third argument, Key=substring, read the way their model reads\nit: last write of the key wins, and a dotted key walks in.\n\nThis is not a nicety. A scriptlet filter can be scoped to a domain and\nnever to a path, so the petzl line ran on every page of the site - and\nsince 1.0.1, where a page has only the empty initGmaps placeholder the\ntag is loaded anyway after ten seconds, which meant 320KB of Maps on\nevery page. A page the trigger does not match now gets nothing: a\ntrigger is not a thing to give the benefit of the doubt to, unlike a\ncallback that may simply be late.\n\ntools/tags.mjs resolves each tag''s trigger through the container''s\nrules, predicates and macros and writes the whole line. Two things it\nhad to get right: rules reference tags by index into tags, not by\ntag_id; and the same script can be in a container twice behind different\ntriggers - petzl''s Maps tag is there for their sandbox hosts as well as\nlive, so deduplicating by url kept the first and reported the sandbox\none. They are merged now.\n\nA mutation found a weak test while this was written: the data layer\nfixtures had the matching push last, which no real page does, because a\ncontainer pushes gtm.dom and gtm.load after it.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPCSVWMUDHjp4kSP8mCo6DMbbZd\nwVKwk1D89AEPXKgVYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQP7cNNH5jzaKpnSKRBGXJbtWEPeOFlzcCBzvRUjdii+DNXTdfsA1cKRT8LkiaOa+uR\nk+Yk6Ng+qJVzgAfBkAWQM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T01:01:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/0a63fcd0f0fd08997bec657f706c0d5ca7efe61a","node_id":"C_kwDOU4p2ytoAKDBhNjNmY2QwZjBmZDA4OTk3YmVjNjU3ZjcwNmMwZDVjYTdlZmU2MWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/17a57816c86ebc148dd158966e9af57758766277","sha":"17a57816c86ebc148dd158966e9af57758766277","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/17a57816c86ebc148dd158966e9af57758766277"}],"sha":"0a63fcd0f0fd08997bec657f706c0d5ca7efe61a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/0a63fcd0f0fd08997bec657f706c0d5ca7efe61a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/17a57816c86ebc148dd158966e9af57758766277/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T00:39:24Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T00:39:24Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"message":"tag 1.0.2: look one task after DOMContentLoaded, not in the listener\n\nA scriptlet runs at document_start, so its DOMContentLoaded listener is\nregistered before any the page adds and runs before them. petzl.com''s\ndealer page assigns the real initGmaps from one of the page''s:\n\n  $(document).ready(function(){ new petzl.controllers.DealerLocator; });\n\npetzl.controllers.DealerLocator is what assigns it, and DealerLocatorAdv.js\nconstructs that controller nowhere else at load time. So looking in our own\nlistener finds the empty placeholder from the head, every time, on a page\nthat has not set itself up yet. 1.0.1 recovered by rejecting the\nplaceholder and retrying 50ms later; being first in that queue is an\nartefact of injection timing and not something to lean on.\n\nEvery listener for that event runs in the one task, so a timeout scheduled\nfrom ours runs after all of them, and what this looks at is what the page\nhas finished building.\n\nThe container got this right by accident of its own design: its Maps tag\nfires on a consent event, long after the page is ready.","tree":{"sha":"ff936fc06f768a25f674949913bdcd5783e1ed18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/trees/ff936fc06f768a25f674949913bdcd5783e1ed18"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/commits/17a57816c86ebc148dd158966e9af57758766277","verification":{"payload":"tree ff936fc06f768a25f674949913bdcd5783e1ed18\nparent 1bb4f012ce271ea2c520bde7967112b92400bde6\nauthor Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1790987964 +1300\ncommitter Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1790987964 +1300\n\ntag 1.0.2: look one task after DOMContentLoaded, not in the listener\n\nA scriptlet runs at document_start, so its DOMContentLoaded listener is\nregistered before any the page adds and runs before them. petzl.com''s\ndealer page assigns the real initGmaps from one of the page''s:\n\n  $(document).ready(function(){ new petzl.controllers.DealerLocator; });\n\npetzl.controllers.DealerLocator is what assigns it, and DealerLocatorAdv.js\nconstructs that controller nowhere else at load time. So looking in our own\nlistener finds the empty placeholder from the head, every time, on a page\nthat has not set itself up yet. 1.0.1 recovered by rejecting the\nplaceholder and retrying 50ms later; being first in that queue is an\nartefact of injection timing and not something to lean on.\n\nEvery listener for that event runs in the one task, so a timeout scheduled\nfrom ours runs after all of them, and what this looks at is what the page\nhas finished building.\n\nThe container got this right by accident of its own design: its Maps tag\nfires on a consent event, long after the page is ready.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPCSVWMUDHjp4kSP8mCo6DMbbZd\nwVKwk1D89AEPXKgVYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQOFIePoZQsJE3Z6QdJ7GMSBETbsPh6Qx1AaW0f/BtMegs+fuxqvRS9qLDVXEVkmd5M\nQArq6VSH+DG3DxTx82LwQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T00:39:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/17a57816c86ebc148dd158966e9af57758766277","node_id":"C_kwDOU4p2ytoAKDE3YTU3ODE2Yzg2ZWJjMTQ4ZGQxNTg5NjZlOWFmNTc3NTg3NjYyNzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/1bb4f012ce271ea2c520bde7967112b92400bde6","sha":"1bb4f012ce271ea2c520bde7967112b92400bde6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/1bb4f012ce271ea2c520bde7967112b92400bde6"}],"sha":"17a57816c86ebc148dd158966e9af57758766277","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/17a57816c86ebc148dd158966e9af57758766277"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/1bb4f012ce271ea2c520bde7967112b92400bde6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T00:08:06Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T00:08:06Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"message":"tag 1.0.1: wait for a function with a body, not for the name\n\ntypeof window.initGmaps === ''function'' was true from the moment petzl''s\nhead ran, because the page defines\n\n  window.initGmaps = window.initGmaps || function() { };\n\nthere so their other pages do not throw. The real initGmaps is assigned\ninside petzl.controllers.map, their map controller, when the page\nconstructs it - later. So the tag went in at DOMContentLoaded, Maps called\nthe empty function, and nothing was drawn, with no error and no console\nline anywhere to say so. Allowing the container worked because GTM''s own\nMaps tag fires on the consent event, late enough that the real one exists.\n\nField-found: the report was that allowing the container made the browser\nask for the user''s location and the map open. Asking for the location is\nthe first thing the real callback does - onSearchDealer({ mode:\n''current_position'' }) - so it was proof of which initGmaps had answered.\n\nThe gate now wants a function with a body, in either form. On a timeout it\nloads the tag anyway and says waited-out=, because the page''s own code\nguards on the loader''s global existing (if (!window.google) return;), so a\nsearch made later works where injecting nothing leaves nothing.","tree":{"sha":"8aa9b4bac3c6b5318efacdc5972ef17ff5498e44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/trees/8aa9b4bac3c6b5318efacdc5972ef17ff5498e44"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/commits/1bb4f012ce271ea2c520bde7967112b92400bde6","verification":{"payload":"tree 8aa9b4bac3c6b5318efacdc5972ef17ff5498e44\nparent 522f15be717dccb33c89b4035b2ef3bd39926341\nauthor Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1790986086 +1300\ncommitter Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1790986086 +1300\n\ntag 1.0.1: wait for a function with a body, not for the name\n\ntypeof window.initGmaps === ''function'' was true from the moment petzl''s\nhead ran, because the page defines\n\n  window.initGmaps = window.initGmaps || function() { };\n\nthere so their other pages do not throw. The real initGmaps is assigned\ninside petzl.controllers.map, their map controller, when the page\nconstructs it - later. So the tag went in at DOMContentLoaded, Maps called\nthe empty function, and nothing was drawn, with no error and no console\nline anywhere to say so. Allowing the container worked because GTM''s own\nMaps tag fires on the consent event, late enough that the real one exists.\n\nField-found: the report was that allowing the container made the browser\nask for the user''s location and the map open. Asking for the location is\nthe first thing the real callback does - onSearchDealer({ mode:\n''current_position'' }) - so it was proof of which initGmaps had answered.\n\nThe gate now wants a function with a body, in either form. On a timeout it\nloads the tag anyway and says waited-out=, because the page''s own code\nguards on the loader''s global existing (if (!window.google) return;), so a\nsearch made later works where injecting nothing leaves nothing.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgPCSVWMUDHjp4kSP8mCo6DMbbZd\nwVKwk1D89AEPXKgVYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQMqNqX2XUJ8qBsjPBAgq0pBkTx7htVY3tKRaidjTzveddMiWBmKMQ9xxHn7Ci9Wi55\nQ7DFjb1MDIPV5yWw9wqQw=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T00:08:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/1bb4f012ce271ea2c520bde7967112b92400bde6","node_id":"C_kwDOU4p2ytoAKDFiYjRmMDEyY2UyNzFlYTJjNTIwYmRlNzk2NzExMmI5MjQwMGJkZTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commit/522f15be717dccb33c89b4035b2ef3bd39926341","sha":"522f15be717dccb33c89b4035b2ef3bd39926341","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/522f15be717dccb33c89b4035b2ef3bd39926341"}],"sha":"1bb4f012ce271ea2c520bde7967112b92400bde6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/1bb4f012ce271ea2c520bde7967112b92400bde6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1659004?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanbr","id":1659004,"login":"ryanbr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTkwMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanbr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/commits/522f15be717dccb33c89b4035b2ef3bd39926341/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T23:37:26Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T23:37:26Z","email":"mp3geek@gmail.com","name":"Fanboynz"},"message":"ci: a pinned install URL has to resolve, not just match the version\n\nv1.1.2 and v1.1.4 were pinned in the README and never tagged, so for two\nreleases every URL it gave returned 404. uBO skips a user resource URL\nthat fails without a word, so the resource was simply missing, with\nnothing to see in the console, the logger or the settings panel - it\nlooked like several URLs in userResourcesLocation not working, which they\ndo. The build already checked a pinned URL names the version being built;\nthis checks the version exists, asked of the API because the raw host\ncaches a 404 for minutes after a tag lands.","tree":{"sha":"be9dbea27b4adf1f4b50fa95ee3b6ab329295275","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/trees/be9dbea27b4adf1f4b50fa95ee3b6ab329295275"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ryanbr/gtm-rr/git/commits/522f15be717dccb33c89b4035b2ef3bd39926341","verification":{"payload":"tree be9dbea27b4adf1f4b50fa95ee3b6ab329295275\nparent 30e5aa92eacfa20bd7eecd5f57e498d12dfa3bbb\nauthor Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1790984246 +1300\ncommitter Fanboynz <mp3geek@gmail.com> 1790984246 +1300\n\nci: a pinned install URL has to resolve, not just match the version\n\nv1.1.2 and v1.1.4 were pinned in the README and never tagged, so for two\nreleases every URL it gave returned 404. uBO skips a user resource URL\nthat fails without a word, so the resource was simply missing, with\nnothing to see in the console, the logger or the settings panel - it\nlooked like several URLs in userResourcesLocation not working, which they\ndo. The build already checked a pinned URL names the version being built;\nthis checks the version exists, asked of the API because the raw host\ncaches a 404 for minutes after a tag lands.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAAL