orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhia10/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhia10/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhia10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhia10/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhia10","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhia10/EstateMind/commits/63d554c60de8c94f39cda574f50a4001ac379e02/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-05T21:18:51Z","email":"dhia.romd1@gmail.com","name":"dhia10"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-05T21:18:51Z","email":"dhia.romd1@gmail.com","name":"dhia10"},"message":"fix: villa3d CORS on error + nginx CORS safety net\n\nmain.py: wrap all httpx calls in try/except and raise HTTPException\n  so FastAPI''s CORS middleware always adds Access-Control headers,\n  even on 401/402/5xx responses from Tripo API.\n  Clear user-facing messages: \"API key expired\", \"credits exhausted\".\n\nnginx.azure.conf: add CORS headers to /villa3d/ block with `always`\n  flag — nginx adds them even when upstream returns an error status,\n  preventing browser from blocking the error message from being read.\n  Also handle OPTIONS preflight with 204 directly at nginx level.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c74cfe00a77f2f926533add76e8dd6043f7ed0d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhia10/EstateMind/git/trees/c74cfe00a77f2f926533add76e8dd6043f7ed0d1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhia10/EstateMind/git/commits/63d554c60de8c94f39cda574f50a4001ac379e02","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20670848?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhia10/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhia10/followers","following_url":"https:/