d{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/commits/bf61f6e8973600d36da0bd7b7a75875c04baa6ad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T04:13:54Z","email":"317562256+smanoj1813-collab@users.noreply.github.com","name":"smanoj1813-collab"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T04:13:54Z","email":"317562256+smanoj1813-collab@users.noreply.github.com","name":"smanoj1813-collab"},"message":"feat(access): sell platform access as a product with duration, price and MIS\n\nOnboarding used to record nothing about how long a student''s platform access\nruns, so the college could not bill it or report on it. A \"product\" is now a\nname + durationMonths (12/24/36 presets) + price per student, stored in\naccessProducts; assigning one stamps accessProductId/accessProductName/\naccessDurationMonths/accessPrice/accessCurrency/accessStart/accessEnd on the\nstudent. The window is inclusive of its last day (start + months - 1 day,\nmonth-end clamped) and status (active / expiring <= 60 days / expired) is\nderived from accessEnd vs today-IST, so no cron is needed.\n\n- catalogue + archive: /superadmin/products (Products tab)\n- import: UserImport picks a product and start date, with a live \"valid till\"\n  preview; the product is resolved server-side before any Auth account is\n  created, so a bad product fails the whole batch cleanly\n- existing students: Students page bulk \"Change platform access\" (assign or\n  clear; start date; preview); CSV re-import cannot retro-fix a dupe-skipped row\n- MIS: server-side callable aggregates per-product and per-college buckets,\n  active/lapsed subscription value and the next expiries (Expired excludes\n  unassigned students so the college columns stay disjoint)\n- student side: an access pill on the dashboard (product, duration, valid till)\n- rules: accessProducts readable by signed-in staff, writable by superadmin\n\nPure window maths is duplicated functions/src/accessProducts.ts <->\nsrc/shared/utils/accessWindow.ts and parity-pinned in\nfunctions/test/accessProducts.test.ts (24) + src/shared/utils/accessWindow.test.ts (6).\n\nCo-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"a51ac365bd124703905c1f1a7204d449b0e5a483","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/git/trees/a51ac365bd124703905c1f1a7204d449b0e5a483"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/git/commits/bf61f6e8973600d36da0bd7b7a75875c04baa6ad","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/317562256?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab","id":317562256,"login":"smanoj1813-collab","node_id":"U_kgDOEu2dkA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/commit/bf61f6e8973600d36da0bd7b7a75875c04baa6ad","node_id":"C_kwDOU53JZNoAKGJmNjFmNmU4OTczNjAwZDM2ZGEwYmQ3YjdhNzU4NzVjMDRiYWE2YWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/commit/d1e2371a673a935b53e384d608f21211edec2250","sha":"d1e2371a673a935b53e384d608f21211edec2250","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/commits/d1e2371a673a935b53e384d608f21211edec2250"}],"sha":"bf61f6e8973600d36da0bd7b7a75875c04baa6ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/commits/bf61f6e8973600d36da0bd7b7a75875c04baa6ad"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/317562256?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab","id":317562256,"login":"smanoj1813-collab","node_id":"U_kgDOEu2dkA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/commits/d1e2371a673a935b53e384d608f21211edec2250/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T03:40:34Z","email":"317562256+smanoj1813-collab@users.noreply.github.com","name":"smanoj1813-collab"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T03:40:34Z","email":"317562256+smanoj1813-collab@users.noreply.github.com","name":"smanoj1813-collab"},"message":"fix(flow): match the cohort the same way from auto-schedule to the student\n\nThe student page already knew that \"2026-2027\" is the class of 2027 and\nthat a division field may be a list (\"A,B,C,D\"), but the scheduling leg\nstill compared those fields as literal strings. A directory full of\ncorrect mappings therefore produced \"No active faculty mappings ... run\nAuto Map first\" in the auto-scheduler, and the timetable clash warning\ncould not see the class it was double-booking.\n\nThe auto-scheduler demand filter now reads batch tokens as keys and\ndivision/section as letter sets (a whole-batch mapping is demand for a\nrun of division A; a division-specific mapping is never expanded into a\nblank run). Occupancy and clash detection use one shared overlap rule\n(cohortScopesOverlap) in both the server and the browser copy, and the\ndivision-letter logic moved to the one server cohort module\n(cohortBatch.ts) so the student page, the scheduler and the clash\ndetector cannot drift apart again.\n\nAdds functions/test/curriculumFlow.test.ts, which walks one cohort\n(BBA, batch 2027, mapped 2026-2027 / A,B,C,D) through demand ->\ntimetable row -> session -> student matcher -> clash detection, and\ndocs/curriculum-to-student-flow.md with the flow chart.\n\nCo-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"9f36b6e31e8a9aae7aad2667b6124d3e589533df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/git/trees/9f36b6e31e8a9aae7aad2667b6124d3e589533df"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/git/commits/d1e2371a673a935b53e384d608f21211edec2250","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/317562256?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab","id":317562256,"login":"smanoj1813-collab","node_id":"U_kgDOEu2dkA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/commit/d1e2371a673a935b53e384d608f21211edec2250","node_id":"C_kwDOU53JZNoAKGQxZTIzNzFhNjczYTkzNWI1M2UzODRkNjA4ZjIxMjExZWRlYzIyNTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/commit/d95b58467e384967a45cb41a4a5c8648e4ac115e","sha":"d95b58467e384967a45cb41a4a5c8648e4ac115e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/commits/d95b58467e384967a45cb41a4a5c8648e4ac115e"}],"sha":"d1e2371a673a935b53e384d608f21211edec2250","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/commits/d1e2371a673a935b53e384d608f21211edec2250"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/317562256?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab","id":317562256,"login":"smanoj1813-collab","node_id":"U_kgDOEu2dkA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/commits/d95b58467e384967a45cb41a4a5c8648e4ac115e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T19:01:18Z","email":"317562256+smanoj1813-collab@users.noreply.github.com","name":"smanoj1813-collab"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T19:01:18Z","email":"317562256+smanoj1813-collab@users.noreply.github.com","name":"smanoj1813-collab"},"message":"feat(onboarding): require the columns that cohort matching actually needs\n\nStudent imports silently accepted rows with no Batch, Division, Department\nor Semester, and then students never appeared in the right cohort lists.\nThe importer now requires Name, Email, Registration Number, Department,\nBatch, Division and Semester (whole number 1-12), so a semester is never\nsilently defaulted to 1; the server validates the same fields per row and\nreports the exact missing column. The onboarding template and the User\nImport hint now show exactly which columns are required vs optional, and\nthe Course and Blood Group columns are gone -- the importer dropped both.\n\nCo-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"5fe8301723819714ab10db8400eda212aaa91973","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/git/trees/5fe8301723819714ab10db8400eda212aaa91973"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/git/commits/d95b58467e384967a45cb41a4a5c8648e4ac115e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/317562256?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab","id":317562256,"login":"smanoj1813-collab","node_id":"U_kgDOEu2dkA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/commit/d95b58467e384967a45cb41a4a5c8648e4ac115e","node_id":"C_kwDOU53JZNoAKGQ5NWI1ODQ2N2UzODQ5NjdhNDVjYjQxYTRhNWM4NjQ4ZTRhYzExNWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/commit/dec2341bd5dd8a6a6dda5bbde84bcea84e6ec2a8","sha":"dec2341bd5dd8a6a6dda5bbde84bcea84e6ec2a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/commits/dec2341bd5dd8a6a6dda5bbde84bcea84e6ec2a8"}],"sha":"d95b58467e384967a45cb41a4a5c8648e4ac115e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/commits/d95b58467e384967a45cb41a4a5c8648e4ac115e"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/commits/dec2341bd5dd8a6a6dda5bbde84bcea84e6ec2a8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T18:42:19Z","email":"agent@arena.ai","name":"Arena Agent"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T18:42:19Z","email":"agent@arena.ai","name":"Arena Agent"},"message":"fix(cohort): read a division/section list as a set of letters\n\nAuto-Map let staff write DIVISION = \"A,B,C,D\" (the subject is taught to all\nfour divisions). Both matchers normalised the WHOLE field to one token —\n\"A,B,C,D\" became \"abcd\" — which equals no student''s \"A\", so eight correctly\nmapped subjects showed up as \"mapped — but to a different class than yours\"\nand the page blamed the student''s division. The same value would also blank\nthe attendance roster, which compares the class''s letters against the\nstudent''s the same way.\n\nDivision/section are now letter SETS on both sides:\n\n  * \"A,B,C,D\" (also \"A/B\", \"A;B\", \"A B\", \"A&B\" and \"Div A, Div B\") is the\n    set {a, b, c, d};\n  * a field with no separator is still ONE token — a bare letter code\n    \"ABCD\" does not start matching division \"A\";\n  * the two slots still combine into one set per side, as before, so a\n    student recorded under `section: \"A\"` still matches a class for\n    division \"A\";\n  * mismatch attribution checks the student''s whole set against the class''s\n    whole set, so a student \"D,E\" is not blamed for a class {a,b,c,d} it\n    partly covers, while \"E\" still is.\n\nKept in sync across both copies: src/shared/utils/cohortMatching.ts\n(cohortLetters, used by the roster matcher and its diagnostics) and\nfunctions/src/studentCurriculum.ts (cohortLetters, used by\nsessionMatchesCohort and therefore by diagnoseCohortExclusion).\n\nTests: the new cases in both suites fail against the previous single-token\nreading (5 failures over the two files) and pass with it. Verified: functions\n1109/1109, root 611/611, functions build + root tsc clean, dead-code and\neslint clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"c2f90f356b368e6e98733aa9b182b3c71e2399aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/git/trees/c2f90f356b368e6e98733aa9b182b3c71e2399aa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/git/commits/dec2341bd5dd8a6a6dda5bbde84bcea84e6ec2a8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/commit/dec2341bd5dd8a6a6dda5bbde84bcea84e6ec2a8","node_id":"C_kwDOU53JZNoAKGRlYzIzNDFiZDVkZDhhNmE2ZGRhNWJiZGU4NGJjZWE4NGU2ZWMyYTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/commit/51fa3e580d8f18e11afe3d0b553a092cb695c41b","sha":"51fa3e580d8f18e11afe3d0b553a092cb695c41b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/commits/51fa3e580d8f18e11afe3d0b553a092cb695c41b"}],"sha":"dec2341bd5dd8a6a6dda5bbde84bcea84e6ec2a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/commits/dec2341bd5dd8a6a6dda5bbde84bcea84e6ec2a8"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/commits/51fa3e580d8f18e11afe3d0b553a092cb695c41b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T18:04:21Z","email":"agent@arena.ai","name":"Arena Agent"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T18:04:21Z","email":"agent@arena.ai","name":"Arena Agent"},"message":"fix(cohort): an academic-year range names the class of its end year\n\nA student whose batch is \"2027\" was reported as being in a different class\nthan the curriculum mappings stored as \"2026-2027\" / \"2026-27\", so the\nstudent curriculum page showed \"mapped — but to a different class than\nyours\" while correct mappings sat in the database. The same strict string\ncomparison made runAutoMapping drop an already-mapped faculty row from\n`taken`, so applyAutoMapping re-proposed them and wrote a DUPLICATE mapping\nfor the same class.\n\nThe rule, now shared by both copies (browser + server):\n\n  * an academic-year range canonicalises to its END year — \"2026-2027\",\n    \"2026-27\", \"2026 – 2027\" and \"2026/2027\" are all the class of \"2027\";\n  * a bare start year is a DIFFERENT cohort — \"2026\" is neither \"2027\" nor\n    \"2026-2027\";\n  * only a CONSECUTIVE pair is an academic year — \"2026-2028\" keeps its\n    literal token so it cannot match by accident;\n  * everything else is unchanged — \"2027\" = 2027 = \" 2027 \", \"A\" = \"a\".\n\n  * src/shared/utils/cohortMatching.ts — normalizeBatchKey / batchKeysMatch,\n    used by matchStudentToCohort (roster + diagnostics).\n  * functions/src/cohortBatch.ts — the server copy (functions/ cannot import\n    src/ at build time: tsconfig rootDir is src), shared by the two callables.\n  * functions/src/studentCurriculum.ts — sessionMatchesCohort, the faculty\n    ledger filter (ledgerRowBatchMatches) and the cohort diagnosis (which\n    inherits the matcher).\n  * functions/src/autoCurriculumMapping.ts — the already-mapped skip.\n\nTests: the frontend suite and functions/test/studentCurriculum.test.ts pin\nthe rule at matcher and diagnosis level; functions/test/autoCurriculumMapping\n.test.ts pins the dedupe (a faculty who would win the course must not be\nre-proposed once already mapped to it); functions/test/cohortBatch.test.ts\nimports BOTH copies and fails if they ever drift apart.\n\nVerified: functions 1106 unit tests, root 607, functions tsc build and root\ntsc --noEmit all clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"8573248905ac457c478c757b702dcf209cc0d175","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/git/trees/8573248905ac457c478c757b702dcf209cc0d175"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/git/commits/51fa3e580d8f18e11afe3d0b553a092cb695c41b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/commit/51fa3e580d8f18e11afe3d0b553a092cb695c41b","node_id":"C_kwDOU53JZNoAKDUxZmEzZTU4MGQ4ZjE4ZTExYWZlM2QwYjU1M2EwOTJjYjY5NWM0MWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/commit/71bfb50321f48635f9d7bad6e438c0e19a00f5b6","sha":"71bfb50321f48635f9d7bad6e438c0e19a00f5b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/commits/71bfb50321f48635f9d7bad6e438c0e19a00f5b6"}],"sha":"51fa3e580d8f18e11afe3d0b553a092cb695c41b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/commits/51fa3e580d8f18e11afe3d0b553a092cb695c41b"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/commits/71bfb50321f48635f9d7bad6e438c0e19a00f5b6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T17:10:38Z","email":"dev@vriddhi.local","name":"Vriddhi Dev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T17:10:38Z","email":"dev@vriddhi.local","name":"Vriddhi Dev"},"message":"chore: ignore the emulator''s database-debug.log","tree":{"sha":"d5153b5d8560e4a4c6f0cc1e8130efb44942a449","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/git/trees/d5153b5d8560e4a4c6f0cc1e8130efb44942a449"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/git/commits/71bfb50321f48635f9d7bad6e438c0e19a00f5b6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/commit/71bfb50321f48635f9d7bad6e438c0e19a00f5b6","node_id":"C_kwDOU53JZNoAKDcxYmZiNTAzMjFmNDg2MzVmOWQ3YmFkNmU0MzhjMGUxOWEwMGY1YjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/commit/9e72a865ebcee02b80894afa44634936f5ad1a69","sha":"9e72a865ebcee02b80894afa44634936f5ad1a69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/commits/9e72a865ebcee02b80894afa44634936f5ad1a69"}],"sha":"71bfb50321f48635f9d7bad6e438c0e19a00f5b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/commits/71bfb50321f48635f9d7bad6e438c0e19a00f5b6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/4187077?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arena-ai-coding-agent%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arena-ai-coding-agent%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arena-ai-coding-agent%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arena-ai-coding-agent%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/arena-ai-coding-agent","id":298482267,"login":"arena-ai-coding-agent[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDOEcp6Ww","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arena-ai-coding-agent%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arena-ai-coding-agent%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arena-ai-coding-agent%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arena-ai-coding-agent%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arena-ai-coding-agent%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arena-ai-coding-agent%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/commits/9e72a865ebcee02b80894afa44634936f5ad1a69/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T16:48:53Z","email":"298482267+arena-ai-coding-agent[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"arena-ai-coding-agent[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T16:48:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Curriculum → Timetable → Reschedule: one admin flow, plus a real reschedule path (#95)\n\n* Curriculum → Timetable → Reschedule: one admin flow, and a real way to move a class\n\nThe admin''s curriculum surface was three tabs on one page plus two other pages\nfor the same job: assign faculty on Curriculum, read the assignment on Mappings,\nbuild the timetable on Class Schedule, and move a class nowhere at all — admins\nhad no reschedule path, so editing a slot left every dated class it had already\nproduced sitting at the old time.\n\nOne screen now (src/modules/admin/pages/AdminCurriculum.tsx):\n\n  1. branch + batch, with programme-level progress\n  2. a semester ladder 1…6 — every semester is a tile, empty ones included, so\n     a missing syllabus is visible instead of blank\n  3. the semester''s subjects: assign/reassign faculty, add timetable slots,\n     create the dated classes, reschedule, or cancel the slot\n\nScheduling happens in place (ScheduleSlotDialog) and can materialise the next\nfour weeks through the existing generateClassSessions callable, so plan and\nactual are linked in one action. The timetable query now uses\n[''weeklySchedules'',''admin'',collegeId] — the same key useAdminSchedule uses — so\nthis page and the Class Schedule page never disagree (this also lands the\npending useEffect → useQuery fix).\n\nRescheduling is new server work (functions/src/classSchedule.ts, S2.6):\nrescheduleClass moves either the recurring slot (every future unmarked class\nfollows) or a single dated class. Only scheduled, future, unmarked classes are\never touched; a class already on the new weekday stays put; a destination that\nis taken is merged (slot) or refused (one-off); cross-day moves write to the\ndeterministic new id and remove the old one so generateClassSessions can\nneither resurrect nor duplicate; hard faculty/room clashes abort with details\nunless explicitly forced. The planner is pure (planReschedule) and the dialog\npreviews its outcome before anything is written.\n\nAlso:\n  * firestore.indexes.json: the classSessions indexes the Attendance page needs\n    when a branch and/or batch filter is applied (collegeId + branch/batch +\n    date DESC + startTime DESC).\n  * render checks (scripts/render-check/run.mjs): the flow page mounts against\n    fixtures and the ladder, the joins, both dialogs and the reschedule preview\n    are asserted.\n\nTests: npm run test:unit 599 (was 575), npm run test:render 400 checks,\nfunctions node --test 1093, tsc + vite build clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix the two Windows-only CRLF failures in the seed tests at the source\n\nBoth failures were the same bug: `All_QuestionBank.csv` is inlined through\nVite''s `?raw` (and the unit tests'' raw-asset hook), so the module saw whatever\nline endings the working tree happened to hold. With a CRLF copy — a Windows\nregeneration, or a checkout from before `.gitattributes` pinned `*.csv` — the\ncombined CSV''s header arrived as `…examName\\r` while the derived per-programme\ndatasets came back LF-only from filterSeedCsvByBranch, so:\n\n  * ''bundles only the combined CSV and filters the others out of it'' failed on\n    `file.csv.split(''\\n'')[0] !== SEED_ALL_CSV.split(''\\n'')[0]`\n  * ''falls back to the whole CSV when there is nothing to filter on'' failed on\n    the same comparison against the header-only fallback\n\nThree changes, in dependency order:\n\n  * generate_seed.py writes with `newline=\"\\n\"`. Python translates `\\n` to CRLF\n    on Windows by default, so regenerating the seed there was what produced the\n    mismatched file in the first place.\n  * questionBankSeed.ts normalises the bundled CSV to LF once, at the module\n    boundary. Everything downstream — the per-programme derivations, row counts,\n    fingerprints and the seeded content — is now byte-identical on every platform\n    instead of depending on the checkout.\n  * the two assertions split on /\\r?\\n/ and a new test pins the invariant (the\n    bundled and derived CSVs are LF-only, and the normalisation is lossless: 759\n    rows still parse).\n\nVerified by forcing a CRLF working copy of the combined CSV and running the\nsuite: 600/600 pass with CRLF and 600/600 with LF (was 599 with 2 failing on\nWindows, 599 passing on Linux because the fixture only breaks there).\n\nCo-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs(curriculum-flow): record the line-ending fix in the verification block\n\nThe suite is 600, not 599, since 0e648e3 fixed the two Windows-only CRLF\nfailures in the seed tests; note what moved the count and why it only ever\nfailed on a Windows checkout.\n\nCo-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: smanoj1813-collab <317562256+smanoj1813-collab@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"64d1c546b727a3b5e87155af09219e14263c8a12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/git/trees/64d1c546b727a3b5e87155af09219e14263c8a12"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/git/commits/9e72a865ebcee02b80894afa44634936f5ad1a69","verification":{"payload":"tree 64d1c546b727a3b5e87155af09219e14263c8a12\nparent ec1f0d821fb7db02a2d6725ac24fa81f2a1a65f7\nauthor arena-ai-coding-agent[bot] <298482267+arena-ai-coding-agent[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1790786933 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790786933 +0530\n\nCurriculum → Timetable → Reschedule: one admin flow, plus a real reschedule path (#95)\n\n* Curriculum → Timetable → Reschedule: one admin flow, and a real way to move a class\n\nThe admin''s curriculum surface was three tabs on one page plus two other pages\nfor the same job: assign faculty on Curriculum, read the assignment on Mappings,\nbuild the timetable on Class Schedule, and move a class nowhere at all — admins\nhad no reschedule path, so editing a slot left every dated class it had already\nproduced sitting at the old time.\n\nOne screen now (src/modules/admin/pages/AdminCurriculum.tsx):\n\n  1. branch + batch, with programme-level progress\n  2. a semester ladder 1…6 — every semester is a tile, empty ones included, so\n     a missing syllabus is visible instead of blank\n  3. the semester''s subjects: assign/reassign faculty, add timetable slots,\n     create the dated classes, reschedule, or cancel the slot\n\nScheduling happens in place (ScheduleSlotDialog) and can materialise the next\nfour weeks through the existing generateClassSessions callable, so plan and\nactual are linked in one action. The timetable query now uses\n[''weeklySchedules'',''admin'',collegeId] — the same key useAdminSchedule uses — so\nthis page and the Class Schedule page never disagree (this also lands the\npending useEffect → useQuery fix).\n\nRescheduling is new server work (functions/src/classSchedule.ts, S2.6):\nrescheduleClass moves either the recurring slot (every future unmarked class\nfollows) or a single dated class. Only scheduled, future, unmarked classes are\never touched; a class already on the new weekday stays put; a destination that\nis taken is merged (slot) or refused (one-off); cross-day moves write to the\ndeterministic new id and remove the old one so generateClassSessions can\nneither resurrect nor duplicate; hard faculty/room clashes abort with details\nunless explicitly forced. The planner is pure (planReschedule) and the dialog\npreviews its outcome before anything is written.\n\nAlso:\n  * firestore.indexes.json: the classSessions indexes the Attendance page needs\n    when a branch and/or batch filter is applied (collegeId + branch/batch +\n    date DESC + startTime DESC).\n  * render checks (scripts/render-check/run.mjs): the flow page mounts against\n    fixtures and the ladder, the joins, both dialogs and the reschedule preview\n    are asserted.\n\nTests: npm run test:unit 599 (was 575), npm run test:render 400 checks,\nfunctions node --test 1093, tsc + vite build clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix the two Windows-only CRLF failures in the seed tests at the source\n\nBoth failures were the same bug: `All_QuestionBank.csv` is inlined through\nVite''s `?raw` (and the unit tests'' raw-asset hook), so the module saw whatever\nline endings the working tree happened to hold. With a CRLF copy — a Windows\nregeneration, or a checkout from before `.gitattributes` pinned `*.csv` — the\ncombined CSV''s header arrived as `…examName\\r` while the derived per-programme\ndatasets came back LF-only from filterSeedCsvByBranch, so:\n\n  * ''bundles only the combined CSV and filters the others out of it'' failed on\n    `file.csv.split(''\\n'')[0] !== SEED_ALL_CSV.split(''\\n'')[0]`\n  * ''falls back to the whole CSV when there is nothing to filter on'' failed on\n    the same comparison against the header-only fallback\n\nThree changes, in dependency order:\n\n  * generate_seed.py writes with `newline=\"\\n\"`. Python translates `\\n` to CRLF\n    on Windows by default, so regenerating the seed there was what produced the\n    mismatched file in the first place.\n  * questionBankSeed.ts normalises the bundled CSV to LF once, at the module\n    boundary. Everything downstream — the per-programme derivations, row counts,\n    fingerprints and the seeded content — is now byte-identical on every platform\n    instead of depending on the checkout.\n  * the two assertions split on /\\r?\\n/ and a new test pins the invariant (the\n    bundled and derived CSVs are LF-only, and the normalisation is lossless: 759\n    rows still parse).\n\nVerified by forcing a CRLF working copy of the combined CSV and running the\nsuite: 600/600 pass with CRLF and 600/600 with LF (was 599 with 2 failing on\nWindows, 599 passing on Linux because the fixture only breaks there).\n\nCo-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs(curriculum-flow): record the line-ending fix in the verification block\n\nThe suite is 600, not 599, since 0e648e3 fixed the two Windows-only CRLF\nfailures in the seed tests; note what moved the count and why it only ever\nfailed on a Windows checkout.\n\nCo-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: smanoj1813-collab <317562256+smanoj1813-collab@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvT11CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVaAQACqhjkNRe7Zsyc6E+FEW8o/I\nvL+p5cA4py02bRJ1wM2XG2Hc98g1zeBIcCXy/GtDB3IwNT4wbpLBH5Tr/MFT07Dg\nSCq8gARPIIaDdzQ1jzeEaKGmjCINojtZd6ImDBYrEcmKOCW+xM40aCXcmBcaqO2z\nvS70XbKu7OhsuEozq/KaxKqVkO3B/+/CFV8onGa2A2ukga9/NxJi+FHqxC9wQbjV\nKW/sDhuX15F5+ui9z9RYS5XuChWMf/z30PGdUuuiaLAELWAJ4xDccOn1BDMc9ll/\nB/TcW82Gzx4ux3yHJWfVaK7TMkVuVgyFestUGB1UYLHcM0AVbMfUgHSxyaU9T7Jb\nE40DjKd2ieMwxRdX2rEixkxoq5T8FPkDTidG7wHEt65jxciFV4n6lZCQoWyVI+C3\n2vNuP58h2KRWESx3S87cqwRngaBf2L5atESXoxqlfD3XDoOl8wjqMYi8fCMmZvK/\nvFVYKcRirmqworCr3QWKTCLzpNeQP/bJb59/6BmPZhIEg7mRvuYzsiN4anF+U/DD\n9XG+CPORl2oDg+mH0bjlWmU+vnQb+POFHLp4EsWHIF0xljiVKYzgVJV2IPrvSit4\nrGE71rXMBglrphF/sU4F+3ONT6F1JloLZX95e76DAwTZgxCSVxWAwvzfT5pOSLFv\nXI94JJcW/XiDkh0979m5\n=bhJo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T08:19:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flo