b/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi-engineering/commits/ae250e63688bb057694f5539785d8a1247b6b3d4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T08:47:38Z","email":"317562256+smanoj1813-collab@users.noreply.github.com","name":"smanoj1813-collab"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T08:47:38Z","email":"317562256+smanoj1813-collab@users.noreply.github.com","name":"smanoj1813-collab"},"message":"fix(question-import): sub-topic grouping in superadmin bulk paper import\n\nThe superadmin Universal Question Bank ''Import papers (ZIP / PDF)'' flow had\nthe same problem as the faculty paper upload: a printed question carrying\nsub-topics (a)/(b)/(c) or (A)-(D) surfaced as individual questions — and the\nstructured ''parts'' the model returns were invisible in the Review Queue and\npool cards, which render only the text.\n\n- Extract the sub-topic helpers into functions/src/subpartMerge.ts so both\n  parse pipelines share the exact same grouping rules (paperParsing.ts now\n  imports/re-exports them; all its tests still pass).\n- normalizeImportedQuestions folds printed parts into the visible question\n  text, so one row shows the stem and all its sub-topics.\n- New mergeImportedSubparts re-combines AI-split sub-topic entries into the\n  parent question (same marker-chain rules as the paper-upload parser),\n  summing sub-part marks and recording the joins in parts/importParts, with\n  a warning reporting how many entries were joined.\n- lastSubpartRank now ignores bare digits (question numbers/dates like ''11.''\n  or ''2025.'') so a ''(a) …'' sub-part merges into 