ttps://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41597107?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diberry/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diberry/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diberry/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diberry/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/diberry","id":41597107,"login":"diberry","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxNTk3MTA3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diberry/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diberry/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diberry/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diberry/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diberry/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/diberry","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/diberry/aca-3/commits/048888d17364942ce3b359d74b840b138e9b9714/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T22:25:02Z","email":"diberry@microsoft.com","name":"Dina Berry (MSFT)"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T22:25:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"(ignore) Establish ACA test-driven delivery policy (#4)\n\n* docs: require tests-first wave delivery\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs: adopt red-green-refactor workflow\n\nReplace the mandatory two-PR test gate with a single-PR TDD workflow that records an expected failing test before implementation while keeping main and merge-ready pull requests green.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* ci: enforce test-driven pull requests\n\nAdd a required TDD evidence check, a dedicated test status, cross-platform idempotent GitHub configuration scripts, and documentation for the current private-repository plan limitation.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat: adapt GitHub configuration to capabilities\n\nDetect repository ownership, visibility, reported plan, rulesets, and classic branch protection before applying the maximum supported configuration. Preserve explicit partial-enforcement failure when protection is unavailable.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* ci: require complete pull request descriptions\n\nRequire nonempty goal, scope, implementation steps, risks, and validation criteria in every pull request. Add a dedicated policy check, tests, contributor guidance, and branch-protection contexts.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: grandfather pre-policy Wave 1 PR\n\nRecord an explicit reviewed exemption for PR #3 so the automated TDD gate matches the documented Wave 2 adoption boundary while retaining description and validation checks.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"d85ff74c52e1479d2424c7a8ce4ab9bf5bd3167e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/diberry/aca-3/git/trees/d85ff74c52e1479d2424c7a8ce4ab9bf5bd3167e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/diberry/aca-3/git/commits/048888d17364942ce3b359d74b840b138e9b9714","verification":{"payload":"tree d85ff74c52e1479d2424c7a8ce4ab9bf5bd3167e\nparent 1af339738ed7ae739ab7ee2ae950f8859a7dcffe\nauthor Dina Berry (MSFT) <diberry@microsoft.com> 1791066302 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791066302 -0700\n\n(ignore) Establish ACA test-driven delivery policy (#4)\n\n* docs: require tests-first wave delivery\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs: adopt red-green-refactor workflow\n\nReplace the mandatory two-PR test gate with a single-PR TDD workflow that records an expected failing test before implementation while keeping main and merge-ready pull requests green.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* ci: enforce test-driven pull requests\n\nAdd a required TDD evidence check, a dedicated test status, cross-platform idempotent GitHub configuration scripts, and documentation for the current private-repository plan limitation.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat: adapt GitHub configuration to capabilities\n\nDetect repository ownership, visibility, reported plan, rulesets, and classic branch protection before applying the maximum supported configuration. Preserve explicit partial-enforcement failure when protection is unavailable.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* ci: require complete pull request descriptions\n\nRequire nonempty goal, scope, implementation steps, risks, and validation criteria in every pull request. Add a dedicated policy check, tests, contributor guidance, and branch-protection contexts.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: grandfather pre-policy Wave 1 PR\n\nRecord an explicit reviewed exemption for PR #3 so the automated TDD gate matches the documented Wave 2 adoption boundary while retaining description and validation checks.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwYC+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5qsQAACi+sVTrLDmpY4Rb+aslW5A\nmmztY7XLOUoD0x58tmKVbB4hsZ4bNfehnHAXwC0VR81MD3nScrUNJDfPMaELxNgB\n/B07kLYSaGGvun+PIrNLs71DNI7w5hgKeMw8dBqfmyYrWRFG9en8AYydGKIyIZMP\nLPmn+mn+40UujSQquLQxymZK2RxaiuJQ/lkK+nIllDbBmx15aF/oOGZCHSFgSF8q\nVWPVAoT7JVYNDij3/VvevkI1oi5v5ZG18RXwVpEqXDJwCnmfa/f61Fx74nSikYUd\nXSxgSZYTYWS+NThthuI6WQKswU/jqSRORsaMrYdaKiz/4R9x3rW/EuaMJy4CB7JM\nWX8Eq/olXtA4s1hjxK1Gfj5oz+lEK5AguDWsH37TDPEPYMkIB+otzk1l45VlTKJR\nNwI6p7/hB2n0EZf2XyX0krO2ofCuNXRV0