{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-planning/commits/0c89f80efb77e51763e1d7113814992d9f5ade09/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T17:02:36Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T17:02:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(plans): require canonical site_id on capacity plans (#32)\n\nAdd a required canonical site_id (a facility-layout Site site_code) to\nCapacityPlan: Create rejects a blank id, Rehydrate tolerates empty for\nlegacy rows, and migration 0008 backfills capacity_plans.site_id as\nTEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '''' with a clean down.\n\n- domain: site_id on CapacityPlan + CreateCapacityPlanCommand; planPublishedData\n  gains site_id (omitempty) on the same v1 CloudEvents type/dataschema\n- adapters: Postgres + memory repos persist/return site_id; REST and MCP\n  require it (422 on missing, additive in responses); encoder emits it\n- API specs: openapi.yaml + asyncapi.yaml additive, spectral clean; REST\n  docs regenerated via gen-api-docs (drift-free)\n- tests: BDD features reworded across 4 files; encoder goldens updated +\n  2 new legacy-decode tests; 7 integration fixtures/tests updated for the\n  required site_id (incl. migration-version sensor now tracking 0008 and\n  an assertion that down drops the column)\n- docs: ADR 0012, sidebars.ts, DDD docs, .claude rules\n- web: required Site id field on CapacityPlansScreen","tree":{"sha":"6f6b299b14a0727f03e4927d4c8a29701ba9ca30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-planning/git/trees/6f6b299b14a0727f03e4927d4c8a29701ba9ca30"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-planning/git/commits/0c89f80efb77e51763e1d7113814992d9f5ade09","verification":{"payload":"tree 6f6b299b14