pi.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-planning/commits/55a94a165427eb37fe9e13cbe1c50eddbd0a0f6f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T15:21:26Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T15:21:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: resolve findings from the 2026-10-05 docs audit (#31)\n\n* docs(domain): ProcessPath is locally owned, not a Conformist copy\n\nThe processpath package doc, the ProcessPath type doc and\nprocesscapacity.ProcessType doc still described ProcessPath as a\nConformist read-only copy of process-path-management, contradicting the\nADR 0001 Addendum. Comments only. Drops the matching \"Stale wording\"\nnote from docs/ddd/ubiquitous-language.md.\n\n* docs(kafka): storage consumer does not call RegisterProcessCapacityConstraint\n\nPackage doc claimed both consumers call the use case; since ADR 0002\nStorageCapacityConsumer only maintains the storage tally. Comment only.\n\n* docs(ci): fix gen-api-docs target in docs-api-drift comment\n\nComment named `inventory`; the docusaurus plugin id is warehouse-planning.\n\n* docs(harness): align HARNESS.md and README with harness-template v3\n\nCLAUDE.md and the repo''s scripts/harness, Makefile and fitness tests are\nv3; HARNESS.md and README still said v2.","tree":{"sha":"12560f19e46b63fca467daea8584ab9b9c602889","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-planning/git/trees/12560f19e46b63fca467daea8584ab9b9c602889"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-planning/git/commits/55a94a165427eb37fe9e13cbe1c50eddbd0a0f6f","verification":{"payload":"tree 12560f19e46b63fca467daea8584ab9b9c602889\nparent c821981d1a6717578e414e0cfd098ecba0f4dfca\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791300086 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791300086 -0300\n\nfix: resolve findings from the 2026-10-05 docs audit (#31)\n\n* docs(domain): ProcessPath is locally owned, not a Conformist copy\n\nThe processpath package doc, the ProcessPath type doc and\nprocesscapacity.ProcessType doc still described ProcessPath as a\nConformist read-only copy of process-path-management, contradicting the\nADR 0001 Addendum. Comments only. Drops the matching \"Stale wording\"\nnote from docs/ddd/ubiquitous-language.md.\n\n* docs(kafka): storage consumer does not call RegisterProcessCapacityConstraint\n\nPackage doc claimed both consumers call the use case; since ADR 0002\nStorageCapacityConsumer only maintains the storage tally. Comment only.\n\n* docs(ci): fix gen-api-docs target in docs-api-drift comment\n\nComment named `inventory`; the docusaurus plugin id is warehouse-planning.\n\n* docs(harness): align HARNESS.md and README with harness-template v3\n\nCLAUDE.md and the repo''s scripts/harness, Makefile and fitness tests are\nv3; HARNESS.md and README still said v2.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxRH2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAb7QQAALutLv6i9Kd0hju++0P+OqV\nwUYPNXwwhWRjtWLtT6hVVp40aeQ+nPy8rZDkXMvVYDdnXRs7QVpFAZphZn+9t87y\nrg7g8tEcKOS5tZFhXF/BVLq4NoQ+zgvQEd3n7NQv3itGc4qPcZqtCquXEWfeHH2p\nAum12p42JGDVQ+69Mb