d/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-planning/commits/647a0aeea5aba0609c5332a2fe84bc14544aa206/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:11:42Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:11:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: refresh product docs and add ddd-crew DDD artifact pack (#29)\n\n* docs: refresh product docs against origin/develop code\n\nPart A of the docs refresh. Every change is grounded in the code on\norigin/develop:\n\n- MCP surface is 11 tools (get_expected_demand, maxTools = 11), not 10\n  (README, overview/context, overview/runtime, api-reference/overview).\n- The three domain Kafka consumers dead-letter to <topic>.dlq after 5\n  attempts (deadletter.go, ADR 0007 section 3); \"There is no DLQ yet\" removed.\n- order-management demand ingestion (ADR 0004) is implemented: context map,\n  relationship table, upstream contracts and use cases updated; the demand\n  note no longer claims assigned_demand is optional on the path-capacity\n  endpoint.\n- order-management now consumes the capacity-plan events and\n  warehouse-ops-agent calls four read-only MCP tools: context map updated.\n- Reports binary serves four endpoints (freshness included).\n- events.md no longer says the analytics stream does not exist.\n- Layers table lists the demand package, analyticsstore, telemetry, the\n  CloudEvents helper and all four composition roots.\n- Aggregates page: DemandSource, analytics-only binding_constraint, the\n  expected-demand read model.\n- Tie-break order in step composition matches ComposeStepCapacity.\n- API overview lists the demand and reports tags, list endpoints and\n  /healthz, /readyz.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(ddd): add the ddd-crew DDD artifact pack\n\nPart B: eleven new pages under docs/docs/ddd/ plus a refreshed ubiquitous\nlanguage, wired into docs/sidebars.ts under \"DDD artifacts (ddd-crew)\".\n\n- ddd-artifacts: index and sources-of-truth note\n- core-domain-chart: Core (quadrant-1), evidence and evolution\n- bounded-context-canvas: v5, every message mapped to a route, tool or topic\n- context-map: U/D, patterns and technology per edge, live vs opt-in vs\n  deliberately absent, with sibling-side evidence\n- aggregate-design-canvas: ProcessCapacity and CapacityPlan, read models apart\n- domain-message-flow: three scenarios (shortage, demand defaulting, ops agent)\n- eventstorming: three design-level flows, legend, sticky inventory, hotspots\n- class-diagram: domain packages, ports and adapters, hexagonal view\n- entity-relationship: OLTP and analytical schemas, the single real FK,\n  table-is-not-aggregate mapping\n- sequence-diagrams: nine use-case flows incl. consumers, relay, projector\n- domain-events: every published and consumed event with full type, topic,\n  partition key, payload, producer and consumers\n- ubiquitous-language: refreshed, each term mapped to its code identifier\n\nMermaid validator: 27/27 diagrams render, 0 failed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(claude): order demand consumer, MCP tool budget 11, ADR range, DDD pack pointer\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"478419f19b3eeb7542c7dc750c8233a787473111","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-planning/git/trees/478419f19b3eeb7542c7dc750c8233a787473111"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-planning/git/commits/647a0aeea5aba0609c5332a2fe84bc14544aa206","verification":{"payload":"tree 478419f19b3eeb7542c7dc750c8233a787473111\nparent 168d44b2f7574d4d2847ff5d8fd2f32799aad002\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791270702 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791270702 -0300\n\ndocs: refresh product docs and add ddd-crew DDD artifact pack (#29)\n\n* docs: refresh product docs against origin/develop code\n\nPart A of the docs refresh. Every change is grounded in the code on\norigin/develop:\n\n- MCP surface is 11 tools (get_expected_demand, maxTools = 11), not 10\n  (README, overview/context, overview/runtime, api-reference/overview).\n- The three domain Kafka consumers dead-letter to <topic>.dlq after 5\n  attempts (deadletter.go, ADR 0007 section 3); \"There is no DLQ yet\" removed.\n- order-management demand ingestion (ADR 0004) is implemented: context map,\n  relationship table, upstream contracts and use cases updated; the demand\n  note no longer claims assigned_demand is optional on the path-capacity\n  endpoint.\n- order-management now consumes the capacity-plan events and\n  warehouse-ops-agent calls four read-only MCP tools: context map updated.\n- Reports binary serves four endpoints (freshness included).\n- events.md no longer says the analytics stream does not exist.\n- Layers table lists the demand package, analyticsstore, telemetry, the\n  CloudEvents helper and all four composition roots.\n- Aggregates page: DemandSource, analytics-only binding_constraint, the\n  expected-demand read model.\n- Tie-break order in step composition matches ComposeStepCapacity.\n- API overview lists the demand and reports tags, list endpoints and\n  /healthz, /readyz.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(ddd): add the ddd-crew DDD artifact pack\n\nPart B: eleven new pages under docs/docs/ddd/ plus a refreshed ubiquitous\nlanguage, wired into docs/sidebars.ts under \"DDD artifacts (ddd-crew)\".\n\n- ddd-artifacts: index and sources-of-truth note\n- core-domain-chart: Core (quadrant-1), evidence and evolution\n- bounded-context-canvas: v5, every message mapped to a route, tool or topic\n- context-map: U/D, patterns and technology per edge, live vs opt-in vs\n  deliberately absent, with sibling-side evidence\n- aggregate-design-canvas: ProcessCapacity and CapacityPlan, read models apart\n- domain-message-flow: three scenarios (shortage, demand defaulting, ops agent)\n- eventstorming: three design-level flows, legend, sticky inventory, hotspots\n- class-diagram: domain packages, ports and adapters, hexagonal view\n- entity-relationship: OLTP and analytical schemas, the single real FK,\n  table-is-not-aggregate mapping\n- sequence-diagrams: nine use-case flows incl. consumers, relay, projector\n- domain-events: every published and consumed event with full type, topic,\n  partition key, payload, producer and consumers\n- ubiquitous-language: refreshed, each term mapped to its code identifier\n\nMermaid validator: 27/27 diagrams render, 0 failed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(claude): order demand consumer, MCP tool budget 11, ADR range, DDD pack pointer\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxJ8uCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALSUQAAWuDvOp9wxRO8y6EZJMV1hT\n5YoFEsuEMpv74duitMZXodk3fYu8NnuQkjCm2iCe3kddZPMh8N3HyZycAWD1Dfyj\nNKl4dkth+bhEsRk+Btn9IH2tjBv9z6lQEcX32Qg86r+11ZqocRFl7oZBCy4P9/5D\nIletmBvwHDnBykZn4WlEU+C9AIhJ5B0llrsic0OHepVk0cuNV1Jp46RJK7SvUzdT\nHG2oGUTU2vcBryig3VitpMKia+nQFkQ0K216fdEWfg7Eno+NSIfZSCXN8+9wGnYU\nW7pd7Lw+UPZZKpvDU9y2F9i7rlWIAlYXD5oKhrXe5nfvoC+j+NBb4FDe98zQt3jN\nTkmz7Bla1Z4QpcFrDZ7s+s0TpqnrhloHxwkzXRLxTS6GVJe1/dOfAh0352zDjnpG\nd3LhMeN6bZp1HHSQv+apYwjjY/vbBCvFqbsahjyrplQim6J2Du5YZfa5ufjNgTGe\njhhek7HwF0J2YeULlu+KenFUnlYPEyu6vkEJ60BX+ayWvOMB8+wAUS6/okhQYSst\nTwR8TBR/rsJ6tSvgcxUPH2/tVzczMhjp6dEw4V/akzd5OVw5fVr2ZDzfDjQUx0ON\nYLyzJcvPS8CeRodNGo1MILFmL2kxZQezpFv+VI3TFiLpXGrsz0ezoZe3T9Uevrir\nsmwO+n1XgMCIQyeg1ixF\n=AbF2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T07:11:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/pr