//api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-planning/commits/6093d7131f2b9738602bd934bb5a33844cfe5578/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T00:57:21Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T00:57:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Phase 4 -- CapacityPlan, shortage detection, transactional outbox (#6)\n\n* feat(domain): CapacityPlan aggregate with shortage and bottleneck events\n\nCreate computes pathCapacity (ORDER/h), capacityOverWindow and\nshortage = max(0, demand - capacity) from an already-computed\nProcessPathCapacity (no I/O). Publish moves DRAFT->PUBLISHED, rejects a\nsecond publish, and records CapacityPlanPublished plus\nCapacityShortageDetected/BottleneckDetected only when shortage > 0.\n\nSection-43 worked example (12000 over 8h, 1000/h, REBIN -> shortage\n4000), within-capacity (6000) and the exact 8000 boundary are pinned as\nregression fixtures. gremlins: 14 killed, 0 lived.\n\n* feat(app): CreateCapacityPlan and PublishCapacityPlan over one UnitOfWork\n\nAdds ports.CapacityPlanRepository, ports.OutboxRepository and\nports.EventEncoder (+ application/outbox.Message), memory\nimplementations, and the two use cases. Each saves the aggregate and\ninserts its already-encoded events into the outbox inside ONE\nUnitOfWork.Do, so they commit or roll back together.\n\nCreate reuses GetProcessPathCapacity (Phase 2); the step\nProcessCapacities must be registered for exactly the plan window.\nDemand arrives on the request (documented simplification).\n\n* feat(postgres): capacity_plans + outbox_events migration and repositories\n\nMigration 0003 adds capacity_plans and outbox_events (mirrors\nworkforce-management: event_id, topic, full event_type, subject, key,\ndataschema, value, headers, created/published timestamps). The plan\nrepo joins the ctx transaction and locks the row on FindByID inside a\nUnitOfWork so concurrent publishes serialize. OutboxRepo.Drain claims\nrows FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED and sends one at a time in id order.\n\n* feat(events): CloudEvents encoder and Kafka relay sink for CapacityPlan events\n\nEncoder turns the four published domain events into outbox messages\nthrough the cloudevents helper (type com.warehouse.wes.warehouse-planning.\ncapacityplan.<Event>, id minted once, key = plan id, content-type\nheader). Golden exact-JSON tests pin every attribute per type.\nRelaySink uses RequireAll, 10ms BatchTimeout, Hash balancer and\nAllowAutoTopicCreation, and never dials at construction.\n\n* feat(outbox): relay draining outbox_events to Kafka or a log sink\n\nRelay drains every interval (default 1s), a full batch is followed\nimmediately by another pass, a failed pass is logged and retried. LogSink\nis the broker-free default for EVENT_PUBLISHER=log.\n\n* chore: make google/uuid and the testcontainers kafka module direct dependencies\n\n* feat(rest): POST /capacity-plans, POST /capacity-plans/{id}/publish, GET /capacity-plans/{id}\n\nRFC 7807 errors: 404 unknown path/plan, 422 missing step capacity, bad or\nmissing conversion factor, negative or absent demand, 409 already\npublished, 400 malformed or inverted window. The WorkloadProfile factors\nand the demand travel in the body.\n\n* feat(api): wire the outbox relay and a Postgres boot retry into cmd/api\n\nEVENT_PUBLISHER=kafka|log (default log), OUTBOX_RELAY_INTERVAL (default\n1s), KAFKA_BROKERS. The relay starts next to the consumers and dials\nKafka lazily on its first send, so a broker outage at boot cannot crash\nthe process. cmd/api had no boot retry, so migrations and the first\nPostgres ping now go through internal/bootretry (5 attempts, 1s doubling,\nlast error returned, abort on ctx cancel) with its four fleet tests.\n\n* test(bdd): CapacityPlan scenarios through the real HTTP surface\n\nSection-43 worked example (12000 over 8h -> shortage 4000, bound by\nREBIN, publish 200, second publish 409) and the within-capacity case\n(6000 -> shortage 0, only Created+Published queued), plus unknown path,\nnegative demand and unknown plan. Steps assert the GET read side and the\nqueued outbox event types.\n\n* test(integration): real Postgres + Kafka proof of the transactional outbox\n\ntestcontainers Postgres and Kafka (unique topic, never skip-gated):\n- plan + outbox rows commit or roll back together, both directions, for\n  create and publish\n- overlapping publishes publish once (FOR UPDATE; fails without it)\n- relay drains a shortage plan to Kafka; the four CloudEvents arrive with\n  correct type, subject, key, dataschema, content-type header\n- a simulated lost ack republishes the SAME persisted id, byte-identical\n- the topic is auto-created on first send\n- SKIP LOCKED: overlapping relays never claim the same row\n\nEncoder gains an optional Topic override for the unique test topics.\n\n* docs: OpenAPI, AsyncAPI and rules for Phase 4\n\n- openapi.yaml: /capacity-plans, /capacity-plans/{id}, .../publish\n- asyncapi.yaml: real channels and messages for the four published\n  capacityplan events and the three consumed events (valid for spectral)\n- integration-events.md: published types corrected to the aggregate\n  segment capacityplan (no separator), ProcessCapacityRegistered/Changed\n  removed from the published table and marked not implemented, outbox\n  section added\n- domain-model.md, rest-api.md: CapacityPlan is real\n\n* test: split long golden/handler tests for lint; gremlins re-measure comment\n\n* fix: truncate the default plan clock to microseconds (Postgres timestamptz precision)","tree":{"sha":"c9e736727fddfbaa862c6e7af0e0435b2308d6d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-planning/git/trees/c9e736727fddfbaa862c6e7af0e0435b2308d6d6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-planning/git/commits/6093d7131f2b9738602bd934bb5a33844cfe5578","verification":{"payload":"tree c9e736727fddfbaa862c6e7af0e0435b2308d6d6\nparent 1988ad8496847531e819dfc8db9d2ce2de2dd61f\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791075441 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791075441 -0300\n\nfeat: Phase 4 -- CapacityPlan, shortage detection, transactional outbox (#6)\n\n* feat(domain): CapacityPlan aggregate with shortage and bottleneck events\n\nCreate computes pathCapacity (ORDER/h), capacityOverWindow and\nshortage = max(0, demand - capacity) from an already-computed\nProcessPathCapacity (no I/O). Publish moves DRAFT->PUBLISHED, rejects a\nsecond publish, and records CapacityPlanPublished plus\nCapacityShortageDetected/BottleneckDetected only when shortage > 0.\n\nSection-43 worked example (12000 over 8h, 1000/h, REBIN -> shortage\n4000), within-capacity (6000) and the exact 8000 boundary are pinned as\nregression fixtures. gremlins: 14 killed, 0 lived.\n\n* feat(app): CreateCapacityPlan and PublishCapacityPlan over one UnitOfWork\n\nAdds ports.CapacityPlanRepository, ports.OutboxRepository and\nports.EventEncoder (+ application/outbox.Message), memory\nimplementations, and the two use cases. Each saves the aggregate and\ninserts its already-encoded events into the outbox inside ONE\nUnitOfWork.Do, so they commit or roll back together.\n\nCreate reuses GetProcessPathCapacity (Phase 2); the step\nProcessCapacities must be registered for exactly the plan window.\nDemand arrives on the request (documented simplification).\n\n* feat(postgres): capacity_plans + outbox_events migration and repositories\n\nMigration 0003 adds capacity_plans and outbox_events (mirrors\nworkforce-management: event_id, topic, full event_type, subject, key,\ndataschema, value, headers, created/published timestamps). The plan\nrepo joins the ctx transaction and locks the row on FindByID inside a\nUnitOfWork so concurrent publishes serialize. OutboxRepo.Drain claims\nrows FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED and sends one at a time in id order.\n\n* feat(events): CloudEvents encoder and Kafka relay sink for CapacityPlan events\n\nEncoder turns the four published domain events into outbox messages\nthrough the cloudevents helper (type com.warehouse.wes.warehouse-planning.\ncapacityplan.<Event>, id minted once, key = plan id, content-type\nheader). Golden exact-JSON tests pin every attribute per type.\nRelaySink uses RequireAll, 10ms BatchTimeout, Hash balancer and\nAllowAutoTopicCreation, and never dials at construction.\n\n* feat(outbox): relay draining outbox_events to Kafka or a log sink\n\nRelay drains every interval (default 1s), a full batch is followed\nimmediately by another pass, a failed pass is logged and retried. LogSink\nis the broker-free default for EVENT_PUBLISHER=log.\n\n* chore: make google/uuid and the testcontainers kafka module direct dependencies\n\n* feat(rest): POST /capacity-plans, POST /capacity-plans/{id}/publish, GET /capacity-plans/{id}\n\nRFC 7807 errors: 404 unknown path/plan, 422 missing step capacity, bad or\nmissing conversion factor, negative or absent demand, 409 already\npublished, 400 malformed or inverted window. The WorkloadProfile factors\nand the demand travel in the body.\n\n* feat(api): wire the outbox relay and a Postgres boot retry into cmd/api\n\nEVENT_PUBLISHER=kafka|log (default log), OUTBOX_RELAY_INTERVAL (default\n1s), KAFKA_BROKERS. The relay starts next to the consumers and dials\nKafka lazily on its first send, so a broker outage at boot cannot crash\nthe process. cmd/api had no boot retry, so migrations and the first\nPostgres ping now go through internal/bootretry (5 attempts, 1s doubling,\nlast error returned, abort on ctx cancel) with its four fleet tests.\n\n* test(bdd): CapacityPlan scenarios through the real HTTP surface\n\nSection-43 worked example (12000 over 8h -> shortage 4000, bound by\nREBIN, publish 200, second publish 409) and the within-capacity case\n(6000 -> shortage 0, only Created+Published queued), plus unknown path,\nnegative demand and unknown plan. Steps assert the GET read side and the\nqueued outbox event types.\n\n* test(integration): real Postgres + Kafka proof of the transactional outbox\n\ntestcontainers Postgres and Kafka (unique topic, never skip-gated):\n- plan + outbox rows commit or roll back together, both directions, for\n  create and publish\n- overlapping publishes publish once (FOR UPDATE; fails without it)\n- relay drains a shortage plan to Kafka; the four CloudEvents arrive with\n  correct type, subject, key, dataschema, content-type header\n- a simulated lost ack republishes the SAME persisted id, byte-identical\n- the topic is auto-created on first send\n- SKIP LOCKED: overlapping relays never claim the same row\n\nEncoder gains an optional Topic override for the unique test topics.\n\n* docs: OpenAPI, AsyncAPI and rules for Phase 4\n\n- openapi.yaml: /capacity-plans, /capacity-plans/{id}, .../publish\n- asyncapi.yaml: real channels and messages for the four published\n  capacityplan events and the three consumed events (valid for spectral)\n- integration-events.md: published types corrected to the aggregate\n  segment capacityplan (no separator), ProcessCapacityRegistered/Changed\n  removed from the published table and marked not implemented, outbox\n  section added\n- domain-model.md, rest-api.md: CapacityPlan is real\n\n* test: split long golden/handler tests for lint; gremlins re-measure comment\n\n* fix: truncate the default plan clock to microseconds (Postgres timestamptz precision)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwaRxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAizYQADWYt+9kFmPZZdavvDLiPQwF\nYY1WXSsjco9h8P31W4RhS9sxTTW4BDvJtbThm7X2g+07ziJF2yW0PnRR0XWPInsD\nogkKr3pPSd2cenIhZMfyQQparkDlDjTc65PxgRz8ki3+4/+C3qkAW4xI6xA9Fkdn\nHoeIk7NrITjFW6HSFE5YkCFY4MpxsYYBMn29swpzAjwnuJClW5m/j++agm3rvYnQ\nfRq9Grf6mt8ERN8WCsYHV+20W16tdxId9Xvkq/rzjVSAz/zQ5r3pUSzih6iR4Rsc\nF0M4Bjt+38nhnHmd8m8hrA7lR9lTz37kCoNJowytCtNGTGw2++ojLQsk9bhbuBDD\natLLPvvA8DKsKyPOzlKNH+kMDIZjxCqzjyO81APueJ1APBE9XPd0AtIo3ydYh+Ck\nyjwJo/1o5mAQ4RD+7uydvoOvcEYhnEaxzsnG94PRgtiRYPCjDVywJe5RTrWXCTS6\n6yy/2GIhFyIH+mKxAMEWo4yvZkC9Qs9B2sKVg9WGbA/YkqtAl+WaxmafJRKCViaY\nLQu8kkDYEQnVyBJm/xwB3/vdnxskdl3VH4ZKUhXJToJSAReBxLhHLiGrycdNZYP4\nm6gou3c94eMf1PWLn42DUSCl8M9Djvcs7at+u9KCDtHSQJBikhzBJGIovKGODAzs\n403rsiMnf7QjOMD3oLJi\n=y+it\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T00:57:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-planning/commit/6093d7131f2b9738602bd934bb5a33844cfe5578","node_id":"C_kwDOU6h1KNoAKDYwOTNkNzEzMWYyYjk3Mzg2MDJiZDkzNGJiNWEzMzg0NGNmZTU1Nzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-planning/commit/1988ad8496847531e819dfc8db9d2ce2de2dd61f","sha":"1988ad8496847531e819dfc8db9d2ce2de2dd61f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-planning/commits/1988ad8496847531e819dfc8db9d2ce2de2dd61f"}],"sha":"6093d7131f2b9738602bd934bb5a33844cfe5578","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-planning/commits/6093d7131f2b9738602bd934bb5a33844cfe5578"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-planning/commits/1988ad8496847531e819dfc8db9d2ce2de2dd61f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T22:56:23Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T22:56:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: atomic at-least-once Kafka consumers via UnitOfWork (#5)\n\n* feat(ports): add UnitOfWork with ctx-carried pgx tx; repos join it\n\nports.UnitOfWork.Do runs fn atomically. The Postgres implementation\nbegins one pgx tx, carries it in ctx (pgtx.With/From) and commits/rolls\nback; Do joins an existing tx. ProcessCapacityRepo, ProcessedEventRepo and\nStorageTallyRepo use the ctx tx when present (and never Begin/Commit their\nown then); without one they behave exactly as before. The memory double\nsnapshots/restores its participants so unit tests get real rollback, and\nnow stores/returns aggregate copies like a real store.\n\n* feat(usecases): IsDomainValidationError classifies Register errors\n\nAllow-list of the command-rejection sentinels RegisterProcessCapacityConstraint\ncan surface; anything else (repo/infra) is retryable by design.\n\n* fix(kafka): atomic at-least-once consumers (FetchMessage/CommitMessages + UoW)\n\n- Run loops use FetchMessage/CommitMessages and commit the offset only\n  after HandleMessage returned nil; a failure retries the SAME message with\n  capped exponential backoff (200ms..5s, ctx-cancellable), never skipping.\n- Per-message handling runs in ONE UnitOfWork.Do: processed-event claim +\n  tally + constraint upsert commit or roll back together.\n- HandleMessage returns non-nil only for infrastructure errors;\n  applyTallyUpdates and the labor consumer no longer swallow Register\n  errors -- only usecases.IsDomainValidationError ones are skipped.\n- cmd/api wires postgres.UnitOfWork (memory UoW with rollback in\n  DATABASE_URL-less mode).\n\n* test(kafka): prove atomicity, error classification and run-loop commit ordering\n\nTransactional in-memory doubles + failure-injecting repo wrapper show that a\nfailure after the tally step rolls back tally, constraint and claim and that\nthe retry heals; deterministic bad payloads return nil without touching the\nDB; the run loop commits exactly once, after success, with capped backoff.\n\n* test(postgres): UnitOfWork integration tests (commit, rollback, panic, join)\n\n* test(kafka): integration proofs of atomic at-least-once consumers\n\nReal Postgres + Kafka (testcontainers): failure after the tally step rolls\nback real rows incl. the processed_events claim and the retry heals;\nretry-in-process commits after success only; an always-failing consumer\nleaves the offset uncommitted and the next consumer in the group is\nredelivered the message. Existing integration tests pass UoW.\n\n* docs: describe the real idempotency mechanism (atomic claim, explicit commits)\n\nintegration-events.md said claim-before-work, which is the bug. Also fix the\nport and migration comments.","tree":{"sha":"68eaad5e1a038c6db3eaa3b3205fcd582e42ef4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-planning/git/trees/68eaad5e1a038c6db3eaa3b3205fcd582e42ef4d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-planning/git/commits/1988ad8496847531e819dfc8db9d2ce2de2dd61f","verification":{"payload":"tree 68eaad5e1a038c6db3eaa3b3205fcd582e42ef4d\nparent 3381839e9edb80457abf2bbb202adb23b89c9773\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791068183 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791068183 -0300\n\nfix: atomic at-least-once Kafka consumers via UnitOfWork (#5)\n\n* feat(ports): add UnitOfWork with ctx-carried pgx tx; repos join it\n\nports.UnitOfWork.Do runs fn atomically. The Postgres implementation\nbegins one pgx tx, carries it in ctx (pgtx.With/From) and commits/rolls\nback; Do joins an existing tx. ProcessCapacityRepo, ProcessedEventRepo and\nStorageTallyRepo use the ctx tx when present (and never Begin/Commit their\nown then); without one they behave exactly as before. The memory double\nsnapshots/restores its participants so unit tests get real rollback, and\nnow stores/returns aggregate copies like a real store.\n\n* feat(usecases): IsDomainValidationError classifies Register errors\n\nAllow-list of the command-rejection sentinels RegisterProcessCapacityConstraint\ncan surface; anything else (repo/infra) is retryable by design.\n\n* fix(kafka): atomic at-least-once consumers (FetchMessage/CommitMessages + UoW)\n\n- Run loops use FetchMessage/CommitMessages and commit the offset only\n  after HandleMessage returned nil; a failure retries the SAME message with\n  capped exponential backoff (200ms..5s, ctx-cancellable), never skipping.\n- Per-message handling runs in ONE UnitOfWork.Do: processed-event claim +\n  tally + constraint upsert commit or roll back together.\n- HandleMessage returns non-nil only for infrastructure errors;\n  applyTallyUpdates and the labor consumer no longer swallow Register\n  errors -- only usecases.IsDomainValidationError ones are skipped.\n- cmd/api wires postgres.UnitOfWork (memory UoW with rollback in\n  DATABASE_URL-less mode).\n\n* test(kafka): prove atomicity, error classification and run-loop commit ordering\n\nTransactional in-memory doubles + failure-injecting repo wrapper show that a\nfailure after the tally step rolls back tally, constraint and claim and that\nthe retry heals; deterministic bad payloads return nil without touching the\nDB; the run loop commits exactly once, after success, with capped backoff.\n\n* test(postgres): UnitOfWork integration tests (commit, rollback, panic, join)\n\n* test(kafka): integration proofs of atomic at-least-once consumers\n\nReal Postgres + Kafka (testcontainers): failure after the tally step rolls\nback real rows incl. the processed_events claim and the retry heals;\nretry-in-process commits after success only; an always-failing consumer\nleaves the offset uncommitted and the next consumer in the group is\nredelivered the message. Existing integration tests pass UoW.\n\n* docs: describe the real idempotency mechanism (atomic claim, explicit commits)\n\nintegration-events.md said claim-before-work, which is the bug. Also fix the\nport and migration comments.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwYgXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhCkQAGLMMrgmm+6HPNcFcJenKH8I\nol38ka07J8+EXMhr5yJXjx0IADaJAXJDI9pKj4cgb2zvhZaLj43VChIKPELReEfC\nZJivcdfMPH0yvMD213X+nmqnJFJ4TiYrFlw2bT0pTndFnEb2hQk2R3I1PdLMr/DN\nUWmKVPlMLokIeiPytliV/fxcJpnWfe6SWYQbfMegssh3zpOrS0SPbBJLv7xpbFeK\nkCSf8gks74jl6feO23dNXpXnppCK42hA6rpaOTSaJNxSo8g6RhsxOLbSCjPIq+Bj\nsnA1XZ1iqQ5dHUjrsqpWWrPNqBvs8kOFbBb3JDfArigKFwNTtgsRw+D4vRZ1dpFQ\n7op6wrE4YuEtLtepQQ5uT1WX2cfdekjwxX+YQp1OUq6QajSHBhmyEpls/Z+XONkz\n5dw6PDymrS3rYo1ToqbJ15FLpIR9G68p6pOp3zJAk9tmqKDwpyZmWM3jSerJnkWH\n0QiQfbP+ZxzXFZdWAHF7liBkb7H6Cdx68wo9bP0lF5NBJcEz6rfNRYCphyOEAE9j\n7UKnhWrD6QcZd3a3kSRNZSSxPh0qzIWGYJ8IU0Wc5khkH8Tz4f76vc6iFbytPHpM\n8Vzlrkh5sGANCShpLH+WwP9I99mOiUBXtk2lazsfQLx3iWheyzaeL0OihD+b0GpW\n9FSjwk2avYysE3rp2uVm\n=+ybg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T22:56:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-planning/commit/1988ad8496847531e819dfc8db9d2ce2de2dd61f","node_id":"C_kwDOU6h1KNoAKDE5ODhhZDg0OTY4NDc1MzFlODE5ZGZjOGRiOWQyY2UyZGUyZGQ2MWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-planning/commit/3381839e9edb80457abf2bbb202adb23b89c9773","sha":"3381839e9edb80457abf2bbb202adb23b89c9773","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-planning/commits/3381839e9edb80457abf2bbb202adb23b89c9773"}],"sha":"1988ad8496847531e819dfc8db9d2ce2de2dd61f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-planning/commits/1988ad8496847531e819dfc8db9d2ce2de2dd61f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-planning/commits/3381839e9edb80457abf2bbb202adb23b89c9773/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T22:34:11Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T22:34:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Phase 3 -- Kafka ingestion for labor and storage/station capacity (#4)\n\n* feat(kafka): Phase 3 labor + storage/station capacity consumers\n\n- internal/adapters/inbound/kafka/labor_capacity_consumer.go: consumes\n  workforce-management''s ShiftPlanCommitted (warehouse.workforce.events),\n  upserting a LABOR CapacityConstraint via the existing\n  RegisterProcessCapacityConstraint use case. ProcessType = uppercase\n  path_id, Location = building_id, window = [event time, event time +\n  planned_hours) (documented assumption per the ADR addendum), rate =\n  planned_heads * planned_rate in UNIT/HOUR (documented default unit).\n- internal/adapters/inbound/kafka/storage_capacity_consumer.go: consumes\n  facility-layout''s LocationSlotRegistered/LocationSlotDecommissioned\n  (warehouse.facility.events). role=Storage (or absent) tallies per\n  (zoneId, locationType) into a LOCATION constraint; role=WorkCenter\n  tallies per (zoneId, activity) into a STATION constraint per activity.\n  Decommission decrements the matching tally, floored at 0, logging a\n  warning (never crashing) for an untracked slot.\n- New local read models (consumer-owned, not shared aggregates):\n  processed_events (idempotency claim, ports.ProcessedEventRepository),\n  location_slot_registration + location_slot_tally\n  (ports.StorageTallyRepository) -- migration 0002. In-memory + Postgres\n  implementations of both new ports.\n- Both consumers decode via the existing cloudevents helper, dispatch on\n  the full , ignore unknown types, and skip (log, never crash)\n  malformed/legacy-flat messages. Consumer group ids are left to the\n  composition root to supply via env var (no literal in this package) --\n  TestKafkaConsumerGroupNeverHardcodedInline already passes.\n- Unit tests (in-memory repos, no real Kafka) cover: normal\n  ShiftPlanCommitted, normal Storage registration tally, a 2-activity\n  WorkCenter registration producing 2 STATION constraints, decommission\n  decrementing, an untracked-slot decommission no-op, malformed/garbage\n  messages, and -- the key idempotency proof -- replaying the same\n  CloudEvents id twice does not double count for either consumer.\n\nDesign decisions needing review (flagged per the task brief):\n- Storage (role=Storage) has no naturally implied ProcessType, unlike a\n  WorkCenter activity. This phase registers it under a sentinel\n  ProcessType=\"STORAGE\" with Location=\"<zoneId>:<locationType>\" (a\n  composite key, since ConstraintType=LOCATION is a single fixed\n  vocabulary entry that can''t itself be parameterized per locationType\n  on one aggregate). This is a pragmatic fit onto\n  ProcessCapacity''s (ProcessType, Location, Window) identity, not a\n  clean one -- see storage_capacity_consumer.go''s doc comments.\n- LOCATION/STATION tallies are a standing structural count, not a\n  time-windowed rate. Registered under a fixed, deterministic\n  [epoch, epoch+100y) CapacityWindow (StandingWindowStart/End) and\n  CapacityUnit=LINE (the nearest-fit of the domain''s four units) paired\n  with a 1-hour period purely to satisfy CapacityRate''s required\n  period.\n\nmake check-all passes locally (lint/build/vet/test, coverage 95.9%,\narch-test, bdd).\n\n* test(kafka): real testcontainers Kafka+Postgres integration tests\n\nmain_integration_test.go owns the package-wide Kafka broker lifecycle\n(confluentinc/confluent-local via testcontainers-go/modules/kafka, one\nbroker shared per test binary, unique topic per test) plus a\nstartPostgresPool helper reusing Phase 1''s migration runner -- mirrors\ninventory-storage''s facilitycache/consumer_integration_test.go recipe.\n\n- labor_capacity_consumer_integration_test.go: produces a real\n  ShiftPlanCommitted CloudEvents message onto a throwaway topic, runs\n  LaborCapacityConsumer against a real Kafka reader, asserts the LABOR\n  constraint landed in the real Postgres-backed ProcessCapacityRepository.\n- storage_capacity_consumer_integration_test.go: same recipe for\n  LocationSlotRegistered (asserts the STORAGE/<zone>:<locationType>\n  LOCATION constraint reaches count 1) then LocationSlotDecommissioned\n  (asserts it decrements back to 0).\n\nBoth satisfy TestKafkaIntegrationTestsUseTestcontainers (no skip-gated\nKAFKA_BROKERS, no hardcoded localhost:9092, both blank-import\ntestcontainers-go/modules/kafka). go test -tags=integration ./... -race\npasses locally against real Docker containers (Postgres AND Kafka).\n\n* feat(cmd): first composition root, wires REST + both Kafka consumers\n\ncmd/api/main.go -- Phase 1/2 had no cmd/ at all (wired directly from\ntests). This is the first real composition root:\n\n- DATABASE_URL set: runs migrations, opens a pgxpool, uses the\n  Postgres-backed ProcessCapacityRepository/ProcessedEventRepository/\n  StorageTallyRepository. Unset: falls back to in-memory adapters\n  (local dev, matching the fleet''s established convention, e.g.\n  inventory-storage''s cmd/inventory).\n- ports.ProcessPathRepository has no Postgres implementation yet (a\n  Phase 1/2 gap, not something this phase set out to close) -- always\n  in-memory, documented as a known limitation in buildAdapters'' doc\n  comment.\n- KAFKA_BROKERS set: starts LaborCapacityConsumer and\n  StorageCapacityConsumer as background goroutines, consumer group ids\n  from LABOR_CAPACITY_CONSUMER_GROUP/STORAGE_CAPACITY_CONSUMER_GROUP\n  (env-driven, defaulted but never hardcoded inline). Unset: Kafka\n  ingestion is disabled with a warning log, REST still serves standalone.\n  kafka-go''s Reader never dials synchronously at construction -- the\n  real TCP connection only happens inside ReadMessage, called from these\n  goroutines, so nothing here blocks process startup on Kafka.\n- HTTP_ADDR (default :8080), graceful shutdown on SIGINT/SIGTERM:\n  readiness... HTTP server Shutdown, then both consumer contexts\n  cancelled and their Run loops waited on (bounded), matching the\n  fleet''s established shutdown ordering.\n\nSmoke-tested standalone (no DATABASE_URL/KAFKA_BROKERS): builds, listens,\nGET /healthz -> 200. internal/architecture''s hexagonal + MCP fitness\ntests, full make check-all, and go test -tags=integration ./... (real\nPostgres + Kafka via testcontainers) all still pass.\n\n* docs: document Phase 3''s actual keying/idempotency decisions\n\n.claude/rules/integration-events.md''s Consumed types section now states\nHOW each tally maps onto ProcessCapacity''s (ProcessType, Location,\nCapacityWindow) identity (left open by the ADR Addendum), since the real\nimplementation had to make calls the Addendum didn''t spell out:\n\n- LABOR and STATION are clean fits (ProcessType from path_id/activity).\n- LOCATION (role=Storage) is NOT a clean fit -- documented as a\n  pragmatic sentinel ProcessType=STORAGE + composite\n  Location=<zoneId>:<locationType> workaround, flagged for a future ADR.\n- Both LOCATION/STATION use a fixed standing CapacityWindow + LINE unit,\n  not a time-sliced labor-style window.\n- New Idempotency subsection documents the processed_events claim-first\n  pattern and why it matters most for the storage/station INCREMENT\n  tally, not just the labor overwrite-style upsert.\n\n(CLAUDE.md''s matching \"Consumed types: FILL IN\" placeholder was left\nunedited -- this session''s tooling blocks writes to that file; flagged\nin the final delivery report.)","tree":{"sha":"d84b9fd994553ebcf27925ee4578053cac8be955","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-planning/git/trees/d84b9fd994553ebcf27925ee4578053cac8be955"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-planning/git/commits/3381839e9edb80457abf2bbb202adb23b89c9773","verification":{"payload":"tree d84b9fd994553ebcf27925ee4578053cac8be955\nparent bf33def0d9013205fbe6a7fa8cec77045514f320\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791066851 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791066851 -0300\n\nfeat: Phase 3 -- Kafka ingestion for labor and storage/station capacity (#4)\n\n* feat(kafka): Phase 3 labor + storage/station capacity consumers\n\n- internal/adapters/inbound/kafka/labor_capacity_consumer.go: consumes\n  workforce-management''s ShiftPlanCommitted (warehouse.workforce.events),\n  upserting a LABOR CapacityConstraint via the existing\n  RegisterProcessCapacityConstraint use case. ProcessType = uppercase\n  path_id, Location = building_id, window = [event time, event time +\n  planned_hours) (documented assumption per the ADR addendum), rate =\n  planned_heads * planned_rate in UNIT/HOUR (documented default unit).\n- internal/adapters/inbound/kafka/storage_capacity_consumer.go: consumes\n  facility-layout''s LocationSlotRegistered/LocationSlotDecommissioned\n  (warehouse.facility.events). role=Storage (or absent) tallies per\n  (zoneId, locationType) into a LOCATION constraint; role=WorkCenter\n  tallies per (zoneId, activity) into a STATION constraint per activity.\n  Decommission decrements the matching tally, floored at 0, logging a\n  warning (never crashing) for an untracked slot.\n- New local read models (consumer-owned, not shared aggregates):\n  processed_events (idempotency claim, ports.ProcessedEventRepository),\n  location_slot_registration + location_slot_tally\n  (ports.StorageTallyRepository) -- migration 0002. In-memory + Postgres\n  implementations of both new ports.\n- Both consumers decode via the existing cloudevents helper, dispatch on\n  the full , ignore unknown types, and skip (log, never crash)\n  malformed/legacy-flat messages. Consumer group ids are left to the\n  composition root to supply via env var (no literal in this package) --\n  TestKafkaConsumerGroupNeverHardcodedInline already passes.\n- Unit tests (in-memory repos, no real Kafka) cover: normal\n  ShiftPlanCommitted, normal Storage registration tally, a 2-activity\n  WorkCenter registration producing 2 STATION constraints, decommission\n  decrementing, an untracked-slot decommission no-op, malformed/garbage\n  messages, and -- the key idempotency proof -- replaying the same\n  CloudEvents id twice does not double count for either consumer.\n\nDesign decisions needing review (flagged per the task brief):\n- Storage (role=Storage) has no naturally implied ProcessType, unlike a\n  WorkCenter activity. This phase registers it under a sentinel\n  ProcessType=\"STORAGE\" with Location=\"<zoneId>:<locationType>\" (a\n  composite key, since ConstraintType=LOCATION is a single fixed\n  vocabulary entry that can''t itself be parameterized per locationType\n  on one aggregate). This is a pragmatic fit onto\n  ProcessCapacity''s (ProcessType, Location, Window) identity, not a\n  clean one -- see storage_capacity_consumer.go''s doc comments.\n- LOCATION/STATION tallies are a standing structural count, not a\n  time-windowed rate. Registered under a fixed, deterministic\n  [epoch, epoch+100y) CapacityWindow (StandingWindowStart/End) and\n  CapacityUnit=LINE (the nearest-fit of the domain''s four units) paired\n  with a 1-hour period purely to satisfy CapacityRate''s required\n  period.\n\nmake check-all passes locally (lint/build/vet/test, coverage 95.9%,\narch-test, bdd).\n\n* test(kafka): real testcontainers Kafka+Postgres integration tests\n\nmain_integration_test.go owns the package-wide Kafka broker lifecycle\n(confluentinc/confluent-local via testcontainers-go/modules/kafka, one\nbroker shared per test binary, unique topic per test) plus a\nstartPostgresPool helper reusing Phase 1''s migration runner -- mirrors\ninventory-storage''s facilitycache/consumer_integration_test.go recipe.\n\n- labor_capacity_consumer_integration_test.go: produces a real\n  ShiftPlanCommitted CloudEvents message onto a throwaway topic, runs\n  LaborCapacityConsumer against a real Kafka reader, asserts the LABOR\n  constraint landed in the real Postgres-backed ProcessCapacityRepository.\n- storage_capacity_consumer_integration_test.go: same recipe for\n  LocationSlotRegistered (asserts the STORAGE/<zone>:<locationType>\n  LOCATION constraint reaches count 1) then LocationSlotDecommissioned\n  (asserts it decrements back to 0).\n\nBoth satisfy TestKafkaIntegrationTestsUseTestcontainers (no skip-gated\nKAFKA_BROKERS, no hardcoded localhost:9092, both blank-import\ntestcontainers-go/modules/kafka). go test -tags=integration ./... -race\npasses locally against real Docker containers (Postgres AND Kafka).\n\n* feat(cmd): first composition root, wires REST + both Kafka consumers\n\ncmd/api/main.go -- Phase 1/2 had no cmd/ at all (wired directly from\ntests). This is the first real composition root:\n\n- DATABASE_URL set: runs migrations, opens a pgxpool, uses the\n  Postgres-backed ProcessCapacityRepository/ProcessedEventRepository/\n  StorageTallyRepository. Unset: falls back to in-memory adapters\n  (local dev, matching the fleet''s established convention, e.g.\n  inventory-storage''s cmd/inventory).\n- ports.ProcessPathRepository has no Postgres implementation yet (a\n  Phase 1/2 gap, not something this phase set out to close) -- always\n  in-memory, documented as a known limitation in buildAdapters'' doc\n  comment.\n- KAFKA_BROKERS set: starts LaborCapacityConsumer and\n  StorageCapacityConsumer as background goroutines, consumer group ids\n  from LABOR_CAPACITY_CONSUMER_GROUP/STORAGE_CAPACITY_CONSUMER_GROUP\n  (env-driven, defaulted but never hardcoded inline). Unset: Kafka\n  ingestion is disabled with a warning log, REST still serves standalone.\n  kafka-go''s Reader never dials synchronously at construction -- the\n  real TCP connection only happens inside ReadMessage, called from these\n  goroutines, so nothing here blocks process startup on Kafka.\n- HTTP_ADDR (default :8080), graceful shutdown on SIGINT/SIGTERM:\n  readiness... HTTP server Shutdown, then both consumer contexts\n  cancelled and their Run loops waited on (bounded), matching the\n  fleet''s established shutdown ordering.\n\nSmoke-tested standalone (no DATABASE_URL/KAFKA_BROKERS): builds, listens,\nGET /healthz -> 200. internal/architecture''s hexagonal + MCP fitness\ntests, full make check-all, and go test -tags=integration ./... (real\nPostgres + Kafka via testcontainers) all still pass.\n\n* docs: document Phase 3''s actual keying/idempotency decisions\n\n.claude/rules/integration-events.md''s Consumed types section now states\nHOW each tally maps onto ProcessCapacity''s (ProcessType, Location,\nCapacityWindow) identity (left open by the ADR Addendum), since the real\nimplementation had to make calls the Addendum didn''t spell out:\n\n- LABOR and STATION are clean fits (ProcessType from path_id/activity).\n- LOCATION (role=Storage) is NOT a clean fit -- documented as a\n  pragmatic sentinel ProcessType=STORAGE + composite\n  Location=<zoneId>:<locationType> workaround, flagged for a future ADR.\n- Both LOCATION/STATION use a fixed standing CapacityWindow + LINE unit,\n  not a time-sliced labor-style window.\n- New Idempotency subsection documents the processed_events claim-first\n  pattern and why it matters most for the storage/station INCREMENT\n  tally, not just the labor overwrite-style upsert.\n\n(CLAUDE.md''s matching \"Consumed types: FILL IN\" placeholder was left\nunedited -- this session''s tooling blocks writes to that file; flagged\nin the final delivery report.)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwYLjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgwMQAGD+OUBKzb57YmhgMVMwdTfn\nLPEatew1sApCPunQQhpq39PFIHJOZB1oUagB0LRpMwO18+Goxu9uLYhh/BM5kGzc\nS94N88oPBaNt3JSm3c65o6L8/rU+IZ/ERFL17TZ3crAQE2Rt6+4/1esO/NBcgbYD\nmxX9IS+5GzKR+hvBVZXzP9/dknMO49eNmBwT3sxA3aBDSTq1AvZLs2mmrtVSABk6\nIN5aLRYy52gPGs4ibXxDX5rfYavNiB3NMd07fMYmgFQfqpCkyCJ9UkJ2yNN7SXYe\nivwtxU0X73Tvuc2RYmlgZ1jkMkYr3/sYRYPG7eWUPyz0jfjx7nFGtGtd6MSR0VsB\nGTWTCwNMfJswRdnUWNCkJWFOf2W/ahSyK8ry2hTnuMLyjMSuQ3YtME9DplEW+h3H\nJafDzOgg1R5oMOTvURC+bXMxRfRQBzQAObhXf8ATJtLf3hriMkGNheqPJ/TjfIB6\n+GB1hxcP50QHNVcdBTY5MARMkox6wJROfWg8OBjMn+C52TEyOiXSB0Y2jLYRExCV\nbdOa8d6gLLJShOIhsL48dkTuB2lFEGvlLQ5Vp9qyTdkClEoKfBqErPKOw5uq9F19\nq5QZEZGvcyHLlPnJBGz9oTcAUllKNp8CdO1NncOW1YV3lw7QcLhp1cb6qzf+ixnX\nyxVNh/+WLyugpUKVGm/4\n=9MxJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T22:34:12Z"}},"committ