ogin":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-planning/commits/bf33def0d9013205fbe6a7fa8cec77045514f320/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T20:12:04Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T20:12:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: Task 0.4 spike -- confirm Phase 3 upstream event contracts (#3)\n\nworkforce-management publishes ShiftPlanCommitted (labor signal, usable).\nfacility-layout has no dedicated capacity event but LocationSlotRegistered/\nDecommissioned carry role+activities, tallyable for LOCATION/STATION\nconstraints.\n\nCorrection: process-path-management''s ProcessPath carries no ordered\nstep sequence (path_id/required_capabilities/eligibility only) -- this\ncontext''s own ProcessPath stays locally operator-declared, not a\nConformist copy. Phase 3 therefore drops the process-path-management\nconsumer entirely.\n\nUpdates ADR 0001 (addendum), domain-model.md, integration-events.md.","tree":{"sha":"d11774ad5cb73be5ac225ca4a43479031f1e8473","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-planning/git/trees/d11774ad5cb73be5ac225ca4a43479031f1e8473"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-planning/git/commits/bf33def0d9013205fbe6a7fa8cec77045514f320","verification":{"payload":"tree d11774ad5cb73be5ac225ca4a43479031f1e8473\nparent a2e23c51119b023b9d3a826e7b745e28aeafcf8f\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791058324 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791058324 -0300\n\ndocs: Task 0.4 spike -- confirm Phase 3 upstream event contracts (#3)\n\nworkforce-management publishes ShiftPlanCommitted (labor signal, usable).\nfacility-layout has no dedicated capacity event but LocationSlotRegistered/\nDecommissioned carry role+activities, tallyable for LOCATION/STATION\nconstraints.\n\nCorrection: process-path-management''s ProcessPath carries no ordered\nstep sequence (path_id/required_capabilities/eligibility only) -- this\ncontext''s own ProcessPath stays locally operator-declared, not a\nConformist copy. Phase 3 therefore drops the process-path-management\nconsumer entirely.\n\nUpdates ADR 0001 (addendum), domain-model.md, integration-events.md.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwWGUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVWgQACxKH1K4wBfUqQp8U8Sw8iqP\nPX0cAAdIpyQj2wqQW1L1AQLaCUQ9bgJHEnRbEVkrIAd8vgwQfmyT9B3myf8OdFWj\nbPI4H270yQY+k+VuBkxgIMjjoh3iLjFHJ/rLr23pGTt+9aKK/UYqaYt6lL8CD0pa\nVLHe5XQckP6T1RkVQ7kbuB/B+9+WWp3ObD8P06zXJAF500Ayk5IqP77N1G/kzBN5\n0mQTi5ornXid4HM4BEtAffzGdZqEGdnTlqP33qLTWnM/ApXyO7dtH6cqhkzgQTXE\nGgPJZV1GG+DoYJGkLyOkIYeydcg/L18Nt+5mhORB2Ilf87etLquR+kYWQSfomiQo\nJHLAkvTWf9C5alTCu7d9b1UnflnRiElEe+m+met5QadQ14Ucg45/pt5HzZBs+tHJ\nyfbXJBDopU6jPO3+XCjHkKkJgk0ApSicZxADpIrIQoJcdAelPi7gNiWDWFbBkutm\n+Gg2OAFlF4fofmfRTmV846rbyMWlQfD2p3CIKTPncL8ZY/IJGQmd/MbhC0AT3BoG\nLc/N7fvMpOhXo3U5tLdtwZbxzYoJUtkfDL42oyFhQVSUmHf3MNQ85vmDDb1JMH5Y\n0X3XDz0koFgPWZVSX5SgCI/w1o/90PbA65hEzbqIi/uXmTVf6SVkotE+9dY6hVvN\nUGU+FL1qxcHIeVidY8y3\n=gjk3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T20:12:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-planning/commit/bf33def0d9013205fbe6a7fa8cec77045514f320","node_id":"C_kwDOU6h1KNoAKGJmMzNkZWYwZDkwMTMyMDVmYmU2YTdmYThjZWM3NzA0NTUxNGYzMjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-planning/commit/a2e23c51119b023b9d3a826e7b745e28aeafcf8f","sha":"a2e23c51119b023b9d3a826e7b745e28aeafcf8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-planning/commits/a2e23c51119b023b9d3a826e7b745e28aeafcf8f"}],"sha":"bf33def0d9013205fbe6a7fa8cec77045514f320","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-planning/commits/bf33def0d9013205fbe6a7fa8cec77045514f320"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-planning/commits/a2e23c51119b023b9d3a826e7b745e28aeafcf8f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T19:57:09Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T19:57:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Phase 2 -- normalization and ProcessPathCapacity (#2)\n\n* feat(processcapacity): add WorkloadProfile normalization value object\n\nWorkloadProfile holds optional per-warehouse UNIT/PACKAGE-per-ORDER\nconversion factors and normalizes a CapacityRate into ORDER/period.\nConstructor rejects a zero or negative factor for any configured field.\n\n* feat(processpath): add read-only ProcessPath value object\n\nProcessPath is a local, read-only copy of a concept owned by\nprocess-path-management: id, name, ordered non-empty steps. No\nmutation/update method beyond construction -- this context is a\nConformist consumer, never the owner.\n\n* feat(processcapacity): add ComputeProcessPathCapacity domain service\n\nDomain service (not a stored aggregate): for each ProcessPath step,\nnormalizes its ProcessCapacity''s EffectiveRate() into ORDER/period via\na WorkloadProfile, returns the minimum rate and its bottleneck step.\nReproduces the Pick->Rebin->Pack worked example (1000 ORDER/HOUR,\nRebin bottleneck) as a regression fixture. A step missing from the\ncapacities map returns ErrMissingStepCapacity, never a false zero.\n\n* feat(application): add RegisterProcessPath and GetProcessPathCapacity\n\n- ports.ProcessPathRepository + memory.ProcessPathRepo (in-memory only\n  for now -- no event-driven sync from process-path-management yet).\n- RegisterProcessPath use case seeds a ProcessPath read model directly.\n- GetProcessPathCapacity loads the path, loads each step''s\n  ProcessCapacity via the existing ProcessCapacityRepository, builds a\n  WorkloadProfile from the request (Phase 2 simplification: no\n  dedicated WorkloadProfile persistence yet), and delegates to\n  processcapacity.ComputeProcessPathCapacity.\n\n* feat(http): add POST /process-paths and GET /process-paths/{id}/capacity\n\n- POST /process-paths seeds a ProcessPath read model (id/name/steps).\n- GET /process-paths/{id}/capacity?location=&window_start=&window_end=\n  &units_per_order=&packages_per_order= calls GetProcessPathCapacity\n  and returns the normalized rate + bottleneck step.\n- errors.go maps the new domain/application errors to RFC 7807\n  problem+json: 404 for an unknown path, 422 for an empty step list,\n  a non-positive/missing conversion factor, an unsupported\n  normalization unit, or a step with no registered ProcessCapacity.\n- httptest coverage: worked example, path not found, a step missing\n  capacity data, and an empty step list rejection.\n\n* test(bdd): add ProcessPathCapacity godog scenarios; docs + gremlins update\n\n- features/process_path_capacity.feature reproduces the Pick->Rebin->\n  Pack worked example end to end through the real HTTP surface (1000\n  ORDER/HOUR, Rebin bottleneck), plus a not-found path and a\n  missing-step-capacity scenario.\n- features_test.go wires RegisterProcessPath/GetProcessPathCapacity\n  into the same composition root and adds their step definitions.\n- .claude/rules/rest-api.md and apis/openapi.yaml document the new\n  POST /process-paths and GET /process-paths/{id}/capacity endpoints.\n- .gremlins.yaml''s threshold comment re-measured for Phase 2''s larger\n  mutant set (21 mutants, still 100% efficacy/coverage) -- the 99\n  threshold value is unchanged, just re-confirmed, not silently kept\n  stale.\n- workload_profile_test.go: added a non-identity PackagesPerOrder\n  fixture (3, not 1) after gremlins caught an ARITHMETIC_BASE mutant\n  surviving on the PACKAGE normalization division -- PackagesPerOrder=1\n  is an identity value for both / and *, so the worked-example fixture\n  alone couldn''t detect it.","tree":{"sha":"e36ade985348f52755665961885ba7b6182bbed5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-planning/git/trees/e36ade985348f52755665961885ba7b6182bbed5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-planning/git/commits/a2e23c51119b023b9d3a826e7b745e28aeafcf8f","verification":{"payload":"tree e36ade985348f52755665961885ba7b6182bbed5\nparent 9bbfe2a42279f8c5db4ca7bc89d89a5b18718e0a\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791057429 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791057429 -0300\n\nfeat: Phase 2 -- normalization and ProcessPathCapacity (#2)\n\n* feat(processcapacity): add WorkloadProfile normalization value object\n\nWorkloadProfile holds optional per-warehouse UNIT/PACKAGE-per-ORDER\nconversion factors and normalizes a CapacityRate into ORDER/period.\nConstructor rejects a zero or negative factor for any configured field.\n\n* feat(processpath): add read-only ProcessPath value object\n\nProcessPath is a local, read-only copy of a concept owned by\nprocess-path-management: id, name, ordered non-empty steps. No\nmutation/update method beyond construction -- this context is a\nConformist consumer, never the owner.\n\n* feat(processcapacity): add ComputeProcessPathCapacity domain service\n\nDomain service (not a stored aggregate): for each ProcessPath step,\nnormalizes its ProcessCapacity''s EffectiveRate() into ORDER/period via\na WorkloadProfile, returns the minimum rate and its bottleneck step.\nReproduces the Pick->Rebin->Pack worked example (1000 ORDER/HOUR,\nRebin bottleneck) as a regression fixture. A step missing from the\ncapacities map returns ErrMissingStepCapacity, never a false zero.\n\n* feat(application): add RegisterProcessPath and GetProcessPathCapacity\n\n- ports.ProcessPathRepository + memory.ProcessPathRepo (in-memory only\n  for now -- no event-driven sync from process-path-management yet).\n- RegisterProcessPath use case seeds a ProcessPath read model directly.\n- GetProcessPathCapacity loads the path, loads each step''s\n  ProcessCapacity via the existing ProcessCapacityRepository, builds a\n  WorkloadProfile from the request (Phase 2 simplification: no\n  dedicated WorkloadProfile persistence yet), and delegates to\n  processcapacity.ComputeProcessPathCapacity.\n\n* feat(http): add POST /process-paths and GET /process-paths/{id}/capacity\n\n- POST /process-paths seeds a ProcessPath read model (id/name/steps).\n- GET /process-paths/{id}/capacity?location=&window_start=&window_end=\n  &units_per_order=&packages_per_order= calls GetProcessPathCapacity\n  and returns the normalized rate + bottleneck step.\n- errors.go maps the new domain/application errors to RFC 7807\n  problem+json: 404 for an unknown path, 422 for an empty step list,\n  a non-positive/missing conversion factor, an unsupported\n  normalization unit, or a step with no registered ProcessCapacity.\n- httptest coverage: worked example, path not found, a step missing\n  capacity data, and an empty step list rejection.\n\n* test(bdd): add ProcessPathCapacity godog scenarios; docs + gremlins update\n\n- features/process_path_capacity.feature reproduces the Pick->Rebin->\n  Pack worked example end to end through the real HTTP surface (1000\n  ORDER/HOUR, Rebin bottleneck), plus a not-found path and a\n  missing-step-capacity scenario.\n- features_test.go wires RegisterProcessPath/GetProcessPathCapacity\n  into the same composition root and adds their step definitions.\n- .claude/rules/rest-api.md and apis/openapi.yaml document the new\n  POST /process-paths and GET /process-paths/{id}/capacity endpoints.\n- .gremlins.yaml''s threshold comment re-measured for Phase 2''s larger\n  mutant set (21 mutants, still 100% efficacy/coverage) -- the 99\n  threshold value is unchanged, just re-confirmed, not silently kept\n  stale.\n- workload_profile_test.go: added a non-identity PackagesPerOrder\n  fixture (3, not 1) after gremlins caught an ARITHMETIC_BASE mutant\n  surviving on the PACKAGE normalization division -- PackagesPerOrder=1\n  is an identity value for both / and *, so the worked-example fixture\n  alone couldn''t detect it.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwV4VCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiuwQAGgrmpbGvDgFAJSpqGtwednG\n+X+YnLU9HoIoY5TMZ1fAaqMseO8yv7Hf14MczKc7QU0hDJtc3YZK7Axi5xZlIbgS\nbtHzl1ju0UgkODwzxK4l8YcldH4bY+XkMivClpO62N5LC4aa5oShoXymsyzPHF12\n2oiqGdAGLWMrrx8pakCPPPjjsZPMoYd00AXBEv4dUgmxPunlb6N4yEe1oldjshGG\nYAURfxQd8m4bgY6X7QomUAwSRQE6DNLzVXZ+TTPAl9lZ0fqy3cWYAIbnliFkV7tv\nQACmKFve4ECD8ye4zLYUJoDQtDduLrPNL4iRmW1QTHAFxpDT2eq8Wem3Lafyxcm3\nxj9ebvKXdM+P8Rq9xh2j2PBP6wfsMubXD/65V9bXW8diur1ZfypIyI/CLRLundAN\n1CmVCKo0IKzgFHwuk92UWrt3ctIJwrtSshuSMYYuObZ37pz6VYpRwP82mBfVYN9L\nUnRY+9/QAfzmUuPa2woWfBAsENvOUGQERIvRGXWjSxx+AuOAiG2cCfqPJN4qLYUF\nXZ/olvgMLHukyBuP5py9y/R3Adigb4KaiEKzRVtRpFNIlsqdhBfHr7t3DrY6k8qC\ng+8/oxAvk4qnaNWQTJ0Upp1ullbWk3v2b5USDk24ibemLWBgxkj/fwk1Z26IoIEv\nOkmJsyHWi+RI/t4/y2C/\n=dAps\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T19:57:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-planning/commit/a2e23c51119b023b9d3a826e7b745e28aeafcf8f","node_id":"C_kwDOU6h1KNoAKGEyZTIzYzUxMTE5YjAyM2I5ZDNhODI2ZTdiNzQ1ZTI4YWVhZmNmOGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/warehouse-planning/commit/9bbfe2a42279f8c5db4ca7bc89d89a5b18718e0a","sha":"9bbfe2a42279f8c5db4ca7bc89d89a5b18718e0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-planning/commits/9bbfe2a42279f8c5db4ca7bc89d89a5b18718e0a"}],"sha":"a2e23c51119b023b9d3a826e7b745e28aeafcf8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-planning/commits/a2e23c51119b023b9d3a826e7b745e28aeafcf8f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-planning/commits/9bbfe2a42279f8c5db4ca7bc89d89a5b18718e0a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T19:38:00Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T19:38:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Phase 1 -- native and effective ProcessCapacity (#1)\n\n* feat(processcapacity): CapacityRate, CapacityWindow, ProcessCapacity domain model\n\n- CapacityRate value object: quantity/unit/period, rejects negative\n  quantity and non-positive period, LessThan compares per-second rate\n- CapacityWindow value object: rejects end<=start (including zero-length)\n- ProcessCapacity aggregate: AddConstraint upserts and enforces a single\n  native unit across all constraints; EffectiveRate returns the minimum\n  rate and its binding constraint type\n- Byte-for-byte regression fixture for the PICK/PICK-ZONE-A worked example\n  (LABOR=4000, LOCATION=3500, EQUIPMENT=5000, CONVEYOR=3800 UNIT/HOUR ->\n  3500 UNIT/HOUR, binding LOCATION)\n- 100% statement coverage\n\n* feat(processcapacity): application layer -- repo port, in-memory adapter, RegisterProcessCapacityConstraint use case\n\n- ports.ProcessCapacityRepository: Save + FindByProcessLocationWindow\n  (nil, nil when not found)\n- memory.ProcessCapacityRepo: mutex-guarded map-backed implementation,\n  for tests only -- never wired into production\n- usecases.RegisterProcessCapacityConstraint.Handle: loads-or-creates the\n  aggregate, applies AddConstraint, saves, returns the new effective rate\n  + binding constraint\n- Unit tests against the in-memory repo reproduce the PICK/PICK-ZONE-A\n  worked example end to end, plus invalid-window/mismatched-unit/\n  repository-error propagation cases\n\n* feat(processcapacity): Postgres persistence (pgx + golang-migrate + testcontainers)\n\n- migrations/0001_process_capacity.{up,down}.sql: process_capacity (native\n  unit) + process_capacity_constraint (one row per registered constraint,\n  FK cascade delete, ordinal column preserves registration order across\n  a save/load round trip)\n- postgres.NewPool / RunMigrations mirror inventory-storage''s pgxpool +\n  golang-migrate wiring pattern (simplified: no otelpgx tracing yet)\n- postgres.ProcessCapacityRepo implements ports.ProcessCapacityRepository:\n  Save upserts the parent row and replaces the full constraint set inside\n  one transaction; FindByProcessLocationWindow returns nil,nil when unseen\n- -tags=integration test boots a REAL Postgres via testcontainers-go\n  (never a skip-gated external DB) and proves a save+load round trip\n  reproduces the PICK/PICK-ZONE-A worked example''s 3500 UNIT/HOUR /\n  LOCATION-binding result, plus the not-found contract\n\n* feat(processcapacity): REST inbound adapter (chi) + OpenAPI/AsyncAPI specs\n\n- POST /process-capacities -> RegisterProcessCapacityConstraint (201 with\n  effective_rate/effective_unit/binding_constraint)\n- GET /process-capacities?process_type=&location=&window_start=&window_end=\n  -> 200 with effective_rate/effective_unit/binding_constraint/constraints,\n  404 if nothing registered for that identity\n- RFC 7807 application/problem+json error responses (mirrors\n  inventory-storage''s statusFor/problemFor convention); no auth middleware\n- apis/openapi.yaml documents both routes; apis/asyncapi.yaml added as a\n  valid-but-empty stub (Phase 1 has no Kafka producer/consumer yet) plus\n  .spectral.yaml/.spectral.asyncapi.yaml rulesets so the api-lint CI job\n  has something to lint\n- .claude/rules/rest-api.md''s Phase 1 route table already matched what\n  was built; left unchanged\n- httptest-based handler tests against the in-memory repo reproduce the\n  PICK/PICK-ZONE-A worked example end to end\n\n* feat(processcapacity): godog BDD suite over the real HTTP surface\n\n- features/process_capacity.feature: byte-for-byte reproduction of the\n  PICK/PICK-ZONE-A worked example (register 4 constraints, assert 3500\n  UNIT/HOUR bound by LOCATION), plus not-found and unit-mismatch scenarios\n- features_test.go (root, package main_test): TestFeatures + godog\n  ScenarioInitializer/world, mirroring inventory-storage''s root-level\n  BDD harness shape -- drives the real chi router via httptest with the\n  in-memory repository\n- Total coverage across internal/domain + internal/application: 96.8%\n  (gate is 90%)\n\n* chore(gremlins): set measured mutation-testing thresholds for processcapacity\n\nMeasured locally with gremlins v0.6.0 (matching CI''s pin):\n./internal/domain/processcapacity -- 9 mutants, all killed, 100.00%\nefficacy and 100.00% mutant coverage. Thresholds set to 99 (strictly\nbelow 100, per gremlins'' <= failure semantics) -- never copied from a\nsibling repo''s numbers, filled in in place of the {{MEASURED_*}}\nplaceholders. Also verified: make check-all passes, govulncheck finds\n0 exploitable vulnerabilities.","tree":{"sha":"10cd76c8f404e419a632d3d30f3b8b95a3f5508a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-planning/git/trees/10cd76c8f404e419a632d3d30f3b8b95a3f5508a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/warehouse-planning/git/commits/9bbfe2a42279f8c5db4ca7bc89d89a5b18718e0a","verification":{"payload":"tree 10cd76c8f404e419a632d3d30f3b8b95a3f5508a\nparent 40c65e3e6da5b988d4e9ebe93dd8edddecfa97c4\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791056280 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791056280 -0300\n\nfeat: Phase 1 -- native and effective ProcessCapacity (#1)\n\n* feat(processcapacity): CapacityRate, CapacityWindow, ProcessCapacity domain model\n\n- CapacityRate value object: quantity/unit/period, rejects negative\n  quantity and non-positive period, LessThan compares per-second rate\n- CapacityWindow value object: rejects end<=start (including zero-length)\n- ProcessCapacity aggregate: AddConstraint upserts and enforces a single\n  native unit across all constraints; EffectiveRate returns the minimum\n  rate and its binding constraint type\n- Byte-for-byte regression fixture for the PICK/PICK-ZONE-A worked example\n  (LABOR=4000, LOCATION=3500, EQUIPMENT=5000, CONVEYOR=3800 UNIT/HOUR ->\n  3500 UNIT/HOUR, binding LOCATION)\n- 100% statement coverage\n\n* feat(processcapacity): application layer -- repo port, in-memory adapter, RegisterProcessCapacityConstraint use case\n\n- ports.ProcessCapacityRepository: Save + FindByProcessLocationWindow\n  (nil, nil when not found)\n- memory.ProcessCapacityRepo: mutex-guarded map-backed implementation,\n  for tests only -- never wired into production\n- usecases.RegisterProcessCapacityConstraint.Handle: loads-or-creates the\n  aggregate, applies AddConstraint, saves, returns the new effective rate\n  + binding constraint\n- Unit tests against the in-memory repo reproduce the PICK/PICK-ZONE-A\n  worked example end to end, plus invalid-window/mismatched-unit/\n  repository-error propagation cases\n\n* feat(processcapacity): Postgres persistence (pgx + golang-migrate + testcontainers)\n\n- migrations/0001_process_capacity.{up,down}.sql: process_capacity (native\n  unit) + process_capacity_constraint (one row per registered constraint,\n  FK cascade delete, ordinal column preserves registration order across\n  a save/load round trip)\n- postgres.NewPool / RunMigrations mirror inventory-storage''s pgxpool +\n  golang-migrate wiring pattern (simplified: no otelpgx tracing yet)\n- postgres.ProcessCapacityRepo implements ports.ProcessCapacityRepository:\n  Save upserts the parent row and replaces the full constraint set inside\n  one transaction; FindByProcessLocationWindow returns nil,nil when unseen\n- -tags=integration test boots a REAL Postgres via testcontainers-go\n  (never a skip-gated external DB) and proves a save+load round trip\n  reproduces the PICK/PICK-ZONE-A worked example''s 3500 UNIT/HOUR /\n  LOCATION-binding result, plus the not-found contract\n\n* feat(processcapacity): REST inbound adapter (chi) + OpenAPI/AsyncAPI specs\n\n- POST /process-capacities -> RegisterProcessCapacityConstraint (201 with\n  effective_rate/effective_unit/binding_constraint)\n- GET /process-capacities?process_type=&location=&window_start=&window_end=\n  -> 200 with effective_rate/effective_unit/binding_constraint/constraints,\n  404 if nothing registered for that identity\n- RFC 7807 application/problem+json error responses (mirrors\n  inventory-storage''s statusFor/problemFor convention); no auth middleware\n- apis/openapi.yaml documents both routes; apis/asyncapi.yaml added as a\n  valid-but-empty stub (Phase 1 has no Kafka producer/consumer yet) plus\n  .spectral.yaml/.spectral.asyncapi.yaml rulesets so the api-lint CI job\n  has something to lint\n- .claude/rules/rest-api.md''s Phase 1 route table already matched what\n  was built; left unchanged\n- httptest-based handler tests against the in-memory repo reproduce the\n  PICK/PICK-ZONE-A worked example end to end\n\n* feat(processcapacity): godog BDD suite over the real HTTP surface\n\n- features/process_capacity.feature: byte-for-byte reproduction of the\n  PICK/PICK-ZONE-A worked example (register 4 constraints, assert 3500\n  UNIT/HOUR bound by LOCATION), plus not-found and unit-mismatch scenarios\n- features_test.go (root, package main_test): TestFeatures + godog\n  ScenarioInitializer/world, mirroring inventory-storage''s root-level\n  BDD harness shape -- drives the real chi router via httptest with the\n  in-memory repository\n- Total coverage across internal/domain + internal/application: 96.8%\n  (gate is 90%)\n\n* chore(gremlins): set measured mutation-testing thresholds for processcapacity\n\nMeasured locally with gremlins v0.6.0 (matching CI''s pin):\n./internal/domain/processcapacity -- 9 mutants, all killed, 100.00%\nefficacy and 100.00% mutant coverage. Thresholds set to 99 (strictly\nbelow 100, per gremlins'' <= failure semantics) -- never copied from a\nsibling repo''s numbers, filled in in place of the {{MEASURED_*}}\nplaceholders. Also verified: make check-all passes, govulncheck finds\n0 exploitable vulnerabilities.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwVmYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvOYQAFBB