thub.com/users/vonmiller1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vonmiller1/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vonmiller1","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vonmiller1/knowledge-center/commits/89ecbf8d25527c27a0f79a2f79e4b1000b07e0ea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T03:20:13Z","email":"Kingtut22009@gmail.com","name":"vonmiller1"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T03:20:13Z","email":"Kingtut22009@gmail.com","name":"vonmiller1"},"message":"Close the bare-invocation gap in the fork rename\n\nThe shell-invocation rule keys on a following subcommand or flag, so a Dockerfile\nexec form (ENTRYPOINT [\"cmd\"], CMD [\"cmd\", ...]) and the command alone on a usage\nline fell through to the bare package rule and were rewritten to the package name: a\nfork''s image would exec a command that no longer exists. Two exec-form anchors and a\nwhole-line anchor now catch those shapes, and the new test was observed red against\nthe unfixed rules before being trusted green.","tree":{"sha":"6bb99041fe1eb273793eb81db7b601fbae490ef4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vonmiller1/knowledge-center/git/trees/6bb99041fe1eb273793eb81db7b601fbae490ef4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vonmiller1/knowledge-center/git/commits/89ecbf8d25527c27a0f79a2f79e4b1000b07e0ea","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/318769617?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vonmiller1/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vonmiller1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vonmiller1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vonmiller1/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vonmiller1","id":318769617,"login":"vonmiller1","node_id":"U_kgDOEwAJ0Q","org